msgid "Writing your first contribution for Django"
msgstr "Scríobh do chéad ranníocaíocht do Django"

msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Réamhrá"

msgid ""
"Interested in giving back to the community a little? Maybe you've found a "
"bug in Django that you'd like to see fixed, or maybe there's a small feature "
"you want added (but remember that proposals for new features should follow "
"the :ref:`process for suggesting new features <requesting-features>`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Contributing back to Django itself is the best way to see your own concerns "
"addressed. This may seem daunting at first, but it's a well-traveled path "
"with documentation, tooling, and a community to support you. We'll walk you "
"through the entire process, so you can learn by example."
msgstr ""
"Is é an bealach is fearr chun do chuid imní féin a fheiceáil ag cur ar ais "
"chuig Django féin. D'fhéadfadh sé seo cosúil daunting ar dtús, ach tá sé ina "
"cosán dea-thaistil le doiciméadú, tooling, agus pobal chun tacú leat. "
"Siúlfaimid tú tríd an bpróiseas ar fad, ionas gur féidir leat foghlaim trí "
"shampla."

msgid "Who's this tutorial for?"
msgstr "Cé dó an rang teagaisc seo?"

msgid ""
"If you are looking for a reference on the details of making code "
"contributions, see the :doc:`/internals/contributing/writing-code/index` "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag lorg teistiméireachta ar na sonraí maidir le ranníocaíochtaí cód "
"a dhéanamh, féach an doiciméadú :doc:`/inmheánach/ranníocaíocht/cód-scríobh/"
"innéacs`."

msgid ""
"For this tutorial, we expect that you have at least a basic understanding of "
"how Django works. This means you should be comfortable going through the "
"existing tutorials on :doc:`writing your first Django app</intro/"
"tutorial01>`. In addition, you should have a good understanding of Python "
"itself. But if you don't, `Dive Into Python`_ is a fantastic (and free) "
"online book for beginning Python programmers."
msgstr ""
"Maidir leis an rang teagaisc seo, táimid ag súil go bhfuil tuiscint "
"bhunúsach ar a laghad agat ar an gcaoi a n-oibríonn Django. Ciallaíonn sé "
"seo gur chóir duit a bheith compordach ag dul tríd na ranganna teagaisc atá "
"ann cheana féin ar :d oc:`writing your first Django app</intro/tutorial01>`. "
"Ina theannta sin, ba chóir go mbeadh tuiscint mhaith agat ar Python féin. "
"Ach mura ndéanann tú, is leabhar iontach (agus saor in aisce) ar líne é "
"`Dive Into Python`_ chun ríomhchláraitheoirí Python a thosú."

msgid ""
"Those of you who are unfamiliar with version control systems and Trac will "
"find that this tutorial and its links include just enough information to get "
"started. However, you'll probably want to read some more about these "
"different tools if you plan on contributing to Django regularly."
msgstr ""
"Iad siúd agaibh nach bhfuil cur amach acu ar chórais rialaithe leaganacha "
"agus gheobhaidh Trac amach go bhfuil an rang teagaisc seo agus a naisc san "
"áireamh ach go leor eolais chun tús a chur leis. Mar sin féin, is dócha gur "
"mhaith leat níos mó a léamh faoi na huirlisí éagsúla seo má tá sé ar intinn "
"agat cur le Django go rialta."

msgid ""
"For the most part though, this tutorial tries to explain as much as "
"possible, so that it can be of use to the widest audience."
msgstr ""
"Den chuid is mó, áfach, déanann an rang teagaisc seo iarracht an oiread agus "
"is féidir a mhíniú, ionas gur féidir é a úsáid don lucht féachana is leithne."

msgid "Where to get help:"
msgstr "Cá háit le cabhair a fháil:"

msgid ""
"If you're having trouble going through this tutorial, please post a message "
"on the `Django Forum`_ or drop by the `Django Discord server`_ to chat with "
"other Django users who might be able to help."
msgstr ""

msgid "What does this tutorial cover?"
msgstr "Cad a chlúdaíonn an rang teagaisc seo?"

msgid ""
"We'll be walking you through contributing to Django for the first time. By "
"the end of this tutorial, you should have a basic understanding of both the "
"tools and the processes involved. Specifically, we'll be covering the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Beimid ag siúl leat trí chur le Django den chéad uair. Faoi dheireadh an "
"teagaisc seo, ba chóir go mbeadh tuiscint bhunúsach agat ar na huirlisí agus "
"ar na próisis atá i gceist. Go sonrach, beimid ag clúdach na nithe seo a "
"leanas:"

msgid "Installing Git."
msgstr "Suiteáil Git."

msgid "Downloading a copy of Django's development version."
msgstr "Cóip de leagan forbartha Django a íoslódáil."

msgid "Running Django's test suite."
msgstr "Ag rith sraith tástála Django."

msgid "Writing a test for your changes."
msgstr "Tástáil a scríobh le haghaidh do chuid athruithe."

msgid "Writing the code for your changes."
msgstr "Scríobh an cód do do chuid athruithe."

msgid "Testing your changes."
msgstr "Do chuid athruithe a thástáil."

msgid "Submitting a pull request."
msgstr "Iarratas ar tharraingt a chur isteach."

msgid "Where to look for more information."
msgstr "Cá háit le tuilleadh eolais a lorg."

msgid ""
"Once you're done with the tutorial, you can look through the rest "
"of :doc:`Django's documentation on contributing</internals/contributing/"
"index>`. It contains lots of great information and is a must read for anyone "
"who'd like to become a regular contributor to Django. If you've got "
"questions, it's probably got the answers."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú ag déanamh leis an rang teagaisc, is féidir leat breathnú "
"tríd an gcuid eile de :d oc:`Django's documentation on contributing</"
"internals/contributing/index>`. Tá go leor eolais iontach ann agus ní mór é "
"a léamh do dhuine ar bith ar mhaith leo a bheith ina ranníocóir rialta le "
"Django. Má tá ceisteanna agat, is dócha go bhfuair sé na freagraí."

msgid "Python 3 required!"
msgstr "Python 3 ag teastáil!"

msgid ""
"The current version of Django doesn't support Python 2.7. Get Python 3 at "
"`Python's download page <https://www.python.org/downloads/>`_ or with your "
"operating system's package manager."
msgstr ""
"Ní thacaíonn an leagan reatha de Django le Python 2.7. Faigh Python 3 ag "
"leathanach íoslódála `Python's <https://www.python.org/downloads/>`_ nó le "
"bainisteoir pacáiste do chórais oibriúcháin."

msgid "For Windows users"
msgstr "D'úsáideoirí Windows"

msgid ""
"See :ref:`install_python_windows` on Windows docs for additional guidance."
msgstr ""
"Féach :ref:`install_python_windows` ar docs Windows le haghaidh treoir "
"bhreise."

msgid "Code of Conduct"
msgstr "Cód Iompair"

msgid ""
"As a contributor, you can help us keep the Django community open and "
"inclusive. Please read and follow our `Code of Conduct <https://"
"www.djangoproject.com/conduct/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Mar ranníocóir, is féidir leat cabhrú linn pobal Django a choinneáil "
"oscailte agus cuimsitheach. Léigh agus lean ár `Cód Iompair <https://"
"www.djangoproject.com/conduct/>`_."

msgid "Installing Git"
msgstr "Git á shuiteáil"

msgid ""
"For this tutorial, you'll need Git installed to download the current "
"development version of Django and to generate a branch for the changes you "
"make."
msgstr ""
"Don rang teagaisc seo, beidh ort Git suiteáilte chun an leagan forbartha "
"reatha de Django a íoslódáil agus brainse a ghiniúint do na hathruithe a "
"dhéanann tú."

msgid ""
"To check whether or not you have Git installed, enter ``git`` into the "
"command line. If you get messages saying that this command could not be "
"found, you'll have to download and install it, see `Git's download page`__."
msgstr ""
"Chun seiceáil an bhfuil Git suiteáilte agat nó nach bhfuil, cuir ``git`` "
"isteach i líne na n-orduithe. Má fhaigheann tú teachtaireachtaí ag rá nach "
"bhféadfaí an t-ordú seo a aimsiú, beidh ort é a íoslódáil agus a shuiteáil, "
"féach `Leathanach íoslódála Git`__."

msgid ""
"If you're not that familiar with Git, you can always find out more about its "
"commands (once it's installed) by typing ``git help`` into the command line."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil tú chomh eolach sin ar Git, is féidir leat níos mó a fháil amach "
"i gcónaí faoina orduithe (nuair atá sé suiteáilte) trí ``cabhair git`` a "
"chlóscríobh isteach i líne na n-orduithe."

msgid "Getting a copy of Django's development version"
msgstr "Cóip de leagan forbartha Django a fháil"

msgid ""
"The first step to contributing to Django is to get a copy of the source "
"code. First, `fork Django on GitHub <https://github.com/django/django/"
"fork>`__. Then, from the command line, use the ``cd`` command to navigate to "
"the directory where you'll want your local copy of Django to live."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad chéim chun cur le Django ná cóip den bhunchód a fháil. Ar "
"dtús, `forc Django ar GitHub < https://github.com/django/django/fork>`__. "
"Ansin, ón líne ordaithe, bain úsáid as an ordú `` cd`` chun dul chuig an "
"eolaire ina mbeidh tú ag iarraidh go mbeadh do chóip áitiúil de Django beo."

msgid "Download the Django source code repository using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Íoslódáil stór cód foinse Django ag baint úsáide as an ordú seo a leanas:"

msgid "Low bandwidth connection?"
msgstr "Nasc bandaleithead íseal?"

msgid ""
"You can add the ``--depth 1`` argument to ``git clone`` to skip downloading "
"all of Django's commit history, which reduces data transfer from  ~250 MB to "
"~70 MB."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an argóint ``--depth 1`` a chur le `` git clone`` chun gan "
"bacadh le híoslódáil a dhéanamh ar stair tiomantais Django go léir, rud a "
"laghdaíonn aistriú sonraí ó ~ 250 MB go ~ 70 MB."

msgid ""
"Now that you have a local copy of Django, you can install it just like you "
"would install any package using ``pip``. The most convenient way to do so is "
"by using a *virtual environment*, which is a feature built into Python that "
"allows you to keep a separate directory of installed packages for each of "
"your projects so that they don't interfere with each other."
msgstr ""
"Anois go bhfuil cóip áitiúil de Django agat, is féidir leat é a shuiteáil "
"díreach mar a dhéanfá aon phacáiste a shuiteáil ag baint úsáide as ``pip``. "
"Is é an bealach is áisiúla chun é sin a dhéanamh ná trí *virtual environment "
"*a úsáid, ar gné é atá tógtha isteach i Python a ligeann duit eolaire ar "
"leith de phacáistí suiteáilte a choinneáil do gach ceann de do thionscadail "
"ionas nach gcuirfidh siad isteach ar a chéile."

msgid ""
"It's a good idea to keep all your virtual environments in one place, for "
"example in ``.virtualenvs/`` in your home directory."
msgstr ""
"Is smaoineamh maith é do thimpeallachtaí fíorúla go léir a choinneáil in aon "
"áit amháin, mar shampla i ``.virtualenvs/`` i d'eolaire baile."

msgid "Create a new virtual environment by running:"
msgstr "Cruthaigh timpeallacht fhíorúil nua trí na nithe seo a leanas a rith:"

msgid "The path is where the new environment will be saved on your computer."
msgstr "Is é an cosán an áit a sábhálfar an timpeallacht nua ar do ríomhaire."

msgid ""
"The final step in setting up your virtual environment is to activate it:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéim dheiridh maidir le do thimpeallacht fhíorúil a bhunú ná é a "
"ghníomhachtú:"

msgid ""
"If the ``source`` command is not available, you can try using a dot instead:"
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil an t-ordú `` foinse`` ar fáil, is féidir leat triail a bhaint as "
"ponc ina ionad sin:"

msgid ""
"You have to activate the virtual environment whenever you open a new "
"terminal window."
msgstr ""
"Caithfidh tú an timpeallacht fhíorúil a ghníomhachtú aon uair a osclaíonn tú "
"fuinneog teirminéil nua."

msgid "To activate your virtual environment on Windows, run:"
msgstr "Chun do thimpeallacht fhíorúil a ghníomhachtú ar Windows, rith:"

msgid ""
"The name of the currently activated virtual environment is displayed on the "
"command line to help you keep track of which one you are using. Anything you "
"install through ``pip`` while this name is displayed will be installed in "
"that virtual environment, isolated from other environments and system-wide "
"packages."
msgstr ""
"Taispeántar ainm na timpeallachta fíorúla atá gníomhachtaithe faoi láthair "
"ar líne na n-orduithe chun cabhrú leat súil a choinneáil ar an gceann atá in "
"úsáid agat. Déanfar aon rud a shuiteálann tú trí ``pip`` agus an t-ainm seo "
"ar taispeáint a shuiteáil sa timpeallacht fhíorúil sin, scoite amach ó "
"thimpeallachtaí eile agus ó phacáistí ar fud an chórais."

msgid "Go ahead and install the previously cloned copy of Django:"
msgstr ""
"Téigh ar aghaidh agus suiteáil an chóip chlónáilte de Django roimhe seo:"

msgid ""
"The installed version of Django is now pointing at your local copy by "
"installing in editable mode. You will immediately see any changes you make "
"to it, which is of great help when testing your first contribution."
msgstr ""

msgid "Running Django's test suite for the first time"
msgstr "Seomra tástála Django a reáchtáil den chéad uair"

msgid ""
"When contributing to Django it's very important that your code changes don't "
"introduce bugs into other areas of Django. One way to check that Django "
"still works after you make your changes is by running Django's test suite. "
"If all the tests still pass, then you can be reasonably sure that your "
"changes work and haven't broken other parts of Django. If you've never run "
"Django's test suite before, it's a good idea to run it once beforehand to "
"get familiar with its output."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag cur le Django tá sé an-tábhachtach nach dtugann d'athruithe cód "
"fabhtanna isteach i réimsí eile de Django. Bealach amháin chun a sheiceáil "
"go n-oibríonn Django fós tar éis duit do chuid athruithe a dhéanamh ná trí "
"shraith tástála Django a reáchtáil. Má éiríonn leis na tástálacha go léir "
"fós, is féidir leat a bheith réasúnta cinnte go n-oibríonn do chuid "
"athruithe agus nár bhris tú codanna eile de Django. Mura ritheann tú sraith "
"tástála Django riamh roimhe seo, is smaoineamh maith é a reáchtáil uair "
"amháin roimh ré chun dul i dtaithí ar a aschur."

msgid ""
"Before running the test suite, enter the Django ``tests/`` directory using "
"the ``cd tests`` command, and install test dependencies by running:"
msgstr ""
"Sula ritheann tú an tsraith tástála, iontráil an chomhadlann Django ``tests/"
"`` ag baint úsáide as an ordú ``cd tests``, agus suiteáil spleáchais tástála "
"trí rith:"

msgid ""
"If you encounter an error during the installation, your system might be "
"missing a dependency for one or more of the Python packages. Consult the "
"failing package's documentation or search the web with the error message "
"that you encounter."
msgstr ""
"Má thagann tú ar earráid le linn na suiteála, d'fhéadfadh spleáchas a bheith "
"in easnamh ar do chóras le haghaidh ceann amháin nó níos mó de na pacáistí "
"Python. Téigh i gcomhairle le doiciméadú an phacáiste a bhfuil ag teip air "
"nó cuardaigh an gréasán leis an teachtaireacht earráide a thagann ort."

msgid "Now we are ready to run the test suite:"
msgstr "Anois táimid réidh leis an tsraith tástála a rith:"

msgid ""
"Now sit back and relax. Django's entire test suite has thousands of tests, "
"and it takes at least a few minutes to run, depending on the speed of your "
"computer."
msgstr ""
"Now sit back and relax. Django's entire test suite has thousands of tests, "
"and it takes at least a few minutes to run, depending on the speed of your "
"computer."

msgid ""
"While Django's test suite is running, you'll see a stream of characters "
"representing the status of each test as it completes. ``E`` indicates that "
"an error was raised during a test, and ``F`` indicates that a test's "
"assertions failed. Both of these are considered to be test failures. "
"Meanwhile, ``x`` and ``s`` indicate expected failures and skipped tests, "
"respectively. Dots indicate passing tests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Skipped tests are typically due to missing external libraries required to "
"run the test; see :ref:`running-unit-tests-dependencies` for a list of "
"dependencies and be sure to install any for tests related to the changes you "
"are making (we won't need any for this tutorial). Some tests are specific to "
"a particular database backend and will be skipped if not testing with that "
"backend. SQLite is the database backend for the default settings. To run the "
"tests using a different backend, see :ref:`running-unit-tests-settings`."
msgstr ""
"Go hiondúil is mar gheall ar leabharlanna seachtracha a bhíonn ag teastáil "
"chun an tástáil a rith a bhíonn na trialacha scipeála in easnamh; "
"féach :ref:`running-unit-tests-dependencies` le haghaidh liosta spleáchais "
"agus bí cinnte go suiteálann tú ceann ar bith do thástálacha a bhaineann "
"leis na hathruithe atá á dhéanamh agat (ní bheidh aon ghá againn don rang "
"teagaisc seo). Baineann roinnt tástálacha go sonrach le hinneal bunachair "
"shonraí ar leith agus déanfar iad a scipeáil mura ndéantar iad a thástáil "
"leis an inneall sin. Is é SQLite inneall an bhunachair shonraí do na "
"socruithe réamhshocraithe. Chun na trialacha a rith ag baint úsáide as "
"inneall difriúil, féach :tag:`running-unit-tests-settings`."

msgid ""
"Once the tests complete, you should be greeted with a message informing you "
"whether the test suite passed or failed. Since you haven't yet made any "
"changes to Django's code, the entire test suite **should** pass. If you get "
"failures or errors make sure you've followed all of the previous steps "
"properly. See :ref:`running-unit-tests` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh na trialacha críochnaithe, ba chóir teachtaireacht a chur "
"chugat ag cur in iúl duit cé acu ar éirigh nó nár éirigh leis an tsraith "
"tástála. Ós rud é nach bhfuil aon athruithe déanta agat fós ar chód Django, "
"ba chóir go mbeadh an tsraith tástála ar fad **ba chóir ** pas a fháil. Má "
"fhaigheann tú teipeanna nó earráidí déan cinnte gur lean tú gach ceann de na "
"céimeanna roimhe seo i gceart. Féach :ref:`running-unit-tests` le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh eolais."

msgid ""
"Note that the latest Django \"main\" branch may not always be stable. When "
"developing against \"main\", you can check `Django's continuous integration "
"builds`__ to determine if the failures are specific to your machine or if "
"they are also present in Django's official builds. If you click to view a "
"particular build, you can view the \"Configuration Matrix\" which shows "
"failures broken down by Python version and database backend."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go mb'fhéidir nach mbeadh an brainse \"príomh\" Django is "
"déanaí cobhsaí i gcónaí. Agus tú ag forbairt i gcoinne \"príomh\", is féidir "
"leat `Tógann comhtháthú leanúnach Django` a sheiceáil __ chun a chinneadh an "
"bhfuil na teipeanna sonrach do do mheaisín nó má tá siad i láthair freisin i "
"dtógáil oifigiúil Django. Má chliceálann tú chun amharc ar thógáil ar leith, "
"is féidir leat féachaint ar an \"Maitrís Cumraíochta\" a thaispeánann "
"teipeanna briste síos de réir leagan Python agus inneall bunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"For this tutorial and the ticket we're working on, testing against SQLite is "
"sufficient, however, it's possible (and sometimes necessary) to :ref:`run "
"the tests using a different database <running-unit-tests-settings>`. When "
"making UI changes, you will need to :ref:`run the Selenium tests <running-"
"selenium-tests>`."
msgstr ""
"Don teagasc seo agus don ticéad a bhfuilimid ag obair air, is leor an "
"tástáil in aghaidh SQLite, áfach, is féidir (agus uaireanta is gá) :ref:`na "
"tástálacha a rith ag baint úsáide as bunachar sonraí eile <running-unit-"
"tests-settings>`. Agus athruithe comhéadain á ndéanamh agat, beidh "
"ort :tag:`na tástálacha Seiléiniam <running-seiléiniam-tests> a rith."

msgid "Working on an approved new feature"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For this tutorial, we'll work on a \"fake accepted ticket\" as a case study. "
"Here are the imaginary details:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ticket #99999 -- Allow making toast"
msgstr "Ticéad #99999 -- Ceadaigh tósta a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"Django should provide a function ``django.shortcuts.make_toast()`` that "
"returns ``'toast'``."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir do Django feidhm ``django.shortcuts.make_toast()`` a chur ar fáil a "
"fhilleann ``'toast``'."

msgid "We'll now implement this feature and associated tests."
msgstr "Cuirfimid an ghné seo agus na trialacha gaolmhara i bhfeidhm anois."

msgid "Creating a branch"
msgstr "Brainse a chruthú"

msgid "Before making any changes, create a new branch for the ticket:"
msgstr "Sula ndéanfaidh tú aon athruithe, cruthaigh brainse nua don ticéad:"

msgid ""
"You can choose any name that you want for the branch, \"ticket_99999\" is an "
"example. All changes made in this branch will be specific to the ticket and "
"won't affect the main copy of the code that we cloned earlier."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat aon ainm is mian leat a roghnú don bhrainse, is sampla é "
"\"ticket_99999\". Beidh na hathruithe ar fad a dhéanfar sa bhrainse seo "
"sonrach don ticéad agus ní bheidh tionchar acu ar an bpríomhchóip den chód a "
"chlónáil muid níos luaithe."

msgid "Writing some tests for your ticket"
msgstr "Scríobh roinnt tástálacha do do thicéad"

msgid ""
"In most cases, for a contribution to be accepted into Django it has to "
"include tests. For bug fix contributions, this means writing a regression "
"test to ensure that  the bug is never reintroduced into Django later on. A "
"regression test should be written in such a way that it will fail while the "
"bug still exists and pass once the bug has been fixed. For contributions "
"containing new features, you'll need to include tests which ensure that the "
"new features are working correctly. They too should fail when the new "
"feature is not present, and then pass once it has been implemented."
msgstr ""
"I bhformhór na gcásanna, chun ranníocaíocht a ghlacadh isteach i Django "
"caithfidh sé tástálacha a chur san áireamh. Maidir le ranníocaíochtaí a "
"shocrú fabht, ciallaíonn sé seo tástáil aischéimnithí a scríobh chun a "
"chinntiú nach n-athbhunaítear an fabht i Django níos déanaí. Ba chóir "
"tástáil aischéimnithí a scríobh sa chaoi is go dteipfidh air agus an fabht "
"fós ann agus pas a fháil nuair a bheidh an fabht socraithe. I gcás "
"ranníocaíochtaí ina bhfuil gnéithe nua, beidh ort tástálacha a chur san "
"áireamh a chinntíonn go bhfuil na gnéithe nua ag obair i gceart. Ba chóir go "
"dteipfeadh orthu freisin nuair nach bhfuil an ghné nua i láthair, agus ansin "
"pas a fháil nuair a bheidh sé curtha i bhfeidhm."

msgid ""
"A good way to do this is to write your new tests first, before making any "
"changes to the code. This style of development is called `test-driven "
"development`__ and can be applied to both entire projects and single "
"changes. After writing your tests, you then run them to make sure that they "
"do indeed fail (since you haven't fixed that bug or added that feature yet). "
"If your new tests don't fail, you'll need to fix them so that they do. After "
"all, a regression test that passes regardless of whether a bug is present is "
"not very helpful at preventing that bug from reoccurring down the road."
msgstr ""
"Bealach maith chun é seo a dhéanamh ná do thástálacha nua a scríobh ar dtús, "
"sula ndéanann tú aon athruithe ar an gcód. Tugtar `forbairt faoi thionchar "
"tástála` ar an stíl forbartha seo agus is féidir é a chur i bhfeidhm ar "
"thionscadail iomlána agus ar athruithe aonair araon. Tar éis duit do chuid "
"tástálacha a scríobh, ritheann tú leo ansin chun a chinntiú go dteipeann "
"orthu go deimhin (ós rud é nach bhfuil an fabht sin socraithe agat nó gur "
"chuir tú an ghné sin leis go fóill). Mura dteipeann ar do thástálacha nua, "
"beidh ort iad a shocrú ionas go ndéanfaidh siad. Tar éis an tsaoil, níl "
"tástáil aischéimnithí a théann beag beann ar cibé an bhfuil fabht i láthair "
"an-chabhrach chun cosc a chur ar an fabht sin dul síos an bóthar."

msgid "Now for our hands-on example."
msgstr "Anois le haghaidh ár lámha-ar shampla."

msgid "Writing a test for ticket #99999"
msgstr "Tástáil a scríobh le haghaidh ticéad #99999"

msgid ""
"In order to resolve this ticket, we'll add a ``make_toast()`` function to "
"the ``django.shortcuts`` module. First we are going to write a test that "
"tries to use the function and check that its output looks correct."
msgstr ""
"Chun an ticéad seo a réiteach, cuirfimid feidhm ``make_toast()`` leis an "
"modúl ``django.shortcuts``. Ar dtús táimid chun tástáil a scríobh a dhéanann "
"iarracht an fheidhm a úsáid agus a sheiceáil go bhfuil cuma cheart ar an "
"aschur."

msgid ""
"Navigate to Django's ``tests/shortcuts/`` folder and create a new file "
"``test_make_toast.py``. Add the following code::"
msgstr ""
"Téigh chuig fillteán ``tests/shortcuts/`` Django agus cruthaigh comhad nua "
"``test_make_toast.py``. Cuir an cód seo a leanas leis::"

msgid "This test checks that the ``make_toast()`` returns ``'toast'``."
msgstr ""
"Seiceálann an tástáil seo go bhfilleann an ``make_toast()`` ar ``'toast'``."

msgid "But this testing thing looks kinda hard..."
msgstr "Ach tá cuma kinda crua ar an rud tástála seo..."

msgid ""
"If you've never had to deal with tests before, they can look a little hard "
"to write at first glance. Fortunately, testing is a *very* big subject in "
"computer programming, so there's lots of information out there:"
msgstr ""
"Mura raibh ort déileáil le tástálacha roimhe seo, is féidir leo breathnú "
"beagán deacair a scríobh ar an gcéad amharc. Ar ámharaí an tsaoil, is ábhar "
"mór *an-* é tástáil i gcláir ríomhaire, mar sin tá go leor eolais amuigh "
"ansin:"

msgid ""
"A good first look at writing tests for Django can be found in the "
"documentation on :doc:`/topics/testing/overview`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir breathnú ar dtús maith ar thástálacha scríbhneoireachta do Django "
"a fháil sna doiciméid ar :d oc:`/topics/testing/overview`."

msgid ""
"Dive Into Python (a free online book for beginning Python developers) "
"includes a great `introduction to Unit Testing`__."
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn Dive Into Python (leabhar ar líne saor in aisce d'fhorbróirí "
"Python tosaigh) `réamhrá iontach ar Thástáil Aonaid`__."

msgid ""
"After reading those, if you want something a little meatier to sink your "
"teeth into, there's always the Python :mod:`unittest` documentation."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis duit iad siúd a léamh, más mian leat rud beag meatier chun do chuid "
"fiacla a dhoirteadh isteach, tá doiciméadú Python :mod:'unittest' ann i "
"gcónaí."

msgid "Running your new test"
msgstr "Do thástáil nua a reáchtáil"

msgid ""
"Since we haven't made any modifications to ``django.shortcuts`` yet, our "
"test should fail. Let's run all the tests in the ``shortcuts`` folder to "
"make sure that's really what happens. ``cd`` to the Django ``tests/`` "
"directory and run:"
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é nach bhfuil aon mhodhnuithe déanta againn ar ``django.shortcuts`` "
"fós, ba cheart go dteipfeadh ar ár dtástáil. Rithimis na trialacha go léir "
"san fhillteán ``shortcuts`` chun a chinntiú gurb é sin an rud a tharlaíonn i "
"ndáiríre. ``cd`` chuig eolaire Django ``tests/`` agus rith:"

msgid ""
"If the tests ran correctly, you should see one failure corresponding to the "
"test method we added, with this error:"
msgstr ""
"Má rith na tástálacha i gceart, ba cheart go bhfeicfeá teip amháin a "
"fhreagraíonn don mhodh tástála a chuireamar leis, leis an earráid seo:"

msgid ""
"If all of the tests passed, then you'll want to make sure that you added the "
"new test shown above to the appropriate folder and file name."
msgstr ""
"Má éirigh leis na tástálacha go léir, beidh tú ag iarraidh a chinntiú gur "
"chuir tú an tástáil nua a thaispeántar thuas leis an bhfillteán cuí agus "
"leis an ainm comhaid."

msgid "Writing the code for your ticket"
msgstr "Scríobh an cód do do thicéad"

msgid "Next we'll be adding the ``make_toast()`` function."
msgstr "Ansin cuirfimid an fheidhm ``make_toast()`` leis."

msgid ""
"Navigate to the ``django/`` folder and open the ``shortcuts.py`` file. At "
"the bottom, add::"
msgstr ""
"Déan nascleanúint go dtí an fillteán ``django/`` agus oscail an comhad "
"``aicearraí.py``. Ag an mbun, cuir leis::"

msgid ""
"Now we need to make sure that the test we wrote earlier passes, so we can "
"see whether the code we added is working correctly. Again, navigate to the "
"Django ``tests/`` directory and run:"
msgstr ""
"Anois ní mór dúinn a chinntiú go dtéann an tástáil a scríobh muid níos "
"luaithe, ionas gur féidir linn a fheiceáil an bhfuil an cód a chuir muid "
"leis ag obair i gceart. Arís, téigh chuig eolaire Django ``tests/`` agus "
"rith:"

msgid ""
"Everything should pass. If it doesn't, make sure you correctly added the "
"function to the correct file."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh gach rud pas a fháil. Mura bhfuil, cinntigh gur chuir tú "
"an fheidhm leis an gcomhad ceart i gceart."

msgid "Running Django's test suite for the second time"
msgstr "Seomra tástála Django a reáchtáil don dara huair"

msgid ""
"Once you've verified that your changes and test are working correctly, it's "
"a good idea to run the entire Django test suite to verify that your change "
"hasn't introduced any bugs into other areas of Django. While successfully "
"passing the entire test suite doesn't guarantee your code is bug free, it "
"does help identify many bugs and regressions that might otherwise go "
"unnoticed."
msgstr ""
"Once you've verified that your changes and test are working correctly, it's "
"a good idea to run the entire Django test suite to verify that your change "
"hasn't introduced any bugs into other areas of Django. While successfully "
"passing the entire test suite doesn't guarantee your code is bug free, it "
"does help identify many bugs and regressions that might otherwise go "
"unnoticed."

msgid ""
"To run the entire Django test suite, ``cd`` into the Django ``tests/`` "
"directory and run:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an tsraith tástála Django ar fad a reáchtáil, ``cd`` isteach san "
"eolaire Django ``tests/`` agus rith:"

msgid "Writing Documentation"
msgstr "Cáipéisíocht Scríbhneoireachta"

msgid ""
"This is a new feature, so it should be documented. Open the file ``docs/"
"topics/http/shortcuts.txt`` and add the following at the end of the file:"
msgstr ""
"Is gné nua é seo, mar sin ba chóir é a dhoiciméadú. Oscail an comhad ``docs/"
"topics/http/shortcuts.txt`` agus cuir an méid seo a leanas ag deireadh an "
"chomhaid:"

msgid ""
"Since this new feature will be in an upcoming release it is also added to "
"the release notes for the next version of Django. Open the release notes for "
"the latest version in ``docs/releases/``, which at time of writing is "
"``2.2.txt``. Add a note under the \"Minor Features\" header:"
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go mbeidh an ghné nua seo i scaoileadh atá le teacht cuirtear é "
"freisin leis na nótaí scaoilte don chéad leagan eile de Django. Oscail na "
"nótaí eisiúna don leagan is déanaí in ``docs/releases/``, arb é ``2.2.txt' é "
"tráth scríofa. Cuir nóta leis faoin gceanntásc \"Mionghnéithe\":"

msgid ""
"For more information on writing documentation, including an explanation of "
"what the ``versionadded`` bit is all about, see :doc:`/internals/"
"contributing/writing-documentation`. That page also includes an explanation "
"of how to build a copy of the documentation locally, so you can preview the "
"HTML that will be generated."
msgstr ""
"Chun tuilleadh eolais a fháil ar cháipéisíocht scríbhneoireachta, lena n-"
"áirítear míniú ar cad atá i gceist leis an ngiolc ``versionadded``, féach :d "
"oc:'/internals/contributing/writing-documentation'. Cuimsíonn an leathanach "
"sin míniú freisin ar conas cóip de na doiciméid a thógáil go háitiúil, ionas "
"gur féidir leat réamhamharc a dhéanamh ar an HTML a ghinfear."

msgid "Previewing your changes"
msgstr "Réamhamharc ar do chuid athruithe"

msgid ""
"Now it's time to review the changes made in the branch. To stage all the "
"changes ready for commit, run:"
msgstr ""
"Anois tá sé in am athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar na hathruithe atá déanta sa "
"chraobh. Chun na hathruithe go léir a chur ar stáitse réidh le tiomantas, "
"rith:"

msgid ""
"Then display the differences between your current copy of Django (with your "
"changes) and the revision that you initially checked out earlier in the "
"tutorial with:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin taispeáin na difríochtaí idir do chóip reatha de Django (le do chuid "
"athruithe) agus an t-athbhreithniú a sheiceáil tú ar dtús níos luaithe sa "
"rang teagaisc le:"

msgid "Use the arrow keys to move up and down."
msgstr "Bain úsáid as na heochracha arrow chun bogadh suas agus síos."

msgid ""
"When you're done previewing the changes, hit the ``q`` key to return to the "
"command line. If the diff looked okay, it's time to commit the changes."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bhíonn réamhamharc déanta agat ar na hathruithe, buail an eochair "
"``q`` chun filleadh ar líne na n-orduithe. Má d'fhéach an diff ceart go "
"leor, tá sé in am na hathruithe a dhéanamh."

msgid "Committing the changes"
msgstr "Na hathruithe a dhéanamh"

msgid "To commit the changes:"
msgstr "Chun na hathruithe a ghealladh:"

msgid ""
"This opens up a text editor to type the commit message. Follow "
"the :ref:`commit message guidelines <committing-guidelines>` and write a "
"message like:"
msgstr ""
"Osclaíonn sé seo eagarthóir téacs chun an teachtaireacht tiomantais a "
"chlóscríobh. Lean an :ref:`commit message guidelines<committing-guidelines>` "
"agus scríobh teachtaireacht mar seo a leanas:"

msgid "Pushing the commit and making a pull request"
msgstr "An tiomantas a bhrú agus iarratas tarraingthe a dhéanamh"

msgid ""
"After committing the changes, send it to your fork on GitHub (substitute "
"\"ticket_99999\" with the name of your branch if it's different):"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis duit na hathruithe a dhéanamh, seol chuig do forc é ar GitHub (cuir "
"\"ticket_99999\" in ionad ainm do bhrainse má tá sé difriúil):"

msgid ""
"You can create a pull request by visiting the `Django GitHub page <https://"
"github.com/django/django/>`_. You'll see your branch under \"Your recently "
"pushed branches\". Click \"Compare & pull request\" next to it."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat iarratas tarraingthe a chruthú trí chuairt a thabhairt ar an "
"leathanach `Django GitHub <https://github.com/django/django/>`_. Feicfidh tú "
"do chraobh faoi \"Do chraobhacha a bhrúitear le déanaí\". Cliceáil \"Déan "
"comparáid idir & iarratas tarraingt\" in aice leis."

msgid ""
"Please don't do it for this tutorial, but on the next page that displays a "
"preview of the changes, you would click \"Create pull request\"."
msgstr ""
"Ná déan é don rang teagaisc seo le do thoil, ach ar an gcéad leathanach eile "
"a thaispeánann réamhamharc ar na hathruithe, chliceáilfeá \"Cruthaigh "
"iarratas tarraingthe\"."

msgid "Next steps"
msgstr "Na chéad chéimeanna eile"

msgid ""
"Congratulations, you've learned how to make a pull request to Django! "
"Details of more advanced techniques you may need are in :doc:`/internals/"
"contributing/writing-code/working-with-git`."
msgstr ""
"Comhghairdeas, d'fhoghlaim tú conas iarratas tarraingthe a dhéanamh chuig "
"Django! Tá sonraí faoi theicnící níos forbartha a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ag "
"teastáil uait in :d oc:`/internals/contributing/writing-code/working-with-"
"git`."

msgid ""
"Now you can put those skills to good use by helping to improve Django's "
"codebase."
msgstr ""
"Anois is féidir leat na scileanna sin a úsáid go maith trí chabhrú le "
"codebase Django a fheabhsú."

msgid "More information for new contributors"
msgstr "Tuilleadh eolais do ranníocóirí nua"

msgid ""
"Before you get too into contributing to Django, there's a little more "
"information on contributing that you should probably take a look at:"
msgstr ""
"Sula gcuirfidh tú isteach ar ranníoc le Django freisin, tá beagán faisnéise "
"breise ar rannchuidiú ar cheart duit féachaint air:"

msgid ""
"You should make sure to read Django's documentation on :doc:`claiming "
"tickets and submitting pull requests </internals/contributing/writing-code/"
"submitting-patches>`. It covers Trac etiquette, how to claim tickets for "
"yourself, expected coding style (both for code and docs), and many other "
"important details."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart duit a chinntiú go léifidh tú doiciméadú Django ar :doc:`ticéid a "
"éileamh agus iarratais tarraingthe a chur isteach </internals/contributing/"
"writing-code/submitting-patches>`. Clúdaíonn sé béasaíocht Trac, conas "
"ticéid a éileamh duit féin, an stíl chódaithe a bhfuiltear ag súil leis (le "
"haghaidh cód agus doiciméad), agus go leor sonraí tábhachtacha eile."

msgid ""
"First time contributors should also read Django's :doc:`documentation for "
"first time contributors</internals/contributing/new-contributors/>`. It has "
"lots of good advice for those of us who are new to helping out with Django."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart do ranníocóirí céaduaire :d oc:`documentation for first time "
"contributors</internals/contributing/new-contributors/>` a léamh freisin. Tá "
"go leor comhairle mhaith ann dóibh siúd againn atá nua chun cabhrú le Django."

msgid ""
"After those, if you're still hungry for more information about contributing, "
"you can always browse through the rest of :doc:`Django's documentation on "
"contributing</internals/contributing/index>`. It contains a ton of useful "
"information and should be your first source for answering any questions you "
"might have."
msgstr ""
"Ina dhiaidh sin, má tá ocras ort fós le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais faoi "
"rannchuidiú, is féidir leat brabhsáil i gcónaí tríd an gcuid eile de :d "
"oc:`Django's documentation on contributing</internals/contributing/index>`. "
"Tá tonna eolais úsáideach ann agus ba chóir go mbeadh sé ar do chéad fhoinse "
"chun aon cheisteanna a d'fhéadfadh a bheith agat a fhreagairt."

msgid "Finding your first real ticket"
msgstr "Do chéad ticéad fíor a aimsiú"

msgid ""
"Once you've looked through some of that information, you'll be ready to go "
"out and find a ticket of your own to contribute to. Pay special attention to "
"tickets with the \"easy pickings\" criterion. These tickets are often much "
"simpler in nature and are great for first time contributors. Once you're "
"familiar with contributing to Django, you can start working on more "
"difficult and complicated tickets."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú ag breathnú trí chuid den fhaisnéis sin, beidh tú réidh le "
"dul amach agus ticéad de do chuid féin a fháil chun cur leis. Tabhair aird "
"ar leith ar thicéid leis an gcritéar \"piocadh éasca\". Is minic a bhíonn na "
"ticéid seo i bhfad níos simplí agus tá siad iontach do rannpháirtithe den "
"chéad uair. Nuair a bhíonn tú eolach ar rannchuidiú le Django, is féidir "
"leat tosú ag obair ar thicéid níos deacra agus níos casta."

msgid ""
"If you just want to get started already (and nobody would blame you!), try "
"taking a look at the list of `easy tickets without a branch`__ and the `easy "
"tickets that have branches which need improvement`__. If you're familiar "
"with writing tests, you can also look at the list of `easy tickets that need "
"tests`__. Remember to follow the guidelines about claiming tickets that were "
"mentioned in the link to Django's documentation on :doc:`claiming tickets "
"and submitting branches </internals/contributing/writing-code/submitting-"
"patches>`."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat tosú cheana féin (agus ní chuirfeadh aon duine an milleán "
"ort!), déan iarracht féachaint ar an liosta `ticéad éasca gan brainse`__ "
"agus ar na `ticéad éasca a bhfuil craobhacha de dhíth orthu a fheabhsú`__. "
"Má tá tú eolach ar thrialacha scríbhneoireachta, is féidir leat breathnú "
"freisin ar an liosta `ticéad éasca a bhfuil tástálacha ag teastáil uathu`__. "
"Ná déan dearmad na treoirlínte a leanúint maidir le ticéid a éileamh a luadh "
"sa nasc chuig doiciméadú Django ar :doc: `ticéad a éileamh agus craobhacha a "
"chur isteach </internals/ranníocaíocht/cód-scríobh/submitting-patches>`."

msgid "What's next after creating a pull request?"
msgstr "Cad atá romhainn tar éis iarratas tarraingthe a chruthú?"

msgid ""
"After a ticket has a branch, it needs to be reviewed by a second set of "
"eyes. After submitting a pull request, update the ticket metadata by setting "
"the flags on the ticket to say \"has patch\", \"doesn't need tests\", etc, "
"so others can find it for review. Contributing doesn't necessarily always "
"mean writing code from scratch. Reviewing open pull requests is also a very "
"helpful contribution. See :doc:`/internals/contributing/triaging-tickets` "
"for details."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis brainse a bheith ag ticéad, ní mór don dara sraith súl athbhreithniú "
"a dhéanamh air. Tar éis iarratas tarraingthe a chur isteach, nuashonraigh "
"meiteashonraí an ticéid trí na bratacha a shocrú ar an ticéad chun \"tá "
"paiste\" a rá, \"ní gá tástálacha\", srl, ionas gur féidir le daoine eile é "
"a fháil le haghaidh athbhreithnithe. Ní gá go gciallódh cur leis an gcód "
"scríbhneoireachta ó thús i gcónaí. Is ranníocaíocht an-chabhrach é "
"athbhreithniú a dhéanamh ar iarratais ar tharraingt oscailte freisin. "
"Féach :d oc:`internals/contributing/triaging-tickets` le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Ag tosnú"

msgid ""
"New to Django? Or to web development in general? Well, you came to the right "
"place: read this material to quickly get up and running."
msgstr ""
"Nua go Django? Nó le forbairt gréasáin i gcoitinne? Bhuel, tháinig tú go dtí "
"an áit cheart: léigh an t-ábhar seo chun éirí agus rith go tapa."

msgid ""
"If you're new to Python_, you might want to start by getting an idea of what "
"the language is like. Django is 100% Python, so if you've got minimal "
"comfort with Python you'll probably get a lot more out of Django."
msgstr ""
"Más rud é nach bhfuil nua agat do Python_, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat tosú le "
"tuairim a fháil faoin teanga atá i gceist. Tá Django 100% Python, mar sin má "
"tá tú ar do chompord íosta le Python is dócha go mbainfidh tú i bhfad níos "
"mó as Django."

msgid ""
"If you're new to programming entirely, you might want to start with this "
"`list of Python resources for non-programmers`_"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú nua le ríomhchlárú go hiomlán, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat tosú leis "
"an `liosta acmhainní Python seo do neamh-ríomhchláraitheoirí`_"

msgid ""
"If you already know a few other languages and want to get up to speed with "
"Python quickly, we recommend referring the official `Python documentation`_, "
"which provides comprehensive and authoritative information about the "
"language, as well as links to other resources such as a list of `books about "
"Python`_."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cúpla teanga eile ar eolas agat cheana féin agus go bhfuil tú ag "
"iarraidh dul i ngleic le Python go tapa, molaimid tagairt a dhéanamh don "
"`cháipéisíocht Python`_ oifigiúil, a sholáthraíonn eolas cuimsitheach agus "
"údarásach faoin teanga, chomh maith le naisc chuig acmhainní eile mar a "
"Liosta de na leabhair faoi Python."

msgid "Quick install guide"
msgstr "Treoir suiteála tapa"

msgid ""
"Before you can use Django, you'll need to get it installed. We have "
"a :doc:`complete installation guide </topics/install>` that covers all the "
"possibilities; this guide will guide you to a minimal installation that'll "
"work while you walk through the introduction."
msgstr ""
"Sula féidir leat Django a úsáid, beidh ort é a shuiteáil. Tá :d oc: 'treoir "
"`suiteála iomlán </topics/install> againn a chlúdaíonn na féidearthachtaí go "
"léir; Tabharfaidh an treoir seo treoir duit maidir le suiteáil íosta a "
"oibreoidh agus tú ag siúl tríd an réamhrá."

msgid "Install Python"
msgstr "Suiteáil Python"

msgid ""
"Being a Python web framework, Django requires Python. See :ref:`faq-python-"
"version-support` for details. Python includes a lightweight database called "
"SQLite_ so you won't need to set up a database just yet."
msgstr ""
"A bheith ina chreat gréasáin Python, éilíonn Django Python. Féach :tag:`faq-"
"python-version-support` le haghaidh sonraí. Áiríonn Python bunachar sonraí "
"éadrom ar a dtugtar SQLite_ mar sin ní bheidh ort bunachar sonraí a bhunú go "
"fóill."

msgid ""
"Get the latest version of Python at https://www.python.org/downloads/ or "
"with your operating system's package manager."
msgstr ""
"Faigh an leagan is déanaí de Python ag https://www.python.org/downloads/ nó "
"le bainisteoir pacáiste do chórais oibriúcháin."

msgid ""
"You can verify that Python is installed by typing ``python`` from your "
"shell; you should see something like:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat a fhíorú go bhfuil Python suiteáilte trí `` python`` a "
"chlóscríobh ó do bhlaosc; ba cheart duit rud éigin mar seo a fheiceáil:"

msgid "Set up a database"
msgstr "Socraigh bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"This step is only necessary if you'd like to work with a \"large\" database "
"engine like PostgreSQL, MariaDB, MySQL, or Oracle. To install such a "
"database, consult the :ref:`database installation information <database-"
"installation>`."
msgstr ""
"Níl an chéim seo riachtanach ach amháin más mian leat oibriú le hinneall "
"bunachar sonraí \"mór\" mar PostgreSQL, MariaDB, MySQL, nó Oracle. Chun a "
"leithéid de bhunachar sonraí a shuiteáil, féach ar an :ref:`faisnéis "
"suiteála bunachar sonraí <database-installation>`."

msgid "Install Django"
msgstr "Suiteáil Django"

msgid "You've got three options to install Django:"
msgstr "Tá trí rogha agat Django a shuiteáil:"

msgid ""
":ref:`Install an official release <installing-official-release>`. This is "
"the best approach for most users."
msgstr ""
":ref:'Suiteáil scaoileadh oifigiúil<installing-official-release>'. Is é seo "
"an cur chuige is fearr d'fhormhór na n-úsáideoirí."

msgid ""
"Install a version of Django :ref:`provided by your operating system "
"distribution <installing-distribution-package>`."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil leagan de Django :ref:'provided by your operating system "
"distribution<installing-distribution-package>'."

msgid ""
":ref:`Install the latest development version <installing-development-"
"version>`. This option is for enthusiasts who want the latest-and-greatest "
"features and aren't afraid of running brand new code. You might encounter "
"new bugs in the development version, but reporting them helps the "
"development of Django. Also, releases of third-party packages are less "
"likely to be compatible with the development version than with the latest "
"stable release."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Install the latest development version <installing-development-"
"version>`. This option is for enthusiasts who want the latest-and-greatest "
"features and aren't afraid of running brand new code. You might encounter "
"new bugs in the development version, but reporting them helps the "
"development of Django. Also, releases of third-party packages are less "
"likely to be compatible with the development version than with the latest "
"stable release."

msgid ""
"Always refer to the documentation that corresponds to the version of Django "
"you're using!"
msgstr ""
"Déan tagairt i gcónaí do na doiciméid a fhreagraíonn don leagan de Django "
"atá in úsáid agat!"

msgid ""
"If you do either of the first two steps, keep an eye out for parts of the "
"documentation marked **new in development version**. That phrase flags "
"features that are only available in development versions of Django, and they "
"likely won't work with an official release."
msgstr ""
"Má dhéanann tú ceachtar den chéad dá chéim, coinnigh súil amach do chodanna "
"de na doiciméid marcáilte **nua i leagan forbartha**. Léiríonn an frása sin "
"gnéithe nach bhfuil ar fáil ach i leaganacha forbartha de Django, agus is "
"dócha nach n-oibreoidh siad le heisiúint oifigiúil."

msgid "Verifying"
msgstr "Fíorú"

msgid ""
"To verify that Django can be seen by Python, type ``python`` from your "
"shell. Then at the Python prompt, try to import Django:"
msgstr ""
"Chun a fhíorú gur féidir Django a fheiceáil ag Python, clóscríobh `` "
"python`` ó do bhlaosc. Ansin ag an leid Python, déan iarracht Django a "
"allmhairiú:"

msgid "You may have another version of Django installed."
msgstr "B'fhéidir go bhfuil leagan eile de Django suiteáilte agat."

msgid "That's it!"
msgstr "Sin é!"

msgid ""
"That's it -- you can now :doc:`move onto the tutorial </intro/tutorial01>`."
msgstr ""
"Sin é -- is féidir leat anois :d oc:`move into the tutorial </intro/"
"tutorial01>`."

msgid "Django at a glance"
msgstr "Sracfhéachaint ar Django"

msgid ""
"Because Django was developed in a fast-paced newsroom environment, it was "
"designed to make common web development tasks fast and easy. Here's an "
"informal overview of how to write a database-driven web app with Django."
msgstr ""
"Toisc gur forbraíodh Django i dtimpeallacht seomra nuachta luas tapa, "
"ceapadh é chun tascanna forbartha gréasáin coitianta a dhéanamh go tapa agus "
"éasca. Seo forbhreathnú neamhfhoirmiúil ar conas aip gréasáin bunaithe ar "
"bhunachar sonraí a scríobh le Django."

msgid ""
"The goal of this document is to give you enough technical specifics to "
"understand how Django works, but this isn't intended to be a tutorial or "
"reference -- but we've got both! When you're ready to start a project, you "
"can :doc:`start with the tutorial </intro/tutorial01>` or :doc:`dive right "
"into more detailed documentation </topics/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Is é sprioc an doiciméid seo go leor sonraí teicniúla a thabhairt duit chun "
"tuiscint a fháil ar an gcaoi a n-oibríonn Django, ach níl sé i gceist gur "
"teagasc nó tagairt a bheadh ​​​​ann -- ach tá an dá cheann againn! Nuair atá tú "
"réidh le tionscadal a thosú, is féidir leat :doc:`tosú leis an rang teagaisc "
"</intro/tutorial01>` nó :doc: `tumadh díreach isteach i gcáipéisíocht níos "
"mionsonraithe </topics/index>`."

msgid "Design your model"
msgstr "Dear do mhúnla"

msgid ""
"Although you can use Django without a database, it comes with an `object-"
"relational mapper`_ in which you describe your database layout in Python "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Cé gur féidir leat Django a úsáid gan bunachar sonraí, tagann sé le `object-"
"relational mapper`_ ina ndéanann tú cur síos ar leagan amach do bhunachar "
"sonraí i gcód Python."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`data-model syntax </topics/db/models>` offers many rich ways of "
"representing your models -- so far, it's been solving many years' worth of "
"database-schema problems. Here's a quick example:"
msgstr ""
"The :doc:`data-model syntax </topics/db/models>` offers many rich ways of "
"representing your models -- so far, it's been solving many years' worth of "
"database-schema problems. Here's a quick example:"

msgid "``news/models.py``"
msgstr "``news/models.py``"

msgid "Install it"
msgstr "Suiteáil é"

msgid ""
"Next, run the Django command-line utilities to create the database tables "
"automatically:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, reáchtáil na fóntais ordú-líne Django a chruthú ar na táblaí bunachar "
"sonraí go huathoibríoch:"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`makemigrations` command looks at all your available models and "
"creates migrations for whichever tables don't already "
"exist. :djadmin:`migrate` runs the migrations and creates tables in your "
"database, as well as optionally providing :doc:`much richer schema control </"
"topics/migrations>`."
msgstr ""
"Breathnaíonn an t-ordú :d jadmin: `makemigrations` ar do chuid samhlacha go "
"léir atá ar fáil agus cruthaíonn sé imirce do cibé táblaí nach bhfuil ann "
"cheana féin. :d JADMIN: Ritheann 'imirce' na himirce agus cruthaíonn sé "
"táblaí i do bhunachar sonraí, chomh maith le :d OC: `Rialú scéimre i bhfad "
"níos saibhre </topics/migrations>Migrations a sholáthar go roghnach `."

msgid "Enjoy the free API"
msgstr "Bain sult as an API saor in aisce"

msgid ""
"With that, you've got a free, and rich, :doc:`Python API </topics/db/"
"queries>` to access your data. The API is created on the fly, no code "
"generation necessary:"
msgstr ""
"Leis sin, tá tú saor in aisce, agus saibhir, :d oc:`Python API </topics/db/"
"queries>` chun rochtain a fháil ar do shonraí. Cruthaítear an API ar an "
"eitilt, gan aon ghiniúint cód riachtanach:"

msgid ""
"A dynamic admin interface: it's not just scaffolding -- it's the whole house"
msgstr ""
"Comhéadan dinimiciúil riaracháin: níl sé ach scafall - is é an teach ar fad é"

msgid ""
"Once your models are defined, Django can automatically create a "
"professional, production ready :doc:`administrative interface </ref/contrib/"
"admin/index>` -- a website that lets authenticated users add, change and "
"delete objects. The only step required is to register your model in the "
"admin site:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shainmhínítear do mhúnlaí, is féidir le Django a chruthú go "
"huathoibríoch gairmiúil, táirgeadh réidh :d oc: `comhéadan riaracháin </ref/"
"contrib/admin/index>` - suíomh gréasáin a ligeann d'úsáideoirí "
"fíordheimhnithe rudaí a chur leis, a athrú agus a scriosadh. Is é an t-aon "
"chéim atá ag teastáil ná do mhúnla a chlárú ar an suíomh riaracháin:"

msgid "``news/admin.py``"
msgstr "``news/admin.py``"

msgid ""
"The philosophy here is that your site is edited by a staff, or a client, or "
"maybe just you -- and you don't want to have to deal with creating backend "
"interfaces only to manage content."
msgstr ""
"Is é an fhealsúnacht anseo go bhfuil do shuíomh curtha in eagar ag foireann, "
"nó cliant, nó b'fhéidir díreach tú - agus níl tú ag iarraidh déileáil le "
"comhéadain inneall a chruthú ach amháin chun ábhar a bhainistiú."

msgid ""
"One typical workflow in creating Django apps is to create models and get the "
"admin sites up and running as fast as possible, so your staff (or clients) "
"can start populating data. Then, develop the way data is presented to the "
"public."
msgstr ""
"Sreabhadh oibre tipiciúil amháin chun apps Django a chruthú ná samhlacha a "
"chruthú agus na suíomhanna riaracháin a chur ar bun chomh tapa agus is "
"féidir, ionas gur féidir le d'fhoireann (nó do chliaint) tús a chur le "
"sonraí daonra. Ansin, forbairt a dhéanamh ar an mbealach a chuirtear sonraí "
"i láthair an phobail."

msgid "Design your URLs"
msgstr "Dear do URLanna"

msgid ""
"A clean, elegant URL scheme is an important detail in a high-quality web "
"application. Django encourages beautiful URL design and doesn't put any "
"cruft in URLs, like ``.php`` or ``.asp``."
msgstr ""
"Is mionsonra tábhachtach é scéim URL glan galánta i bhfeidhmchlár gréasáin "
"ardchaighdeáin. Spreagann Django dearadh URL álainn agus ní chuireann sé aon "
"chrústa in URLanna, cosúil le ``.php`` nó ``.asp``."

msgid ""
"To design URLs for an app, you create a Python module called a :doc:`URLconf "
"</topics/http/urls>`. A table of contents for your app, it contains a "
"mapping between URL patterns and Python callback functions. URLconfs also "
"serve to decouple URLs from Python code."
msgstr ""
"Chun URLanna a dhearadh le haghaidh aip, cruthaíonn tú modúl Python ar a "
"dtugtar :doc:`URLconf </topics/http/urls>`. Clár ábhar do d’aip, tá mapáil "
"ann idir patrúin URL agus feidhmeanna aisghlaoite Python. Freastalaíonn "
"URLconfs freisin chun URLanna a dhíchúpláil ó chód Python."

msgid ""
"Here's what a URLconf might look like for the ``Reporter``/``Article`` "
"example above:"
msgstr ""
"Seo an chuma a bheadh ​​ar URLconf don sampla ``Tuairisceoir``/``Airteagal`` "
"thuas:"

msgid "``news/urls.py``"
msgstr "``news/urls.py``"

msgid ""
"The code above maps URL paths to Python callback functions (\"views\"). The "
"path strings use parameter tags to \"capture\" values from the URLs. When a "
"user requests a page, Django runs through each path, in order, and stops at "
"the first one that matches the requested URL. (If none of them matches, "
"Django calls a special-case 404 view.) This is blazingly fast, because the "
"paths are compiled into regular expressions at load time."
msgstr ""
"Léarscáilíonn an cód thuas cosáin URL chuig feidhmeanna aisghlao Python "
"(\"amhairc\"). Úsáideann teaghráin na gcosán clibeanna paraiméadar chun "
"luachanna a \"ghabháil\" ó na URLanna. Nuair a iarrann úsáideoir leathanach, "
"ritheann Django trí gach cosán, in ord, agus stopann sé ag an gcéad cheann a "
"mheaitseálann an URL iarrtha. (Mura n-oireann aon cheann acu, glaonn Django "
"radharc cás speisialta 404.) Tá sé seo blazingly tapa, toisc go bhfuil na "
"cosáin le chéile i nathanna rialta ag am ualach."

msgid ""
"Once one of the URL patterns matches, Django calls the given view, which is "
"a Python function. Each view gets passed a request object -- which contains "
"request metadata -- and the values captured in the pattern."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a mheaitseálann ceann de na patrúin URL, glaonn Django ar an radharc a "
"thugtar, arb é feidhm Python é. Rachaidh gach radharc ar aghaidh réad "
"iarratais -- ina bhfuil meiteashonraí iarratais -- agus na luachanna a "
"gabhadh sa phatrún."

msgid ""
"For example, if a user requested the URL \"/articles/2005/05/39323/\", "
"Django would call the function ``news.views.article_detail(request, "
"year=2005, month=5, pk=39323)``."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, dá n-iarrfadh úsáideoir an URL \"/articles/2005/05/39323/\", "
"thabharfadh Django an fheidhm ``news.views.article_detail(iarratas, "
"year=2005, month=5, pk=39323)``."

msgid "Write your views"
msgstr "Scríobh do thuairimí"

msgid ""
"Each view is responsible for doing one of two things: Returning "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` object containing the content for the "
"requested page, or raising an exception such "
"as :class:`~django.http.Http404`. The rest is up to you."
msgstr ""
"Tá gach amharc freagrach as ceann amháin de dhá rud a dhéanamh: Ag filleadh "
"ar rud :class:`~django.http.http.HttpResponse' ina bhfuil an t-ábhar don "
"leathanach iarrtha, nó eisceacht a ardú mar :class:'~django.http.Http404`. "
"Fútsa atá an chuid eile."

msgid ""
"Generally, a view retrieves data according to the parameters, loads a "
"template and renders the template with the retrieved data. Here's an example "
"view for ``year_archive`` from above:"
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, aisghabhann radharc sonraí de réir na bparaiméadar, lódálann "
"sé teimpléad agus cuireann sé an teimpléad leis na sonraí a aisghabháil. Seo "
"radharc samplach do ``year_archive`` thuas:"

msgid "``news/views.py``"
msgstr "``news/views.py``"

msgid ""
"This example uses Django's :doc:`template system </topics/templates>`, which "
"has several powerful features but strives to stay simple enough for non-"
"programmers to use."
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann an sampla seo :doc:`córas teimpléid Django </topics/templates>`, a "
"bhfuil roinnt gnéithe cumhachtacha aige ach a dhéanann iarracht fanacht "
"simplí go leor le húsáid gan ríomhchláraitheoirí."

msgid "Design your templates"
msgstr "Dear do teimpléid"

msgid "The code above loads the ``news/year_archive.html`` template."
msgstr "Luchtaíonn an cód thuas an teimpléad ``news/year_archive.html``."

msgid ""
"Django has a template search path, which allows you to minimize redundancy "
"among templates. In your Django settings, you specify a list of directories "
"to check for templates with :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>`. If a template "
"doesn't exist in the first directory, it checks the second, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Tá cosán cuardaigh teimpléad ag Django, a ligeann duit iomarcaíocht a "
"íoslaghdú i measc teimpléid. I do shocruithe Django, sonraíonn tú liosta "
"eolairí le seiceáil le haghaidh teimpléid le:setting:'DIRS<TEMPLATES-DIRS>'. "
"Mura bhfuil teimpléad ann sa chéad eolaire, seiceálann sé an dara ceann, "
"agus mar sin de."

msgid ""
"Let's say the ``news/year_archive.html`` template was found. Here's what "
"that might look like:"
msgstr ""
"Abraimis gur aimsíodh an teimpléad ``news/year_archive.html``. Seo an chuma "
"a d'fhéadfadh a bheith air sin:"

msgid "``news/templates/news/year_archive.html``"
msgstr "``news/templates/news/year_archive.html``"

msgid ""
"Variables are surrounded by double-curly braces. ``{{ article.headline }}`` "
"means \"Output the value of the article's headline attribute.\" But dots "
"aren't used only for attribute lookup. They also can do dictionary-key "
"lookup, index lookup and function calls."
msgstr ""
"Tá athróga timpeallaithe ag braces dúbailte-curly. Ciallaíonn "
"``{{ article.headline }}`` \"Aschur luach phríomhthréith an ailt.\" Ach ní "
"úsáidtear poncanna ach amháin le haghaidh lookup tréith. Is féidir leo "
"cuardach foclóra-eochair, cuardach innéacs agus glaonna feidhme a dhéanamh "
"freisin."

msgid ""
"Note ``{{ article.pub_date|date:\"F j, Y\" }}`` uses a Unix-style \"pipe\" "
"(the \"|\" character). This is called a template filter, and it's a way to "
"filter the value of a variable. In this case, the date filter formats a "
"Python datetime object in the given format (as found in PHP's date function)."
msgstr ""
"Nóta ``{{ article.pub_date|date:\"F j, Y\" }}`` úsáideann \"píopa\" stíl "
"Unix (an carachtar \"|\"). Tugtar scagaire teimpléid air seo, agus is "
"bealach é chun luach athróg a scagadh. Sa chás seo, formáidí an scagaire "
"dáta réad datetime Python san fhormáid a thugtar (mar atá le fáil i bhfeidhm "
"dáta PHP)."

msgid ""
"You can chain together as many filters as you'd like. You can "
"write :ref:`custom template filters <howto-writing-custom-template-"
"filters>`. You can write :doc:`custom template tags </howto/custom-template-"
"tags>`, which run custom Python code behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an oiread scagairí agus is mian leat a shlabhra le chéile. Is "
"féidir leat scríobh: ref: 'custom template <howto-writing-custom-template-"
"filters>filters'. Is féidir leat scríobh :d oc: 'custom template tags </"
"howto/custom-template-tags>', a ritheann cód saincheaptha Python taobh thiar "
"de na radhairc."

msgid ""
"Finally, Django uses the concept of \"template inheritance\". That's what "
"the ``{% extends \"base.html\" %}`` does. It means \"First load the template "
"called 'base', which has defined a bunch of blocks, and fill the blocks with "
"the following blocks.\" In short, that lets you dramatically cut down on "
"redundancy in templates: each template has to define only what's unique to "
"that template."
msgstr ""
"Ar deireadh, úsáideann Django coincheap \"oidhreacht teimpléid\". Sin a "
"dhéanann an ``{% extends \"base.html\" %}`` . Ciallaíonn sé \"An chéad "
"luchtú an teimpléad ar a dtugtar 'bonn', a bhfuil sainithe a bunch de bloic, "
"agus líon na bloic leis na bloic seo a leanas.\" I mbeagán focal, ligeann sé "
"sin duit gearradh síos go mór ar iomarcaíocht i dteimpléid: ní mór do gach "
"teimpléad ach an méid atá uathúil don teimpléad sin a shainiú."

msgid ""
"Here's what the \"base.html\" template, including the use of :doc:`static "
"files </howto/static-files/index>`, might look like:"
msgstr ""
"Seo an méid a d'fhéadfadh an teimpléad \"base.html\", lena n-áirítear úsáid "
"a bhaint as :d oc: 'comhaid statacha < / howto / static-files / index>, cuma "
"mhaith:"

msgid "``templates/base.html``"
msgstr "``templates/base.html``"

msgid ""
"Simplistically, it defines the look-and-feel of the site (with the site's "
"logo), and provides \"holes\" for child templates to fill. This means that a "
"site redesign can be done by changing a single file -- the base template."
msgstr ""
"Go simplí, sainmhíníonn sé cuma agus mothú an tsuímh (le lógó an tsuímh), "
"agus soláthraíonn sé \"poill\" le haghaidh teimpléid leanaí a líonadh. "
"Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir athdhearadh láithreáin a dhéanamh trí chomhad "
"amháin a athrú - an teimpléad bonn."

msgid ""
"It also lets you create multiple versions of a site, with different base "
"templates, while reusing child templates. Django's creators have used this "
"technique to create strikingly different mobile versions of sites by only "
"creating a new base template."
msgstr ""
"Ligeann sé duit leaganacha éagsúla de shuíomh a chruthú freisin, le "
"teimpléid bhunúsacha éagsúla, agus teimpléid leanaí á n-athúsáid. D'úsáid "
"cruthaitheoirí Django an teicníc seo chun leaganacha soghluaiste éagsúla de "
"shuíomhanna a chruthú trí theimpléad bonn nua a chruthú."

msgid ""
"Note that you don't have to use Django's template system if you prefer "
"another system. While Django's template system is particularly well-"
"integrated with Django's model layer, nothing forces you to use it. For that "
"matter, you don't have to use Django's database API, either. You can use "
"another database abstraction layer, you can read XML files, you can read "
"files off disk, or anything you want. Each piece of Django -- models, views, "
"templates -- is decoupled from the next."
msgstr ""
"Note that you don't have to use Django's template system if you prefer "
"another system. While Django's template system is particularly well-"
"integrated with Django's model layer, nothing forces you to use it. For that "
"matter, you don't have to use Django's database API, either. You can use "
"another database abstraction layer, you can read XML files, you can read "
"files off disk, or anything you want. Each piece of Django -- models, views, "
"templates -- is decoupled from the next."

msgid "This is just the surface"
msgstr "Níl anseo ach an dromchla"

msgid ""
"This has been only a quick overview of Django's functionality. Some more "
"useful features:"
msgstr ""
"Ní raibh anseo ach forbhreathnú tapa ar fheidhmiúlacht Django. Roinnt "
"gnéithe níos úsáidí:"

msgid ""
"A :doc:`caching framework </topics/cache>` that integrates with memcached or "
"other backends."
msgstr ""
"A :d oc:`caching framework </topics/cache>` a chomhtháthaíonn le memcached "
"nó le cúil eile."

msgid ""
"A :doc:`syndication framework </ref/contrib/syndication>` that lets you "
"create RSS and Atom feeds by writing a small Python class."
msgstr ""
"A :d oc:`syndication framework </ref/contrib/syndication>` a ligeann duit "
"fothaí RSS agus Adamh a chruthú trí rang beag Python a scríobh."

msgid ""
"More attractive automatically-generated admin features -- this overview "
"barely scratched the surface."
msgstr ""
"Gnéithe riaracháin níos tarraingtí a ghintear go huathoibríoch - is ar "
"éigean a scríob an forbhreathnú seo an dromchla."

msgid ""
"The next steps are for you to `download Django`_, read :doc:`the tutorial </"
"intro/tutorial01>` and join `the community`_. Thanks for your interest!"
msgstr ""
"Is iad na chéad chéimeanna eile ná `íoslódáil Django`_, léigh :d oc:`the "
"tutorial </intro/tutorial01>` agus páirt a ghlacadh i `the community`_. Go "
"raibh maith agat as do spéis!"

msgid "Advanced tutorial: How to write reusable apps"
msgstr "Ardteagasc: Conas aipeanna in-athúsáidte a scríobh"

msgid ""
"This advanced tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 8 </intro/tutorial08>` "
"left off. We'll be turning our web-poll into a standalone Python package you "
"can reuse in new projects and share with other people."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an rang teagaisc chun cinn seo nuair a d'fhág :d oc: `Tutorial 8 "
"< / intro/tutorial08>` as. Beimid ag casadh ár vótaíocht gréasáin i "
"bpacáiste Python neamhspleách is féidir leat a athúsáid i dtionscadail nua "
"agus a roinnt le daoine eile."

msgid ""
"If you haven't recently completed Tutorials 1–8, we encourage you to review "
"these so that your example project matches the one described below."
msgstr ""
"Mura bhfuil Ranganna Teagaisc 1–8 críochnaithe agat le déanaí, molaimid duit "
"iad seo a athbhreithniú ionas go mbeidh do thionscadal samplach ag teacht "
"leis an gceann a gcuirtear síos air thíos."

msgid "Reusability matters"
msgstr "Baineann cúrsaí ath-inúsáidte"

msgid ""
"It's a lot of work to design, build, test and maintain a web application. "
"Many Python and Django projects share common problems. Wouldn't it be great "
"if we could save some of this repeated work?"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé a lán oibre a dhearadh, a thógáil, a thástáil agus a chothabháil "
"iarratas gréasáin. Tá fadhbanna coitianta ag go leor tionscadal Python agus "
"Django. Nach mbeadh sé go hiontach dá bhféadfaimis cuid den obair seo a "
"shábháil arís agus arís eile?"

msgid ""
"Reusability is the way of life in Python. `The Python Package Index (PyPI) "
"<https://pypi.org/>`_ has a vast range of packages you can use in your own "
"Python programs. Check out `Django Packages <https://djangopackages.org>`_ "
"for existing reusable apps you could incorporate in your project. Django "
"itself is also a normal Python package. This means that you can take "
"existing Python packages or Django apps and compose them into your own web "
"project. You only need to write the parts that make your project unique."
msgstr ""
"Is é reusability an bealach maireachtála i Python. `The Python Package Index "
"(PyPI) <https://pypi.org/>`_ tá réimse leathan pacáistí ann ar féidir leat a "
"úsáid i do chláir Python féin. Amharc ar `Django Packages <https://"
"djangopackages.org>`_ le haghaidh feidhmchláir in-athúsáidte atá ann cheana "
"a d'fhéadfá a ionchorprú i do thionscadal. Is gnáthphacáiste Python é Django "
"féin freisin. Ciallaíonn sé seo gur féidir leat pacáistí Python nó "
"feidhmchláir Django atá ann cheana féin a ghlacadh agus iad a chumadh i do "
"thionscadal gréasáin féin. Ní gá duit ach na codanna a dhéanann do "
"thionscadal uathúil a scríobh."

msgid ""
"Let's say you were starting a new project that needed a polls app like the "
"one we've been working on. How do you make this app reusable? Luckily, "
"you're well on the way already. In :doc:`Tutorial 1 </intro/tutorial01>`, we "
"saw how we could decouple polls from the project-level URLconf using an "
"``include``. In this tutorial, we'll take further steps to make the app easy "
"to use in new projects and ready to publish for others to install and use."
msgstr ""
"Deirimid go raibh tú ag cur tús le tionscadal nua a raibh aip pobalbhreithe "
"ag teastáil uaidh cosúil leis an gceann a raibh muid ag obair air. Conas a "
"dhéantar an aip seo a athúsáid? Ar ámharaí an tsaoil, tá tú go maith ar an "
"mbealach cheana féin. In :d oc:`Tutorial 1 </intro/tutorial01>`, "
"chonaiceamar conas a d'fhéadfaimis pobalbhreitheanna a dhíchúpláil ón "
"URLconf ar leibhéal an tionscadail ag baint úsáide as ``include``. Sa rang "
"teagaisc seo, glacfaimid céimeanna breise chun an aip a dhéanamh éasca le "
"húsáid i dtionscadail nua agus réidh le foilsiú do dhaoine eile le suiteáil "
"agus le húsáid."

msgid "Package? App?"
msgstr "Pacáiste? Aip?"

msgid ""
"A Python :term:`package` provides a way of grouping related Python code for "
"easy reuse. A package contains one or more files of Python code (also known "
"as \"modules\")."
msgstr ""
"A Python :term: soláthraíonn `pacáiste` bealach chun cód Python gaolmhar a "
"ghrúpáil le haghaidh athúsáid éasca. Tá comhad amháin nó níos mó de chód "
"Python (ar a dtugtar \"modúil\") i bpacáiste."

msgid ""
"A package can be imported with ``import foo.bar`` or ``from foo import "
"bar``. For a directory (like ``polls``) to form a package, it must contain a "
"special file ``__init__.py``, even if this file is empty."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir pacáiste a allmhairiú le `` import foo.bar`` nó ``ó foo import "
"bar``. Chun pacáiste a fhoirmiú i gcomhadlann (cosúil le ``vótaíocht``), "
"caithfidh comhad speisialta `` __init__.py`` a bheith ann, fiú má tá an "
"comhad seo folamh."

msgid ""
"A Django *application* is a Python package that is specifically intended for "
"use in a Django project. An application may use common Django conventions, "
"such as having ``models``, ``tests``, ``urls``, and ``views`` submodules."
msgstr ""
"Is pacáiste Python é iarratas Django ** atá beartaithe go sonrach lena úsáid "
"i dtionscadal Django. Féadfaidh feidhmchlár gnásanna coitianta Django a "
"úsáid, mar shampla fo-mhodúil ``samhlacha``, `` tástálacha``, `` urls``, "
"agus ``views``."

msgid ""
"Later on we use the term *packaging* to describe the process of making a "
"Python package easy for others to install. It can be a little confusing, we "
"know."
msgstr ""
"Níos déanaí bainimid úsáid as an téarma *pacáistiú* chun cur síos a dhéanamh "
"ar an bpróiseas chun pacáiste Python a dhéanamh éasca do dhaoine eile a "
"shuiteáil. Is féidir leis a bheith beagán mearbhall, tá a fhios againn."

msgid "Your project and your reusable app"
msgstr "Do thionscadal agus d'aip ath-inúsáidte"

msgid "After the previous tutorials, our project should look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Tar éis na ranganna teagaisc roimhe seo, ba chóir go mbeadh cuma mar seo ar "
"ár dtionscadal:"

msgid ""
"You created ``djangotutorial/templates`` in :doc:`Tutorial 7 </intro/"
"tutorial07>`, and ``polls/templates`` in :doc:`Tutorial 3 </intro/"
"tutorial03>`. Now perhaps it is clearer why we chose to have separate "
"template directories for the project and application: everything that is "
"part of the polls application is in ``polls``. It makes the application self-"
"contained and easier to drop into a new project."
msgstr ""
"Chruthaigh tú ``djangotutorial/templates`` in :d oc:'Tutorial 7 </intro/"
"tutorial07>', agus ``polls/templates`` in :d oc:'Tutorial 3 </intro/"
"tutorial03>'. Anois, b'fhéidir go bhfuil sé níos soiléire cén fáth ar "
"roghnaigh muid eolairí teimpléid ar leith a bheith againn don tionscadal "
"agus don chur i bhfeidhm: tá gach rud atá mar chuid d'iarratas na "
"bpobalbhreitheanna i ``polls``. Déanann sé an t-iarratas féinchuimsitheach "
"agus níos éasca le titim isteach i dtionscadal nua."

msgid ""
"The ``polls`` directory could now be copied into a new Django project and "
"immediately reused. It's not quite ready to be published though. For that, "
"we need to package the app to make it easy for others to install."
msgstr ""
"The ``polls`` directory could now be copied into a new Django project and "
"immediately reused. It's not quite ready to be published though. For that, "
"we need to package the app to make it easy for others to install."

msgid "Installing some prerequisites"
msgstr "Roinnt réamhriachtanais a shuiteáil"

msgid ""
"The current state of Python packaging is a bit muddled with various tools. "
"For this tutorial, we're going to use :pypi:`setuptools` to build our "
"package. It's the recommended packaging tool (merged with the ``distribute`` "
"fork). We'll also be using :pypi:`pip` to install and uninstall it. You "
"should install these two packages now. If you need help, you can refer "
"to :ref:`how to install Django with pip<installing-official-release>`. You "
"can install ``setuptools`` the same way."
msgstr ""
"Tá staid reatha pacáistiú Python beagán measctha le huirlisí éagsúla. Don "
"rang teagaisc seo, úsáidfimid :pypi:`setuptools` chun ár bpacáiste a "
"thógáil. Is é an uirlis pacáistithe molta é (cumasc leis an bhforc "
"``distribute``). Beidh :pypi:`pip` á úsáid againn freisin chun é a shuiteáil "
"agus a dhíshuiteáil. Ba cheart duit an dá phacáiste seo a shuiteáil anois. "
"Má tá cabhair uait, is féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh do :ref:`conas Django "
"a shuiteáil le pip <installing-official-release>`. Is féidir leat `` "
"setuptools`` a shuiteáil ar an mbealach céanna."

msgid "Packaging your app"
msgstr "Pacáistiú d'aip"

msgid ""
"Python *packaging* refers to preparing your app in a specific format that "
"can be easily installed and used. Django itself is packaged very much like "
"this. For a small app like polls, this process isn't too difficult."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i gceist le Python *phacáistiú* ná d’aip a ullmhú i bhformáid ar "
"leith ar féidir é a shuiteáil agus a úsáid go héasca. Tá Django féin "
"pacáistithe go mór mar seo. I gcás aip bheag cosúil le pobalbhreith, níl an "
"próiseas seo ró-dheacair."

msgid ""
"First, create a parent directory for the package, outside of your Django "
"project. Call this directory ``django-polls``."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, cruthaigh máthairchomhadlann don phacáiste, lasmuigh de do "
"thionscadal Django. Glaoigh ar an eolaire seo ``django-polls``."

msgid "Choosing a name for your app"
msgstr "Ainm a roghnú do d'fheidhmchlár"

msgid ""
"When choosing a name for your package, check PyPI to avoid naming conflicts "
"with existing packages. We recommend using a ``django-`` prefix for package "
"names, to identify your package as specific to Django, and a corresponding "
"``django_`` prefix for your module name. For example, the ``django-"
"ratelimit`` package contains the ``django_ratelimit`` module."
msgstr ""
"Agus ainm á roghnú agat do do phacáiste, seiceáil PyPI chun coinbhleachtaí "
"le pacáistí atá ann cheana a sheachaint. Molaimid réimír ``django-``  a "
"úsáid le haghaidh ainmneacha pacáiste, chun do phacáiste a aithint mar "
"phacáiste a bhaineann go sonrach le Django, agus réimír chomhfhreagrach "
"``django_`` d'ainm an mhodúil. Mar shampla, tá an modúl ``django-ratelimit`` "
"sa phacáiste ``django_ratelimit``."

msgid ""
"Application labels (that is, the final part of the dotted path to "
"application packages) *must* be unique in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. Avoid "
"using the same label as any of the Django :doc:`contrib packages </ref/"
"contrib/index>`, for example ``auth``, ``admin``, or ``messages``."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór lipéid iarratais (is é sin, an chuid deiridh den chosán poncaithe "
"chuig pacáistí iarratais) *a bheith uathúil i :setting:'INSTALLED_APPS'. "
"Seachain an lipéad céanna a úsáid le haon cheann de na pacáistí Django :d "
"oc:'contrib packages </ref/contrib/index>', mar shampla ``auth``, ``admin``, "
"nó ``messages``."

msgid ""
"Move the ``polls`` directory into ``django-polls`` directory, and rename it "
"to ``django_polls``."
msgstr ""
"Bog an t-eolaire ``polls` isteach san eolaire``django-polls`` , agus "
"athainmnigh é go``django_polls``."

msgid ""
"Edit ``django_polls/apps.py`` so that :attr:`~.AppConfig.name` refers to the "
"new module name and add :attr:`~.AppConfig.label` to give a short name for "
"the app:"
msgstr ""
"Cuir ``django_polls/apps.py`` in eagar ionas go mbeidh :attr:'~. Tagraíonn "
"AppConfig.name' d'ainm an mhodúil nua agus cuir :attr:'~. AppConfig.label' "
"chun ainm gearr a thabhairt ar an bhfeidhmchlár:"

msgid "``django-polls/django_polls/apps.py``"
msgstr "``django-polls/django_polls/apps.py``"

msgid "Create a file ``django-polls/README.rst`` with the following contents:"
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh comhad ``django-polls/README.rst`` leis an ábhar seo a leanas:"

msgid "``django-polls/README.rst``"
msgstr "``django-polls/README.rst``"

msgid ""
"Create a ``django-polls/LICENSE`` file. Choosing a license is beyond the "
"scope of this tutorial, but suffice it to say that code released publicly "
"without a license is *useless*. Django and many Django-compatible apps are "
"distributed under the BSD license; however, you're free to pick your own "
"license. Just be aware that your licensing choice will affect who is able to "
"use your code."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh comhad ``django-polls/LICENSE``. Tá roghnú ceadúnais thar raon "
"feidhme an teagaisc seo, ach is leor a rá go bhfuil an cód a scaoiltear go "
"poiblí gan cheadúnas *useless *. Django agus go leor apps Django-"
"comhoiriúnach a dháileadh faoin gceadúnas BSD; mar sin féin, tá tú saor in "
"aisce do cheadúnas féin a roghnú. Just a bheith ar an eolas go mbeidh "
"tionchar ag do rogha ceadúnaithe ar cé atá in ann do chód a úsáid."

msgid ""
"Next we'll create the ``pyproject.toml`` file which details how to build and "
"install the app. A full explanation of this file is beyond the scope of this "
"tutorial, but the `Python Packaging User Guide <https://packaging.python.org/"
"guides/writing-pyproject-toml/>`_ has a good explanation. Create the "
"``django-polls/pyproject.toml`` file with the following contents:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin cruthóimid an comhad `` pyproject.toml`` ina sonraítear conas an aip a "
"thógáil agus a shuiteáil. Tá míniú iomlán ar an gcomhad seo lasmuigh de "
"scóip an teagaisc seo, ach tá míniú maith ar an `Python Packaging User Guide "
"<https://packaging.python.org/guides/writing-pyproject-toml/>`_. Cruthaigh "
"an comhad ``django-polls/pyproject.toml`` leis an ábhar seo a leanas:"

msgid "``django-polls/pyproject.toml``"
msgstr "``django-polls/pyproject.toml``"

msgid ""
"Many common files and Python modules and packages are included in the "
"package by default. To include additional files, we'll need to create a "
"``MANIFEST.in`` file. To include the templates and static files, create a "
"file ``django-polls/MANIFEST.in`` with the following contents:"
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor comhad coitianta agus modúil agus pacáistí Python san áireamh sa "
"phacáiste de réir réamhshocraithe. Chun comhaid bhreise a chur san áireamh, "
"beidh orainn comhad ``MANIFEST.in`` a chruthú. Chun na teimpléid agus na "
"comhaid statacha a chur san áireamh, cruthaigh comhad ``django-polls/"
"MANIFEST.in`` leis an ábhar seo a leanas:"

msgid "``django-polls/MANIFEST.in``"
msgstr "``django-polls/MANIFEST.in``"

msgid ""
"It's optional, but recommended, to include detailed documentation with your "
"app. Create an empty directory ``django-polls/docs`` for future "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé roghnach, ach moltar é, doiciméid mhionsonraithe a chur san áireamh le "
"d'aip. Cruthaigh eolaire folamh ``django-polls/docs``  le haghaidh "
"doiciméadú amach anseo."

msgid ""
"Note that the ``docs`` directory won't be included in your package unless "
"you add some files to it. Many Django apps also provide their documentation "
"online through sites like `readthedocs.org <https://readthedocs.org>`_."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara nach mbeidh an t-eolaire ``docs`` san áireamh i do "
"phacáiste mura gcuireann tú roinnt comhad leis. Soláthraíonn go leor "
"aipeanna Django a ndoiciméadú ar líne freisin trí shuíomhanna mar "
"`readthedocs.org <https://readthedocs.org>`_."

msgid ""
"Many Python projects, including Django and Python itself, use `Sphinx "
"<https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/usage/quickstart.html>`_ to build "
"their documentation. If you choose to use Sphinx you can link back to the "
"Django documentation by configuring `Intersphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/"
"en/master/usage/quickstart.html#intersphinx>`_ and including a value for "
"Django in your project's ``intersphinx_mapping`` value::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With that in place, you can then cross-link to specific entries, in the same "
"way as in the Django docs, such as "
"\"``:attr:`django.test.TransactionTestCase.databases```\"."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check that the :pypi:`build` package is installed (``python -m pip install "
"build``) and try building your package by running ``python -m build`` inside "
"``django-polls``. This creates a directory called ``dist`` and builds your "
"new package into source and binary formats, ``django_polls-0.1.tar.gz`` and "
"``django_polls-0.1-py3-none-any.whl``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information on packaging, see Python's `Tutorial on Packaging and "
"Distributing Projects <https://packaging.python.org/tutorials/packaging-"
"projects/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais ar phacáistiú, féach `Tutorial on Packaging and "
"Distributing Projects <https://packaging.python.org/tutorials/packaging-"
"projects/>` le Python_."

msgid "Using your own package"
msgstr "Do phacáiste féin a úsáid"

msgid ""
"Since we moved the ``polls`` directory out of the project, it's no longer "
"working. We'll now fix this by installing our new ``django-polls`` package."
msgstr ""
"Ó bhogamar an t-eolaire ``polls`` amach as an tionscadal, níl sé ag obair a "
"thuilleadh. Déanfaimid é seo a shocrú anois trínár bpacáiste nua ``django-"
"polls`` a shuiteáil."

msgid "Installing as a user library"
msgstr "Suiteáil mar leabharlann úsáideora"

msgid ""
"The following steps install ``django-polls`` as a user library. Per-user "
"installs have a lot of advantages over installing the package system-wide, "
"such as being usable on systems where you don't have administrator access as "
"well as preventing the package from affecting system services and other "
"users of the machine."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil na céimeanna seo a leanas ``django-polls`` mar leabharlann "
"úsáideora. Tá go leor buntáistí ag suiteálacha in aghaidh an úsáideora "
"maidir leis an bpacáiste a shuiteáil ar fud an chórais, mar shampla a bheith "
"inúsáidte ar chórais nach bhfuil rochtain riarthóra agat chomh maith le cosc "
"a chur ar an bpacáiste dul i bhfeidhm ar sheirbhísí córais agus ar "
"úsáideoirí eile an mheaisín."

msgid ""
"Note that per-user installations can still affect the behavior of system "
"tools that run as that user, so using a virtual environment is a more robust "
"solution (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur féidir le suiteálacha in aghaidh an úsáideora "
"tionchar a imirt fós ar iompar uirlisí córais a ritheann mar an t-úsáideoir "
"sin, mar sin is réiteach níos láidre é timpeallacht fhíorúil a úsáid (féach "
"thíos)."

msgid ""
"To install the package, use pip (you already :ref:`installed it <installing-"
"reusable-apps-prerequisites>`, right?):"
msgstr ""
"Chun an pacáiste a shuiteáil, bain úsáid as pip (tá tú cheana féin: ref: "
"'suiteáilte sé <installing-reusable-apps-prerequisites>', ceart?):"

msgid "Update ``mysite/settings.py`` to point to the new module name::"
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraigh ``mysite/settings.py`` chun ainm an mhodúil nua a chur in iúl::"

msgid "Update ``mysite/urls.py`` to point to the new module name::"
msgstr ""
"Nuashonraigh ``mysite/urls.py`` chun ainm an mhodúil nua a chur in iúl::"

msgid "Run the development server to confirm the project continues to work."
msgstr ""
"Rith an freastalaí forbartha chun a dheimhniú go leanann an tionscadal ag "
"obair."

msgid "Publishing your app"
msgstr "D'aip a fhoilsiú"

msgid ""
"Now that we've packaged and tested ``django-polls``, it's ready to share "
"with the world! If this wasn't just an example, you could now:"
msgstr ""
"Anois agus ``django-polls`` pacáistithe agus tástáilte againn, tá sé réidh "
"le roinnt leis an domhan mór! Mura raibh anseo ach sampla, d'fhéadfá anois:"

msgid "Email the package to a friend."
msgstr "Ríomhphost an pacáiste chuig cara."

msgid "Upload the package on your website."
msgstr "Uaslódáil an pacáiste ar do láithreán gréasáin."

msgid ""
"Post the package on a public repository, such as `the Python Package Index "
"(PyPI)`_. `packaging.python.org <https://packaging.python.org>`_ has `a good "
"tutorial <https://packaging.python.org/tutorials/packaging-projects/"
"#uploading-the-distribution-archives>`_ for doing this."
msgstr ""
"Cuir an pacáiste ar stór poiblí, mar shampla `Innéacs Pacáiste Python "
"(PyPI)`_. Tá `packaging.python.org <https://packaging.python.org>`_ `a good "
"tutorial <https://packaging.python.org/tutorials/packaging-projects/"
"#uploading-the-distribution-archives>`_ chun é seo a dhéanamh."

msgid "Installing Python packages with a virtual environment"
msgstr "Pacáistí Python a shuiteáil le timpeallacht fhíorúil"

msgid ""
"Earlier, we installed ``django-polls`` as a user library. This has some "
"disadvantages:"
msgstr ""
"Níos luaithe, shuiteáil muid ``django-polls`` mar leabharlann úsáideora. Tá "
"roinnt míbhuntáistí ag baint leis seo:"

msgid ""
"Modifying the user libraries can affect other Python software on your system."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le modhnú na leabharlanna úsáideora dul i bhfeidhm ar bhogearraí "
"Python eile ar do chóras."

msgid ""
"You won't be able to run multiple versions of this package (or others with "
"the same name)."
msgstr ""
"Ní bheidh tú in ann leaganacha iolracha den phacáiste seo (nó leaganacha "
"eile leis an ainm céanna) a rith."

msgid ""
"Typically, these situations only arise once you're maintaining several "
"Django projects. When they do, the best solution is to use :doc:`venv "
"<python:tutorial/venv>`. This tool allows you to maintain multiple isolated "
"Python environments, each with its own copy of the libraries and package "
"namespace."
msgstr ""
"Go hiondúil, ní thagann na cásanna seo chun cinn ach amháin nuair a bhíonn "
"roinnt tionscadal Django á gcothabháil agat. Nuair a dhéanann siad, is é an "
"réiteach is fearr ná :doc:`venv <python:tutorial/venv>` a úsáid. Ligeann an "
"uirlis seo duit timpeallachtaí iomadúla iargúlta Python a chothabháil, gach "
"ceann acu lena chóip féin de na leabharlanna agus ainmspás an phacáiste."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 1"
msgstr "Scríobh do chéad aip Django, cuid 1"

msgid "Let's learn by example."
msgstr "Foghlaimímis trí shampla."

msgid ""
"Throughout this tutorial, we'll walk you through the creation of a basic "
"poll application."
msgstr ""
"Le linn an teagaisc seo, beimid ag siúl leat trí bhunfheidhmchlár vótaíochta "
"a chruthú."

msgid "It'll consist of two parts:"
msgstr "Beidh dhá chuid ann:"

msgid "A public site that lets people view polls and vote in them."
msgstr ""
"Suíomh poiblí a ligeann do dhaoine féachaint ar na pobalbhreitheanna agus "
"vótáil iontu."

msgid "An admin site that lets you add, change, and delete polls."
msgstr ""
"Suíomh riaracháin a ligeann duit pobalbhreitheanna a chur leis, a athrú agus "
"a scriosadh."

msgid ""
"We'll assume you have :doc:`Django installed </intro/install>` already. You "
"can tell Django is installed and which version by running the following "
"command in a shell prompt (indicated by the $ prefix):"
msgstr ""
"Glacfaimid leis go bhfuil :d oc: `Django suiteáilte </intro/install>` agat "
"cheana féin. Is féidir leat a rá go bhfuil Django suiteáilte agus cén leagan "
"tríd an ordú seo a leanas a rith i leid bhlaosc (arna léiriú ag an réimír $):"

msgid ""
"If Django is installed, you should see the version of your installation. If "
"it isn't, you'll get an error telling \"No module named django\"."
msgstr ""
"Má tá Django suiteáilte, ba chóir duit an leagan de do shuiteáil a "
"fheiceáil. Mura bhfuil, gheobhaidh tú earráid ag insint \"Níl modúl darb "
"ainm django\"."

msgid ""
"This tutorial is written for Django |version|, which supports Python 3.10 "
"and later. If the Django version doesn't match, you can refer to the "
"tutorial for your version of Django by using the version switcher at the "
"bottom right corner of this page, or update Django to the newest version. If "
"you're using an older version of Python, check :ref:`faq-python-version-"
"support` to find a compatible version of Django."
msgstr ""
"Scríobhtar an rang teagaisc seo do Django |leagan|, a thacaíonn le Python "
"3.10 agus níos déanaí. Mura bhfuil an leagan Django comhoiriúnach, is féidir "
"leat tagairt a dhéanamh don rang teagaisc do do leagan de Django trí úsáid a "
"bhaint as an switcher leagan ag bun an chúinne ar dheis den leathanach seo, "
"nó Django a nuashonrú go dtí an leagan is nua. Má tá leagan níos sine de "
"Python á úsáid agat, seiceáil :ref:'faq-python-version-support' chun leagan "
"comhoiriúnach de Django a aimsiú."

msgid ""
"If you're having trouble going through this tutorial, please head over to "
"the :doc:`Getting Help</faq/help>` section of the FAQ."
msgstr ""
"Má tá deacracht agat dul tríd an rang teagaisc seo, téigh ar aghaidh chuig "
"an rannán :d oc:'Getting Help</faq/help>' den rannán Ceisteanna Coitianta."

msgid "Creating a project"
msgstr "Tionscadal a chruthú"

msgid ""
"If this is your first time using Django, you'll have to take care of some "
"initial setup. Namely, you'll need to auto-generate some code that "
"establishes a Django :term:`project` -- a collection of settings for an "
"instance of Django, including database configuration, Django-specific "
"options and application-specific settings."
msgstr ""
"Más é seo do chéad uair ag baint úsáide as Django, beidh ort aire a "
"thabhairt do roinnt thus tosaigh. Eadhon, beidh ort roinnt cód a ghiniúint "
"go huathoibríoch a bhunaíonn Django: téarma: 'tionscadal' - bailiúchán "
"socruithe le haghaidh sampla de Django, lena n-áirítear cumraíocht bunachar "
"sonraí, roghanna Django-sonrach agus socruithe a bhaineann go sonrach le "
"feidhmchlár."

msgid ""
"From the command line, ``cd`` into a directory where you'd like to store "
"your code and create a new directory named ``djangotutorial``. (This "
"directory name doesn't matter to Django; you can rename it to anything you "
"like.)"
msgstr ""
"Ó líne na n-orduithe, ``cd`` isteach i gcomhadlann inar mhaith leat do chód "
"a stóráil agus eolaire nua a chruthú darb ainm ``djangotutorial``. (Ní "
"bhaineann an t-ainm eolaire seo le Django; is féidir leat é a athainmniú "
"chuig aon rud is mian leat.)"

msgid "Then, run the following command to bootstrap a new Django project:"
msgstr "Ansin, rith an t-ordú seo a leanas chun tionscadal nua Django a thosú:"

msgid ""
"This will create a project called ``mysite`` inside the ``djangotutorial`` "
"directory. If it didn't work, see :ref:`troubleshooting-django-admin`."
msgstr ""
"Cruthóidh sé seo tionscadal ar a dtugtar ``mysite`` taobh istigh den eolaire "
"``djangotutorial``. Mura n-oibríonn sé, féach :ref:'troubleshooting-django-"
"admin'."

msgid ""
"You'll need to avoid naming projects after built-in Python or Django "
"components. In particular, this means you should avoid using names like "
"``django`` (which will conflict with Django itself) or ``test`` (which "
"conflicts with a built-in Python package)."
msgstr ""
"Beidh ort tionscadail a ainmniú tar éis comhpháirteanna Python nó Django "
"tógtha isteach. Go háirithe, ciallaíonn sé seo gur chóir duit ainmneacha mar "
"``django`` (a thiocfaidh salach ar Django féin) nó ``test`` (a thagann "
"salach ar phacáiste Python ionsuite) a sheachaint."

msgid "Let's look at what :djadmin:`startproject` created:"
msgstr "Breathnaímis ar an méid a chruthaigh :d jadmin:'startproject':"

msgid "These files are:"
msgstr "Is iad seo a leanas na comhaid seo:"

msgid ""
":file:`manage.py`: A command-line utility that lets you interact with this "
"Django project in various ways. You can read all the details "
"about :file:`manage.py` in :doc:`/ref/django-admin`."
msgstr ""
":file:'manage.py': Fóntais líne na n-orduithe a ligeann duit idirghníomhú "
"leis an tionscadal Django seo ar bhealaí éagsúla. Is féidir leat na sonraí "
"go léir faoi :file:'manage.py' a léamh in :d oc:'/ref/django-admin'."

msgid ""
":file:`mysite/`: A directory that is the actual Python package for your "
"project. Its name is the Python package name you'll need to use to import "
"anything inside it (e.g. ``mysite.urls``)."
msgstr ""
":comhad:`mysite/`: Eolaire arb é an pacáiste Python iarbhír do do "
"thionscadal. Is é an t-ainm an t-ainm pacáiste Python a chaithfidh tú a "
"úsáid chun aon rud a allmhairiú laistigh de (m.sh. ``mysite.urls``)."

msgid ""
":file:`mysite/__init__.py`: An empty file that tells Python that this "
"directory should be considered a Python package. If you're a Python "
"beginner, read :ref:`more about packages <tut-packages>` in the official "
"Python docs."
msgstr ""
":file:`mysite/__init__.py`: Comhad folamh a insíonn do Python gur chóir an t-"
"eolaire seo a mheas mar phacáiste Python. Más tosaitheoir Python tú, "
"léigh :ref:'more about packages<tut-packages>' sna docs oifigiúla Python."

msgid ""
":file:`mysite/settings.py`: Settings/configuration for this Django "
"project.  :doc:`/topics/settings` will tell you all about how settings work."
msgstr ""
":file:'mysite/settings.py': Socruithe/cumraíocht don tionscadal Django "
"seo.  :d OC:Inseoidh '/topics/settings' duit faoin gcaoi a n-oibríonn "
"socruithe."

msgid ""
":file:`mysite/urls.py`: The URL declarations for this Django project; a "
"\"table of contents\" of your Django-powered site. You can read more about "
"URLs in :doc:`/topics/http/urls`."
msgstr ""
":file:'mysite/urls.py': Na dearbhuithe URL don tionscadal Django seo; \"clár "
"ábhair\" de do shuíomh faoi thiomáint Django. Is féidir leat tuilleadh a "
"léamh faoi URLanna in :d oc:'/topics/http/urls'."

msgid ""
":file:`mysite/asgi.py`: An entry-point for ASGI-compatible web servers to "
"serve your project. See :doc:`/howto/deployment/asgi/index` for more details."
msgstr ""
":file:`mysite/asgi.py`: Pointe iontrála do fhreastalaithe gréasáin atá "
"comhoiriúnach le ASGI chun freastal ar do thionscadal. Féach :d oc:`/howto/"
"deployment/asgi/index` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid ""
":file:`mysite/wsgi.py`: An entry-point for WSGI-compatible web servers to "
"serve your project. See :doc:`/howto/deployment/wsgi/index` for more details."
msgstr ""
":file:`mysite/wsgi.py`: : Pointe iontrála le haghaidh freastalaithe gréasáin "
"atá comhoiriúnach le WSGI chun freastal ar do thionscadal. Féach :doc:`/"
"howto/deployment/wsgi/index` le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí."

msgid "The development server"
msgstr "An freastalaí forbartha"

msgid ""
"Let's verify your Django project works. Change into "
"the :file:`djangotutorial` directory, if you haven't already, and run the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""
"A ligean ar fhíorú do oibreacha tionscadal Django. Athraigh isteach sa "
"chomhad:`djangotutorial` eolaire, mura bhfuil tú cheana féin, agus rith na "
"horduithe seo a leanas:"

msgid "You'll see the following output on the command line:"
msgstr "Feicfidh tú an t-aschur seo a leanas ar an líne ordaithe:"

msgid ""
"Ignore the warning about unapplied database migrations for now; we'll deal "
"with the database shortly."
msgstr ""
"Déan neamhaird den rabhadh faoi imirce bunachar sonraí neamhfheidhmithe "
"anois; Déileálfaimid leis an mbunachar sonraí go luath."

msgid ""
"Now that the server's running, visit http://127.0.0.1:8000/ with your web "
"browser. You'll see a \"Congratulations!\" page, with a rocket taking off. "
"It worked!"
msgstr ""
"Anois go bhfuil an freastalaí ag rith, tabhair cuairt http://127.0.0.1:8000/ "
"le do bhrabhsálaí gréasáin. Feicfidh tú \"Comhghairdeas!\" leathanach, le "
"roicéad ag éirí as. D'oibrigh sé!"

msgid ""
"You've started the Django development server, a lightweight web server "
"written purely in Python. We've included this with Django so you can develop "
"things rapidly, without having to deal with configuring a production server "
"-- such as Apache -- until you're ready for production."
msgstr ""
"Thosaigh tú an freastalaí forbartha Django, freastalaí gréasáin éadrom "
"scríofa i Python amháin. Táimid tar éis é seo a chur san áireamh le Django "
"ionas gur féidir leat rudaí a fhorbairt go tapa, gan déileáil le freastalaí "
"táirgeachta a chumrú - mar shampla Apache - go dtí go mbeidh tú réidh le "
"táirgeadh."

msgid ""
"Now's a good time to note: **don't** use this server in anything resembling "
"a production environment. It's intended only for use while developing. "
"(We're in the business of making web frameworks, not web servers.)"
msgstr ""
"Is dea-am é anois le tabhairt faoi deara: **ná** úsáid an freastalaí seo in "
"aon rud atá cosúil le timpeallacht táirgthe. Níl sé beartaithe ach le húsáid "
"agus é ag forbairt. (Táimid i mbun creataí gréasáin a dhéanamh, ní "
"freastalaithe gréasáin.)"

msgid ""
"(To serve the site on a different port, see the :djadmin:`runserver` "
"reference.)"
msgstr ""
"(Chun freastal ar an suíomh ar phort eile, féach an tagairt :d "
"jadmin:`runserver`.)"

msgid "Automatic reloading of :djadmin:`runserver`"
msgstr "Athluchtú uathoibríoch :d jadmin: 'runserver'"

msgid ""
"The development server automatically reloads Python code for each request as "
"needed. You don't need to restart the server for code changes to take "
"effect. However, some actions like adding files don't trigger a restart, so "
"you'll have to restart the server in these cases."
msgstr ""
"Athluchtaíonn an freastalaí forbartha cód Python go huathoibríoch do gach "
"iarratas de réir mar is gá. Ní gá duit an freastalaí a atosú chun athruithe "
"cóid a chur i bhfeidhm. Mar sin féin, ní spreagann roinnt gníomhartha cosúil "
"le comhaid a chur leis atosú, mar sin beidh ort an freastalaí a atosú sna "
"cásanna seo."

msgid "Creating the Polls app"
msgstr "Cruthú an aip vótaíochta"

msgid ""
"Now that your environment -- a \"project\" -- is set up, you're set to start "
"doing work."
msgstr ""
"Anois go bhfuil do thimpeallacht -- \"tionscadal\" -- ar bun, tá tú ar tí "
"tosú ag déanamh oibre."

msgid ""
"Each application you write in Django consists of a Python package that "
"follows a certain convention. Django comes with a utility that automatically "
"generates the basic directory structure of an app, so you can focus on "
"writing code rather than creating directories."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i ngach feidhmchlár a scríobhann tú i Django pacáiste Python a "
"leanann coinbhinsiún áirithe. Tagann Django le fóntais a ghineann struchtúr "
"bunúsach eolaire app go huathoibríoch, ionas gur féidir leat díriú ar chód "
"scríbhneoireachta seachas eolairí a chruthú."

msgid "Projects vs. apps"
msgstr "Tionscadail vs apps"

msgid ""
"What's the difference between a project and an app? An app is a web "
"application that does something -- e.g., a blog system, a database of public "
"records or a small poll app. A project is a collection of configuration and "
"apps for a particular website. A project can contain multiple apps. An app "
"can be in multiple projects."
msgstr ""
"Cad é an difríocht idir tionscadal agus aip? Is feidhmchlár gréasáin é aip a "
"dhéanann rud éigin -- m.sh., córas blag, bunachar sonraí de thaifid phoiblí "
"nó aip bheag vótaíochta. Is éard is tionscadal ann ná bailiúchán cumraíochta "
"agus feidhmchlár do shuíomh gréasáin ar leith. Is féidir aipeanna éagsúla a "
"bheith i dtionscadal. Is féidir le app a bheith i dtionscadail éagsúla."

msgid ""
"Your apps can live anywhere in your :ref:`Python path <tut-searchpath>`. In "
"this tutorial, we'll create our poll app inside the ``djangotutorial`` "
"folder."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir le d’aipeanna maireachtáil áit ar bith i do :ref:`Python path <tut-"
"searchpath>`. Sa rang teagaisc seo, cruthóimid ár n-aip vótaíochta laistigh "
"den fhillteán ``djangotutorial``."

msgid ""
"To create your app, make sure you're in the same directory "
"as :file:`manage.py` and type this command:"
msgstr ""
"Chun d'aip a chruthú, cinntigh go bhfuil tú san eolaire céanna "
"le :file:`manage.py` agus clóscríobh an t-ordú seo:"

msgid "That'll create a directory :file:`polls`, which is laid out like this:"
msgstr "Cruthóidh sé sin eolaire :file:`polls`, atá leagtha amach mar seo:"

msgid "This directory structure will house the poll application."
msgstr "Beidh an feidhmchlár vótaíochta sa struchtúr eolaire seo."

msgid "Write your first view"
msgstr "Scríobh do chéad amharc"

msgid ""
"Let's write the first view. Open the file ``polls/views.py`` and put the "
"following Python code in it:"
msgstr ""
"Scríobhaimis an chéad amharc. Oscail an comhad ``polls/views.py`` agus cuir "
"an cód Python seo a leanas ann:"

msgid "``polls/views.py``"
msgstr "``polls/views.py``"

msgid ""
"This is the most basic view possible in Django. To access it in a browser, "
"we need to map it to a URL - and for this we need to define a URL "
"configuration, or \"URLconf\" for short. These URL configurations are "
"defined inside each Django app, and they are Python files named ``urls.py``."
msgstr ""
"Is é seo an dearcadh is bunúsaí is féidir i Django. Chun rochtain a fháil "
"air i mbrabhsálaí, ní mór dúinn é a mhapáil chuig URL - agus chuige seo ní "
"mór dúinn cumraíocht URL, nó \"URLconf\" a shainiú go gairid. Sainmhínítear "
"na cumraíochtaí URL seo taobh istigh de gach feidhmchlár Django, agus is "
"comhaid Python iad darb ainm ``urls.py``."

msgid ""
"To define a URLconf for the ``polls`` app, create a file ``polls/urls.py`` "
"with the following content:"
msgstr ""
"Chun URLconf a shainmhíniú don aip ``polls``, cruthaigh comhad ``polls/"
"urls.py`` leis an ábhar seo a leanas:"

msgid "``polls/urls.py``"
msgstr "``polls/urls.py``"

msgid "Your app directory should now look like:"
msgstr "Ba cheart go mbeadh cuma ar do eolaire feidhmchlár anois:"

msgid ""
"The next step is to configure the root URLconf in the ``mysite`` project to "
"include the URLconf defined in ``polls.urls``. To do this, add an import for "
"``django.urls.include`` in ``mysite/urls.py`` and insert "
"an :func:`~django.urls.include` in the ``urlpatterns`` list, so you have:"
msgstr ""

msgid "``mysite/urls.py``"
msgstr "``mysite/urls.py``"

msgid ""
"The :func:`~django.urls.path` function expects at least two arguments: "
"``route`` and ``view``. The :func:`~django.urls.include` function allows "
"referencing other URLconfs. Whenever Django "
"encounters :func:`~django.urls.include`, it chops off whatever part of the "
"URL matched up to that point and sends the remaining string to the included "
"URLconf for further processing."
msgstr ""
"The :func:`~django.urls.path` function expects at least two arguments: "
"``route`` and ``view``. The :func:`~django.urls.include` function allows "
"referencing other URLconfs. Whenever Django "
"encounters :func:`~django.urls.include`, it chops off whatever part of the "
"URL matched up to that point and sends the remaining string to the included "
"URLconf for further processing."

msgid ""
"The idea behind :func:`~django.urls.include` is to make it easy to plug-and-"
"play URLs. Since polls are in their own URLconf (``polls/urls.py``), they "
"can be placed under \"/polls/\", or under \"/fun_polls/\", or under \"/"
"content/polls/\", or any other path root, and the app will still work."
msgstr ""
"Is é an smaoineamh taobh thiar de :func:`~django.urls.include` é a dhéanamh "
"éasca URLanna plug-and-play. Ós rud é go bhfuil pobalbhreith ina URLconf "
"féin (`` pobalbhreith/urls.py``), is féidir iad a chur faoi \"/polls/\", nó "
"faoi \"/fun_polls/\", nó faoi \"/content/polls/\", nó aon fréimhe cosán "
"eile, agus beidh an app fós ag obair."

msgid "When to use :func:`~django.urls.include()`"
msgstr "Nuair a úsáid: func: '~ django.urls.include ()'"

msgid ""
"You should always use ``include()`` when you include other URL patterns. The "
"only exception is ``admin.site.urls``, which is a pre-built URLconf provided "
"by Django for the default admin site."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir duit ``include()`` a úsáid i gcónaí nuair a chuireann tú patrúin "
"URL eile san áireamh. Is é an t-aon eisceacht ná ``admin.site.urls``, ar "
"URLconf réamhthógtha é a sholáthraíonn Django don suíomh riaracháin "
"réamhshocraithe."

msgid ""
"You have now wired an ``index`` view into the URLconf. Verify it's working "
"with the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Tá amharc ``index`` sreangaithe agat anois sa URLconf. Fíoraigh go bhfuil sé "
"ag obair leis an ordú seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Go to http://localhost:8000/polls/ in your browser, and you should see the "
"text \"*Hello, world. You're at the polls index.*\", which you defined in "
"the ``index`` view."
msgstr ""
"Téigh go http://localhost:8000/polls/ i do bhrabhsálaí, agus ba cheart duit "
"an téacs \"*Dia duit, world. Tá tú ag an innéacs pobalbhreithe.*\" a "
"fheiceáil, a shainigh tú sa radharc ``innéacs`` ."

msgid "Page not found?"
msgstr "Ní bhfuarthas an leathanach?"

msgid ""
"If you get an error page here, check that you're going to http://"
"localhost:8000/polls/ and not http://localhost:8000/."
msgstr ""
"Má fhaigheann tú leathanach earráide anseo, seiceáil go bhfuil tú ag dul "
"chuig http://localhost:8000/polls/ agus ní http://localhost:8000/."

msgid ""
"When you're comfortable with the basic request and response flow, "
"read :doc:`part 2 of this tutorial </intro/tutorial02>` to start working "
"with the database."
msgstr ""
"Nuair atá tú compordach leis an mbunsreabhadh iarratais agus freagartha, "
"léigh :doc:`cuid 2 den rang teagaisc seo </intro/tutorial02>` chun tosú ag "
"obair leis an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 2"
msgstr "Scríobh do chéad aip Django, cuid 2"

msgid ""
"This tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 1 </intro/tutorial01>` left off. "
"We'll set up the database, create your first model, and get a quick "
"introduction to Django's automatically-generated admin site."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an rang teagaisc seo nuair a d'fhág :d oc:`Tutorial 1 </intro/"
"tutorial01>`. Cuirfimid an bunachar sonraí ar bun, cruthóimid do chéad "
"mhúnla, agus cuirfimid réamhrá tapa ar shuíomh riaracháin Django a ghintear "
"go huathoibríoch."

msgid "Database setup"
msgstr "Socrú bunachar sonraí"

msgid ""
"Now, open up :file:`mysite/settings.py`. It's a normal Python module with "
"module-level variables representing Django settings."
msgstr ""
"Anois, oscail suas :file:`mysite/settings.py`. Is gnáth-mhodúl Python é le "
"hathróga ar leibhéal an mhodúil a léiríonn suíomhanna Django."

msgid ""
"By default, the :setting:`DATABASES` configuration uses SQLite. If you're "
"new to databases, or you're just interested in trying Django, this is the "
"easiest choice. SQLite is included in Python, so you won't need to install "
"anything else to support your database. When starting your first real "
"project, however, you may want to use a more scalable database like "
"PostgreSQL, to avoid database-switching headaches down the road."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáideann an chumraíocht :setting:`DATABASES` "
"SQLite. Más rud é go bhfuil bunachair shonraí nua agat, nó mura bhfuil suim "
"agat ach Django a thriail, is é seo an rogha is éasca. Tá SQLite san áireamh "
"i Python, mar sin ní bheidh ort aon rud eile a shuiteáil chun tacú le do "
"bhunachar sonraí. Agus do chéad tionscadal fíor á thosú, áfach, b'fhéidir "
"gur mhaith leat úsáid a bhaint as bunachar sonraí níos inscálaithe cosúil le "
"PostgreSQL, chun tinneas cinn a bhaineann le hathrú bunachar sonraí a "
"sheachaint."

msgid ""
"If you wish to use another database, see :ref:`details to customize and get "
"your database running <database-installation>`."
msgstr ""
"Más mian leat bunachar sonraí eile a úsáid, féach :ref:`mionsonraí chun do "
"bhunachar sonraí a shaincheapadh agus a chur ar siúl <database-"
"installation>`."

msgid ""
"While you're editing :file:`mysite/settings.py`, set :setting:`TIME_ZONE` to "
"your time zone."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ag eagarthóireacht :comhad: `mysite/settings.py`, "
"socraigh :setting:`TIME_ZONE` chuig do chrios ama."

msgid ""
"Also, note the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting at the top of the file. "
"That holds the names of all Django applications that are activated in this "
"Django instance. Apps can be used in multiple projects, and you can package "
"and distribute them for use by others in their projects."
msgstr ""
"Chomh maith leis sin, tabhair faoi deara an socrú :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"ag barr an chomhaid. Coinníonn sé sin ainmneacha na bhfeidhmchlár Django go "
"léir atá i ngníomh sa chás Django seo. Is féidir feidhmchláir a úsáid i "
"dtionscadail iolracha, agus is féidir leat iad a phacáistiú agus a dháileadh "
"lena n-úsáid ag daoine eile ina dtionscadail."

msgid ""
"By default, :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` contains the following apps, all of "
"which come with Django:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, : socrú: tá na haipeanna seo a leanas i "
"`INSTALLED_APPS`, agus tagann gach ceann díobh le Django:"

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.admin` -- The admin site. You'll use it shortly."
msgstr ""
":mod:`django.contrib.admin` -- An suíomh riaracháin. Bainfidh tú úsáid as "
"gan mhoill."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.auth` -- An authentication system."
msgstr ":mod:`django.contrib.auth` -- Córas fíordheimhnithe."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.contenttypes` -- A framework for content types."
msgstr ""
":mod:`django.contrib.contenttypes` -- Creat le haghaidh cineálacha ábhair."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.sessions` -- A session framework."
msgstr ":mod:'django.contrib.sessions' -- Creat seisiúin."

msgid ":mod:`django.contrib.messages` -- A messaging framework."
msgstr ":mod:'django.contrib.messages' -- Creat teachtaireachtaí."

msgid ""
":mod:`django.contrib.staticfiles` -- A framework for managing static files."
msgstr ""
":mod:'django.contrib.staticfiles' -- Creat chun comhaid statacha a "
"bhainistiú."

msgid ""
"These applications are included by default as a convenience for the common "
"case."
msgstr ""
"These applications are included by default as a convenience for the common "
"case."

msgid ""
"Some of these applications make use of at least one database table, though, "
"so we need to create the tables in the database before we can use them. To "
"do that, run the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Baineann cuid de na feidhmchláir seo úsáid as tábla bunachar sonraí amháin "
"ar a laghad, áfach, mar sin ní mór dúinn na táblaí a chruthú sa bhunachar "
"sonraí sular féidir linn iad a úsáid. Chun é sin a dhéanamh, rith an t-ordú "
"seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`migrate` command looks at the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"setting and creates any necessary database tables according to the database "
"settings in your :file:`mysite/settings.py` file and the database migrations "
"shipped with the app (we'll cover those later). You'll see a message for "
"each migration it applies. If you're interested, run the command-line client "
"for your database and type ``\\dt`` (PostgreSQL), ``SHOW TABLES;`` (MariaDB, "
"MySQL), ``.tables`` (SQLite), or ``SELECT TABLE_NAME FROM USER_TABLES;`` "
"(Oracle) to display the tables Django created."
msgstr ""
"The :djadmin:`migrate` command looks at the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` "
"setting and creates any necessary database tables according to the database "
"settings in your :file:`mysite/settings.py` file and the database migrations "
"shipped with the app (we'll cover those later). You'll see a message for "
"each migration it applies. If you're interested, run the command-line client "
"for your database and type ``\\dt`` (PostgreSQL), ``SHOW TABLES;`` (MariaDB, "
"MySQL), ``.tables`` (SQLite), or ``SELECT TABLE_NAME FROM USER_TABLES;`` "
"(Oracle) to display the tables Django created."

msgid "For the minimalists"
msgstr "Do na íostach"

msgid ""
"Like we said above, the default applications are included for the common "
"case, but not everybody needs them. If you don't need any or all of them, "
"feel free to comment-out or delete the appropriate line(s) "
"from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` before running :djadmin:`migrate`. "
"The :djadmin:`migrate` command will only run migrations for apps "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""
"Like we said above, the default applications are included for the common "
"case, but not everybody needs them. If you don't need any or all of them, "
"feel free to comment-out or delete the appropriate line(s) "
"from :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` before running :djadmin:`migrate`. "
"The :djadmin:`migrate` command will only run migrations for apps "
"in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."

msgid "Creating models"
msgstr "Samhlacha a chruthú"

msgid ""
"Now we'll define your models -- essentially, your database layout, with "
"additional metadata."
msgstr ""
"Anois déanfaimid do mhúnlaí a shainiú - go bunúsach, do leagan amach "
"bunachar sonraí, le meiteashonraí breise."

msgid "Philosophy"
msgstr "Fealsúnacht"

msgid ""
"A model is the single, definitive source of information about your data. It "
"contains the essential fields and behaviors of the data you're storing. "
"Django follows the :ref:`DRY Principle <dry>`. The goal is to define your "
"data model in one place and automatically derive things from it."
msgstr ""
"Is éard is samhail ann ná an fhoinse amháin, deifnídeach faisnéise faoi do "
"shonraí. Cuimsíonn sé na réimsí riachtanacha agus iompraíochtaí na sonraí "
"atá á stóráil agat. Leanann Django an :ref:`TIRIM Prionsabal <dry>`. Is é an "
"sprioc ná do mhúnla sonraí a shainiú in aon áit amháin agus rudaí a dhíorthú "
"go huathoibríoch uaidh."

msgid ""
"This includes the migrations - unlike in Ruby On Rails, for example, "
"migrations are entirely derived from your models file, and are essentially a "
"history that Django can roll through to update your database schema to match "
"your current models."
msgstr ""
"Áiríonn sé seo na haistrithe - murab ionann agus Ruby On Rails, mar shampla, "
"díorthaítear ascnaimh go hiomlán ó do chomhad samhlacha, agus go bunúsach is "
"stair iad ar féidir le Django rolladh tríd chun scéimre do bhunachar sonraí "
"a nuashonrú chun do mhúnlaí reatha a mheaitseáil."

msgid ""
"In our poll app, we'll create two models: ``Question`` and ``Choice``. A "
"``Question`` has a question and a publication date. A ``Choice`` has two "
"fields: the text of the choice and a vote tally. Each ``Choice`` is "
"associated with a ``Question``."
msgstr ""
"In ár app vótaíochta, cruthóimid dhá mhúnla: `` Ceist`` agus `` Rogha``. Tá "
"ceist agus dáta foilsithe ag ``Ceist``. Tá dhá réimse ag ``Choice``: téacs "
"na rogha agus scóir vóta. Baineann gach ``Rogha`` le ``Ceist``."

msgid ""
"These concepts are represented by Python classes. Edit the :file:`polls/"
"models.py` file so it looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Déanann ranganna Python ionadaíocht ar na coincheapa seo. Cuir an "
"comhad :comhad:`polls/models.py` in eagar ionas go mbeidh cuma air seo:"

msgid "``polls/models.py``"
msgstr "``polls/models.py``"

msgid ""
"Here, each model is represented by a class that "
"subclasses :class:`django.db.models.Model`. Each model has a number of class "
"variables, each of which represents a database field in the model."
msgstr ""
"Anseo, déantar ionadaíocht ar gach samhail ag aicme a fho-aicmí :aicme: "
"`django.db.models.Model`. Tá roinnt athróg ranga ag gach samhail, agus "
"léiríonn gach ceann acu réimse bunachar sonraí sa tsamhail."

msgid ""
"Each field is represented by an instance of "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.Field` class -- "
"e.g., :class:`~django.db.models.CharField` for character fields "
"and :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` for datetimes. This tells "
"Django what type of data each field holds."
msgstr ""
"Léirítear gach réimse ag sampla de :aicme:`~django.db.models.Réimse` rang -- "
"m.sh., :aicme:`~django.db.models.CharField` le haghaidh réimsí carachtar "
"agus :aicme:`~ django .db.models.DateTimeField` le haghaidh amanna dáta. "
"Insíonn sé seo do Django cén cineál sonraí atá i seilbh gach réimse."

msgid ""
"The name of each :class:`~django.db.models.Field` instance (e.g. "
"``question_text`` or ``pub_date``) is the field's name, in machine-friendly "
"format. You'll use this value in your Python code, and your database will "
"use it as the column name."
msgstr ""
"Is é ainm gach :aicme:`~django.db.models.Field` shampla (m.sh. "
"``question_text`` nó `` pub_date``) ainm an réimse, i bhformáid meaisín-"
"chairdiúil. Úsáidfidh tú an luach seo i do chód Python, agus úsáidfidh do "
"bhunachar sonraí é mar ainm an cholúin."

msgid ""
"You can use an optional first positional argument to "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.Field` to designate a human-readable name. "
"That's used in a couple of introspective parts of Django, and it doubles as "
"documentation. If this field isn't provided, Django will use the machine-"
"readable name. In this example, we've only defined a human-readable name for "
"``Question.pub_date``. For all other fields in this model, the field's "
"machine-readable name will suffice as its human-readable name."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat an chéad argóint suímh roghnach a úsáid "
"chuig:rang:`~django.db.models.Field` chun ainm atá inléite ag an duine a "
"ainmniú. Úsáidtear é sin i gcúpla cuid introspective de Django, agus déantar "
"é a dhúbailt mar dhoiciméadú. Mura soláthraítear an réimse seo, úsáidfidh "
"Django an t-ainm meaisín-inléite. Sa sampla seo, níl ach ainm inléite daonna "
"sainmhínithe againn do ``Question.pub_date``. I gcás gach réimse eile sa "
"mhúnla seo, is leor ainm meaisín-inléite na páirce mar a ainm inléite ag an "
"duine."

msgid ""
"Some :class:`~django.db.models.Field` classes have required "
"arguments. :class:`~django.db.models.CharField`, for example, requires that "
"you give it a :attr:`~django.db.models.CharField.max_length`. That's used "
"not only in the database schema, but in validation, as we'll soon see."
msgstr ""
"Bhí argóintí ag teastáil ó roinnt "
"ranganna :rang:`~django.db.models.Field`. :rang:`~django.db.models.CharField`, "
"mar shampla, éilíonn tú :attr:`~django.db.models.CharField.max_length` a "
"thabhairt dó. Úsáidtear é sin ní hamháin sa scéimre bunachar sonraí, ach i "
"mbailíochtú, mar a fheicfimid go luath."

msgid ""
"A :class:`~django.db.models.Field` can also have various optional arguments; "
"in this case, we've set the :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default` value of "
"``votes`` to 0."
msgstr ""
"A :class:`~django.db.models.Field` can also have various optional arguments; "
"in this case, we've set the :attr:`~django.db.models.Field.default` value of "
"``votes`` to 0."

msgid ""
"Finally, note a relationship is defined, "
"using :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`. That tells Django each "
"``Choice`` is related to a single ``Question``. Django supports all the "
"common database relationships: many-to-one, many-to-many, and one-to-one."
msgstr ""
"Ar deireadh, tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil gaol sainithe, ag baint úsáide "
"as :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey`. Deir sé sin le Django go bhfuil "
"gach ``Rogha`` gaolmhar le ``Ceist`` amháin. Tacaíonn Django leis na "
"caidrimh bhunachar sonraí coitianta go léir: go leor le duine, go leor le go "
"leor, agus duine le duine."

msgid "Activating models"
msgstr "Samhlacha a ghníomhachtú"

msgid ""
"That small bit of model code gives Django a lot of information. With it, "
"Django is able to:"
msgstr ""
"Tugann an cód múnla beag sin go leor faisnéise do Django. Leis, tá Django in "
"ann:"

msgid "Create a database schema (``CREATE TABLE`` statements) for this app."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh scéimre bunachar sonraí (ráitis ``CREATE TABLE``) don aip seo."

msgid ""
"Create a Python database-access API for accessing ``Question`` and "
"``Choice`` objects."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh API le rochtain ar bhunachar sonraí Python chun réada ``Ceist`` "
"agus ``Choice`` a rochtain."

msgid ""
"But first we need to tell our project that the ``polls`` app is installed."
msgstr ""
"Ach ar dtús ní mór dúinn a rá lenár dtionscadal go bhfuil an aip "
"``vótaíochta`` suiteáilte."

msgid ""
"Django apps are \"pluggable\": You can use an app in multiple projects, and "
"you can distribute apps, because they don't have to be tied to a given "
"Django installation."
msgstr ""
"Tá aipeanna Django “in-phlugtha”: Is féidir leat aip a úsáid i dtionscadail "
"iolracha, agus is féidir leat aipeanna a dháileadh, toisc nach gá iad a "
"bheith ceangailte le suiteáil Django ar leith."

msgid ""
"To include the app in our project, we need to add a reference to its "
"configuration class in the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting. The "
"``PollsConfig`` class is in the :file:`polls/apps.py` file, so its dotted "
"path is ``'polls.apps.PollsConfig'``. Edit the :file:`mysite/settings.py` "
"file and add that dotted path to the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting. "
"It'll look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Chun an aip a chur san áireamh inár dtionscadal, ní mór dúinn tagairt a "
"dhéanamh dá rang cumraíochta sa socrú :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`. Tá an rang "
"``PollsConfig`` sa chomhad :comhad:`vótaíocht/apps.py`, mar sin is é an "
"cosán poncaithe atá aige ná ``` pobalbhreith.apps.PollsConfig``. Cuir an "
"comhad :comhad:`mysite/settings.py` in eagar agus cuir an cosán poncaithe "
"sin leis an socrú ::`INSTALLED_APPS`. Beidh sé cuma mar seo:"

msgid "``mysite/settings.py``"
msgstr "``mysite/settings.py``"

msgid ""
"Now Django knows to include the ``polls`` app. Let's run another command:"
msgstr ""
"Anois tá a fhios ag Django an aip `toghcháin`` a chur san áireamh. Rithfimid "
"ordú eile:"

msgid "You should see something similar to the following:"
msgstr "Ba cheart duit rud éigin cosúil leis an méid seo a leanas a fheiceáil:"

msgid ""
"By running ``makemigrations``, you're telling Django that you've made some "
"changes to your models (in this case, you've made new ones) and that you'd "
"like the changes to be stored as a *migration*."
msgstr ""
"Trí ``makemigrations`` a rith, tá tú ag insint do Django go bhfuil roinnt "
"athruithe déanta agat ar do mhúnlaí (sa chás seo, tá cinn nua déanta agat) "
"agus gur mhaith leat na hathruithe a stóráil mar * imirce *."

msgid ""
"Migrations are how Django stores changes to your models (and thus your "
"database schema) - they're files on disk. You can read the migration for "
"your new model if you like; it's the file ``polls/migrations/"
"0001_initial.py``. Don't worry, you're not expected to read them every time "
"Django makes one, but they're designed to be human-editable in case you want "
"to manually tweak how Django changes things."
msgstr ""
"Is éard atá i gceist le himircí ná mar a stórálann Django athruithe ar do "
"mhúnlaí (agus dá bhrí sin do scéimre bunachar sonraí) - is comhaid ar diosca "
"iad. Is féidir leat an t-aistriú do do mhúnla nua a léamh más maith leat; is "
"é an comhad ``polls/migrations/0001_initial.py``. Ná bíodh imní ort, ní "
"bheifear ag súil go léifidh tú iad gach uair a dhéanann Django ceann, ach tá "
"siad deartha le gur féidir iad a chur in eagar ag an duine ar eagla go "
"dteastaíonn uait an chaoi a n-athraíonn Django rudaí a athrú de láimh."

msgid ""
"There's a command that will run the migrations for you and manage your "
"database schema automatically - that's called :djadmin:`migrate`, and we'll "
"come to it in a moment - but first, let's see what SQL that migration would "
"run. The :djadmin:`sqlmigrate` command takes migration names and returns "
"their SQL:"
msgstr ""
"Tá ordú ann a reáchtálfaidh na himscrúduithe duit agus a bhainisteoidh "
"scéimre do bhunachar sonraí go huathoibríoch - ar a dtugtar : djadmin: "
"`imirce`, agus tiocfaimid chuige faoi láthair - ach ar dtús, feicfimid cad a "
"rithfeadh SQL leis an imirce sin. Tógann an t-ordú : djadmin:`sqlmigrate` "
"ainmneacha imirce agus cuireann sé a SQL ar ais:"

msgid ""
"You should see something similar to the following (we've reformatted it for "
"readability):"
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart duit rud éigin cosúil leis an méid seo a leanas a fheiceáil "
"(rinneamar é a athfhormáidiú le haghaidh inléiteachta):"

msgid "Note the following:"
msgstr "Tabhair faoi deara iad seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The exact output will vary depending on the database you are using. The "
"example above is generated for PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""
"Athróidh an t-aschur cruinn ag brath ar an mbunachar sonraí atá in úsáid "
"agat. Gintear an sampla thuas do PostgreSQL."

msgid ""
"Table names are automatically generated by combining the name of the app "
"(``polls``) and the lowercase name of the model -- ``question`` and "
"``choice``. (You can override this behavior.)"
msgstr ""
"Gintear ainmneacha táblaí go huathoibríoch trí ainm na haipe (`` "
"pobalbhreith``) agus ainm litreacha beaga na samhla a chomhcheangal -- `` "
"ceist`` agus `` rogha``. (Is féidir leat an iompar seo a shárú.)"

msgid ""
"Primary keys (IDs) are added automatically. (You can override this, too.)"
msgstr ""
"Cuirtear eochracha príomhúla (IDs) leis go huathoibríoch. (Is féidir leat é "
"seo a shárú freisin.)"

msgid ""
"By convention, Django appends ``\"_id\"`` to the foreign key field name. "
"(Yes, you can override this, as well.)"
msgstr ""
"De réir an ghnáis, cuireann Django `` \"_id\"`` i gceangal leis an ainm "
"réimse eochrach eochrach. (Sea, is féidir leat é seo a shárú, chomh maith.)"

msgid ""
"The foreign key relationship is made explicit by a ``FOREIGN KEY`` "
"constraint. Don't worry about the ``DEFERRABLE`` parts; it's telling "
"PostgreSQL to not enforce the foreign key until the end of the transaction."
msgstr ""
"Léirítear an gaol eochrach eachtrach le srian ``eochair Choigríche``. Ná "
"bíodh imní ort faoi na codanna ``DEFERRABLE``; tá sé ag rá le PostgreSQL gan "
"an eochair choigríche a fhorghníomhú go dtí deireadh an idirbhirt."

msgid ""
"It's tailored to the database you're using, so database-specific field types "
"such as ``auto_increment`` (MySQL), ``bigint PRIMARY KEY GENERATED BY "
"DEFAULT AS IDENTITY`` (PostgreSQL), or ``integer primary key autoincrement`` "
"(SQLite) are handled for you automatically. Same goes for the quoting of "
"field names -- e.g., using double quotes or single quotes."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé in oiriúint don bhunachar sonraí atá in úsáid agat, mar sin cineálacha "
"réimse a bhaineann go sonrach leis an mbunachar sonraí ar nós `` "
"auto_increment`` (MySQL), ``bigint PRIMARY EOCHAIR A GHINEÁLaítear GAN "
"RÉAMHSHLÁN MAR FHÉINIÚLACHT`` (PostgreSQL), nó `` uath-incrimint phríomhúil "
"Láimhseáiltear `` (SQLite) duit go huathoibríoch. Baineann an rud céanna le "
"hainmneacha páirce a lua -- m.sh., ag baint úsáide as Sleachta dúbailte nó "
"Sleachta singil."

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`sqlmigrate` command doesn't actually run the migration on your "
"database - instead, it prints it to the screen so that you can see what SQL "
"Django thinks is required. It's useful for checking what Django is going to "
"do or if you have database administrators who require SQL scripts for "
"changes."
msgstr ""
"Ní ritheann an t-ordú :djadmin:`sqlmigrate` an t-imirce ar do bhunachar "
"sonraí - ina ionad sin, priontaí sé chuig an scáileán ionas gur féidir leat "
"a fheiceáil cad a cheapann SQL Django atá ag teastáil. Tá sé úsáideach chun "
"a sheiceáil cad atá le déanamh ag Django nó má tá riarthóirí bunachar sonraí "
"agat a dteastaíonn scripteanna SQL le haghaidh athruithe."

msgid ""
"If you're interested, you can also run :djadmin:`python manage.py check "
"<check>`; this checks for any problems in your project without making "
"migrations or touching the database."
msgstr ""
"Má tá suim agat, is féidir leat :djadmin:`seiceáil python manage.py <check>` "
"a rith freisin; seiceálann sé seo aon fhadhbanna i do thionscadal gan "
"ascnaimh a dhéanamh nó teagmháil a dhéanamh leis an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Now, run :djadmin:`migrate` again to create those model tables in your "
"database:"
msgstr ""
"Anois, rith :djadmin:`migrate` arís chun na táblaí samhail sin a chruthú i "
"do bhunachar sonraí:"

msgid ""
"The :djadmin:`migrate` command takes all the migrations that haven't been "
"applied (Django tracks which ones are applied using a special table in your "
"database called ``django_migrations``) and runs them against your database - "
"essentially, synchronizing the changes you made to your models with the "
"schema in the database."
msgstr ""
"Tógann an t-ordú :djadmin:`migrate` gach ascnamh nár cuireadh i bhfeidhm "
"(rianann Django cé na cinn a chuirtear i bhfeidhm le tábla speisialta i do "
"bhunachar sonraí darb ainm ``django_migrations``) agus ritheann sé i gcoinne "
"do bhunachar sonraí - go bunúsach, sioncrónú an athruithe a rinne tú ar do "
"mhúnlaí leis an scéimre sa bhunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"Migrations are very powerful and let you change your models over time, as "
"you develop your project, without the need to delete your database or tables "
"and make new ones - it specializes in upgrading your database live, without "
"losing data. We'll cover them in more depth in a later part of the tutorial, "
"but for now, remember the three-step guide to making model changes:"
msgstr ""
"Tá imircigh an-chumhachtach agus ligeann siad duit do mhúnlaí a athrú le "
"himeacht ama, de réir mar a fhorbraíonn tú do thionscadal, gan gá do "
"bhunachar sonraí nó do tháblaí a scriosadh agus cinn nua a dhéanamh - "
"speisialtóireacht sé do bhunachar sonraí a uasghrádú beo, gan sonraí a "
"chailliúint. Déanfaimid iad a chlúdach níos doimhne i gcuid níos déanaí den "
"rang teagaisc, ach faoi láthair, cuimhnigh ar an treoir trí chéim chun "
"athruithe múnla a dhéanamh:"

msgid "Change your models (in ``models.py``)."
msgstr "Athraigh do mhúnlaí (i ``models.py``)."

msgid ""
"Run :djadmin:`python manage.py makemigrations <makemigrations>` to create "
"migrations for those changes"
msgstr ""
"Rith :djadmin:`python manage.py makemigrations <migrations>` chun ascnaimh a "
"chruthú do na hathruithe sin"

msgid ""
"Run :djadmin:`python manage.py migrate <migrate>` to apply those changes to "
"the database."
msgstr ""
"Rith :djadmin:`python manage.py migrate <migrate>` chun na hathruithe sin a "
"chur i bhfeidhm ar an mbunachar sonraí."

msgid ""
"The reason that there are separate commands to make and apply migrations is "
"because you'll commit migrations to your version control system and ship "
"them with your app; they not only make your development easier, they're also "
"usable by other developers and in production."
msgstr ""
"Is é an fáth go bhfuil orduithe ar leith ann chun ascnaimh a dhéanamh agus a "
"chur i bhfeidhm ná go ndéanfaidh tú ascnaimh chuig do chóras rialaithe "
"leagan agus seolfaidh tú le d'aip iad; ní hamháin go ndéanann siad "
"d'fhorbairt níos éasca, is féidir le forbróirí eile iad a úsáid agus i "
"dtáirgeadh."

msgid ""
"Read the :doc:`django-admin documentation </ref/django-admin>` for full "
"information on what the ``manage.py`` utility can do."
msgstr ""
"Léigh an :doc:`doiciméadúchán django-admin </ref/django-admin>` chun "
"faisnéis iomlán a fháil faoin méid is féidir leis an bhfóntas ``manage.py`` "
"a dhéanamh."

msgid "Playing with the API"
msgstr "Ag imirt leis an API"

msgid ""
"Now, let's hop into the interactive Python shell and play around with the "
"free API Django gives you. To invoke the Python shell, use this command:"
msgstr ""
"Anois, léim isteach sa bhlaosc Python idirghníomhach agus imirt timpeall "
"leis an API saor in aisce a thugann Django duit. Chun an bhlaosc Python a "
"agairt, bain úsáid as an ordú seo:"

msgid ""
"We're using this instead of simply typing \"python\", "
"because :file:`manage.py` sets the :envvar:`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` "
"environment variable, which gives Django the Python import path to "
"your :file:`mysite/settings.py` file. By default, the :djadmin:`shell` "
"command automatically imports the models from your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once you're in the shell, explore the :doc:`database API </topics/db/"
"queries>`:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú sa bhlaosc, scrúdaigh an :doc:`database API </topics/db/"
"queries>`:"

msgid ""
"Wait a minute. ``<Question: Question object (1)>`` isn't a helpful "
"representation of this object. Let's fix that by editing the ``Question`` "
"model (in the ``polls/models.py`` file) and adding "
"a :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.__str__` method to both ``Question`` and "
"``Choice``:"
msgstr ""
"Fan nóiméad. ``<Ceist: Ceist oibiachta (1)> Ní léiriú cabhrach é `` ar an "
"oibiacht seo. Déanaimis é sin a shocrú tríd an múnla ``Ceist`` a chur in "
"eagar (sa chomhad ``vótaíocht/models.py``) agus "
"modh :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.__str__` a chur leis an dá ``Ceist `` "
"agus ``Rogha``:"

msgid ""
"It's important to add :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.__str__` methods to "
"your models, not only for your own convenience when dealing with the "
"interactive prompt, but also because objects' representations are used "
"throughout Django's automatically-generated admin."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé tábhachtach modhanna :meth:`~django.db.models.Model.__str__` a chur le "
"do mhúnlaí, ní hamháin ar mhaithe le do chaoithiúlacht féin agus tú ag "
"déileáil leis an leid idirghníomhach, ach freisin toisc go n-úsáidtear "
"léiriúcháin oibiachtaí ar fud Django a ghintear go huathoibríoch riar."

msgid "Let's also add a custom method to this model:"
msgstr "Cuirfimid modh saincheaptha leis an múnla seo freisin:"

msgid ""
"Note the addition of ``import datetime`` and ``from django.utils import "
"timezone``, to reference Python's standard :mod:`datetime` module and "
"Django's time-zone-related utilities in :mod:`django.utils.timezone`, "
"respectively. If you aren't familiar with time zone handling in Python, you "
"can learn more in the :doc:`time zone support docs </topics/i18n/timezones>`."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur cuireadh `` am allmhairiú dáta`` agus `` ó chrios ama "
"iompórtála django.utils`` leis, chun tagairt a dhéanamh do mhodúl "
"caighdeánach Python :mod:` datetime` agus fóntais a bhaineann le crios ama "
"Django i :mod:` django.utils. crios ama`, faoi seach. Mura bhfuil tú eolach "
"ar láimhseáil crios ama i Python, is féidir leat níos mó a fhoghlaim "
"sa :doc:`doiciméid tacaíochta crios ama </topics/i18n/timezones>`."

msgid ""
"Save these changes and start a new Python interactive shell. (If a three-"
"chevron prompt (>>>) indicates you are still in the shell, you need to exit "
"first using ``exit()``). Run ``python manage.py shell`` again to reload the "
"models."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information on model relations, see :doc:`Accessing related objects "
"</ref/models/relations>`. For more on how to use double underscores to "
"perform field lookups via the API, see :ref:`Field lookups <field-lookups-"
"intro>`. For full details on the database API, see our :doc:`Database API "
"reference </topics/db/queries>`."
msgstr ""
"Chun tuilleadh eolais a fháil ar chaidreamh samhlacha, féach :doc:`Rochtain "
"ar réada gaolmhara </ref/models/relations>`. Chun tuilleadh eolais a fháil "
"ar conas béim dhúbailte a úsáid chun cuardaigh allamuigh a dhéanamh tríd an "
"API, féach :ref:`Field lookups <field-lookups-intro>`. Le haghaidh sonraí "
"iomlána ar API an bhunachair shonraí, féach ar ár :doc:`Tagairt API Bunachar "
"Sonraí </topics/db/queries>`."

msgid "Introducing the Django Admin"
msgstr "Riarachán Django a thabhairt isteach"

msgid ""
"Generating admin sites for your staff or clients to add, change, and delete "
"content is tedious work that doesn't require much creativity. For that "
"reason, Django entirely automates creation of admin interfaces for models."
msgstr ""
"Is obair dhian é suíomhanna riaracháin a ghiniúint chun go bhféadfaidh "
"d’fhoireann nó do chliaint ábhar a chur leis, a athrú agus a scriosadh nach "
"dteastaíonn mórán cruthaitheachta. Ar an ábhar sin, déanann Django "
"uathoibriú go hiomlán ar chruthú comhéadain riaracháin le haghaidh samhlacha."

msgid ""
"Django was written in a newsroom environment, with a very clear separation "
"between \"content publishers\" and the \"public\" site. Site managers use "
"the system to add news stories, events, sports scores, etc., and that "
"content is displayed on the public site. Django solves the problem of "
"creating a unified interface for site administrators to edit content."
msgstr ""
"Scríobhadh Django i dtimpeallacht seomra nuachta, le deighilt an-soiléir "
"idir \"foilsitheoirí ábhar\" agus an suíomh \"poiblí\". Úsáideann "
"bainisteoirí láithreáin an córas chun scéalta nuachta, imeachtaí, scóir "
"spóirt, etc., a chur leis, agus taispeántar an t-ábhar sin ar an suíomh "
"poiblí. Réitíonn Django an fhadhb a bhaineann le comhéadan aontaithe a "
"chruthú do riarthóirí láithreáin chun ábhar a chur in eagar."

msgid ""
"The admin isn't intended to be used by site visitors. It's for site managers."
msgstr ""
"Níl an riarthóir ceaptha le húsáid ag cuairteoirí suímh. Is do bhainisteoirí "
"láithreán é."

msgid "Creating an admin user"
msgstr "Úsáideoir admin a chruthú"

msgid ""
"First we'll need to create a user who can login to the admin site. Run the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús beidh orainn úsáideoir a chruthú a bheidh in ann logáil isteach ar "
"an suíomh riaracháin. Rith an t-ordú seo a leanas:"

msgid "Enter your desired username and press enter."
msgstr "Cuir isteach an t-ainm úsáideora atá uait agus brúigh Enter."

msgid "You will then be prompted for your desired email address:"
msgstr "Tabharfar leid duit ansin do sheoladh ríomhphoist atá uait:"

msgid ""
"The final step is to enter your password. You will be asked to enter your "
"password twice, the second time as a confirmation of the first."
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéim dheireanach ná do phasfhocal a chur isteach. Iarrfar ort do "
"phasfhocal a chur isteach faoi dhó, an dara huair mar dheimhniú ar an gcéad "
"cheann."

msgid "Start the development server"
msgstr "Tosaigh an freastalaí forbartha"

msgid ""
"The Django admin site is activated by default. Let's start the development "
"server and explore it."
msgstr ""
"Tá suíomh riaracháin Django gníomhachtaithe de réir réamhshocraithe. A "
"ligean ar tús a chur leis an bhfreastalaí forbartha agus é a iniúchadh."

msgid "If the server is not running start it like so:"
msgstr "Mura bhfuil an freastalaí ag rith cuir tús leis mar seo:"

msgid ""
"Now, open a web browser and go to \"/admin/\" on your local domain -- e.g., "
"http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/. You should see the admin's login screen:"
msgstr ""
"Anois, oscail brabhsálaí gréasáin agus téigh go dtí \"/admin/\" ar "
"d'fhearann ​​​​áitiúil -- m.sh., http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/. Ba cheart duit "
"scáileán logáil isteach an riarthóir a fheiceáil:"

msgid "Django admin login screen"
msgstr "Django scáileán logáil isteach admin"

msgid ""
"Since :doc:`translation </topics/i18n/translation>` is turned on by default, "
"if you set :setting:`LANGUAGE_CODE`, the login screen will be displayed in "
"the given language (if Django has appropriate translations)."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é go gcuirtear :doc:`translation </topics/i18n/translation>` ar siúl "
"de réir réamhshocraithe, má shocraíonn tú :`LANGUAGE_CODE`, taispeánfar an "
"scáileán logála isteach sa teanga a thugtar (má tá aistriúcháin chuí ag "
"Django)."

msgid "Enter the admin site"
msgstr "Cuir isteach an suíomh admin"

msgid ""
"Now, try logging in with the superuser account you created in the previous "
"step. You should see the Django admin index page:"
msgstr ""
"Anois, bain triail as logáil isteach leis an gcuntas sár-úsáideoir a "
"chruthaigh tú sa chéim roimhe seo. Ba cheart duit an leathanach innéacs "
"riaracháin Django a fheiceáil:"

msgid "Django admin index page"
msgstr "Leathanach innéacs admin Django"

msgid ""
"You should see a few types of editable content: groups and users. They are "
"provided by :mod:`django.contrib.auth`, the authentication framework shipped "
"by Django."
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart go bhfeicfeá roinnt cineálacha ábhar in eagar: grúpaí agus "
"úsáideoirí. Soláthraítear iad ag :mod:`django.contrib.auth`, an creat "
"fíordheimhnithe seolta ag Django."

msgid "Make the poll app modifiable in the admin"
msgstr "Déan an aip vótaíochta inathraithe sa riarthóir"

msgid "But where's our poll app? It's not displayed on the admin index page."
msgstr ""
"Ach cá bhfuil ár n-aip vótaíochta? Níl sé ar taispeáint ar an leathanach "
"innéacs admin."

msgid ""
"Only one more thing to do: we need to tell the admin that ``Question`` "
"objects have an admin interface. To do this, open the :file:`polls/admin.py` "
"file, and edit it to look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Níl ach rud amháin eile le déanamh: ní mór dúinn a rá leis an riarthóir go "
"bhfuil comhéadan riaracháin ag réada ``Ceist``. Chun seo a dhéanamh, oscail "
"an comhad ::`polls/admin.py`, agus cuir in eagar é chun breathnú mar seo:"

msgid "``polls/admin.py``"
msgstr "``polls/admin.py``"

msgid "Explore the free admin functionality"
msgstr "Déan iniúchadh ar fheidhmiúlacht admin saor in aisce"

msgid ""
"Now that we've registered ``Question``, Django knows that it should be "
"displayed on the admin index page:"
msgstr ""
"Anois agus ``Ceist`` cláraithe againn, tá a fhios ag Django gur cheart é a "
"thaispeáint ar an leathanach innéacs riaracháin:"

msgid "Django admin index page, now with polls displayed"
msgstr "Leathanach innéacs admin Django, anois le pobalbhreith ar taispeáint"

msgid ""
"Click \"Questions\". Now you're at the \"change list\" page for questions. "
"This page displays all the questions in the database and lets you choose one "
"to change it. There's the \"What's up?\" question we created earlier:"
msgstr ""
"Cliceáil \"Ceisteanna\". Anois tá tú ag an leathanach \"liosta athraithe\" "
"le haghaidh ceisteanna. Taispeánann an leathanach seo na ceisteanna go léir "
"sa bhunachar sonraí agus ligeann sé duit ceann a roghnú chun é a athrú. Tá "
"an \"Cad atá ar bun?\" ceist a chruthaigh muid níos luaithe:"

msgid "Polls change list page"
msgstr "Athraítear leathanach liosta na vótaíochtaí"

msgid "Click the \"What's up?\" question to edit it:"
msgstr ""
"Cliceáil ar an gcnaipe \"Cad atá ar bun?\" ceist chun é a chur in eagar:"

msgid "Editing form for question object"
msgstr "Foirm eagarthóireachta don ábhar ceiste"

msgid "Things to note here:"
msgstr "Rudaí le tabhairt faoi deara anseo:"

msgid "The form is automatically generated from the ``Question`` model."
msgstr "Gintear an fhoirm go huathoibríoch ón múnla ``Ceist``."

msgid ""
"The different model field types "
"(:class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`, :class:`~django.db.models.CharField`) "
"correspond to the appropriate HTML input widget. Each type of field knows "
"how to display itself in the Django admin."
msgstr ""
"Freagraíonn na cineálacha éagsúla réimse samhlacha "
"(:rang:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`, :rang:`~django.db.models.CharField`) "
"don ghiuirléid ionchur HTML cuí. Tá a fhios ag gach cineál réimse conas é "
"féin a thaispeáint sa riarthóir Django."

msgid ""
"Each :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` gets free JavaScript "
"shortcuts. Dates get a \"Today\" shortcut and calendar popup, and times get "
"a \"Now\" shortcut and a convenient popup that lists commonly entered times."
msgstr ""
"Faigheann gach :rang:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` aicearraí JavaScript "
"saor in aisce. Faigheann dátaí aicearra \"Inniu\" agus aníos aníos féilire, "
"agus faigheann uaireanta aicearra \"Anois\" agus mír aníos áisiúil a "
"liostaíonn na hamanna a chuirtear isteach go coitianta."

msgid "The bottom part of the page gives you a couple of options:"
msgstr "Tugann an chuid íochtair den leathanach cúpla rogha duit:"

msgid ""
"Save -- Saves changes and returns to the change-list page for this type of "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Sábháil -- Sábháil athruithe agus filleann sé ar an leathanach liosta "
"athruithe don chineál seo oibiachta."

msgid ""
"Save and continue editing -- Saves changes and reloads the admin page for "
"this object."
msgstr ""
"Sábháil agus lean ar aghaidh leis an eagarthóireacht -- Sábháil na "
"hathruithe agus athlódálann sé an leathanach riaracháin don réad seo."

msgid ""
"Save and add another -- Saves changes and loads a new, blank form for this "
"type of object."
msgstr ""
"Sábháil agus cuir ceann eile leis -- Sábháil athruithe agus lódálann sé "
"foirm bhán nua don chineál seo réad."

msgid "Delete -- Displays a delete confirmation page."
msgstr "Scrios -- Taispeánann sé leathanach deimhnithe scriosta."

msgid ""
"If the value of \"Date published\" doesn't match the time when you created "
"the question in :doc:`Tutorial 1</intro/tutorial01>`, it probably means you "
"forgot to set the correct value for the :setting:`TIME_ZONE` setting. Change "
"it, reload the page and check that the correct value appears."
msgstr ""
"Mura dtagann luach \"Dáta foilsithe\" leis an am ar chruthaigh tú an cheist "
"i :doc:`Teagasc 1</intro/tutorial01>`, is dócha go gciallaíonn sé go ndearna "
"tú dearmad ar an luach ceart a shocrú don :setting:` socrú TIME_ZONE`. "
"Athraigh é, athlódáil an leathanach agus seiceáil go bhfuil an luach ceart "
"le feiceáil."

msgid ""
"Change the \"Date published\" by clicking the \"Today\" and \"Now\" "
"shortcuts. Then click \"Save and continue editing.\" Then click \"History\" "
"in the upper right. You'll see a page listing all changes made to this "
"object via the Django admin, with the timestamp and username of the person "
"who made the change:"
msgstr ""
"Athraigh an \"Dáta foilsithe\" trí chliceáil ar na aicearraí \"Inniu\" agus "
"\"Anois\". Ansin cliceáil \"Sábháil agus leanúint ar aghaidh leis an "
"eagarthóireacht.\" Ansin cliceáil \"Stair\" ar dheis uachtarach. Feicfidh tú "
"leathanach ina liostaítear na hathruithe go léir a rinneadh ar an réad seo "
"tríd an riarthóir Django, le stampa ama agus ainm úsáideora an duine a rinne "
"an t-athrú:"

msgid "History page for question object"
msgstr "Leathanach staire don ábhar ceiste"

msgid ""
"When you're comfortable with the models API and have familiarized yourself "
"with the admin site, read :doc:`part 3 of this tutorial</intro/tutorial03>` "
"to learn about how to add more views to our polls app."
msgstr ""
"Nuair atá tú ar do chompord le API na múnlaí agus nuair a bheidh an suíomh "
"riaracháin curtha ar an eolas agat, léigh :doc:`cuid 3 den rang teagaisc "
"seo</intro/tutorial03>` chun tuilleadh eolais a fháil faoi conas tuilleadh "
"tuairimí a chur lenár bhfeidhmchlár pobalbhreithe."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 3"
msgstr "Do chéad aip Django a scríobh, cuid 3"

msgid ""
"This tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 2 </intro/tutorial02>` left off. "
"We're continuing the web-poll application and will focus on creating the "
"public interface -- \"views.\""
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an rang teagaisc seo nuair a d'fhág :doc:`Tutorial 2 </intro/"
"tutorial02>` as. Táimid ag leanúint leis an bhfeidhmchlár vótaíochta "
"gréasáin agus díreoimid ar chomhéadan poiblí a chruthú -- \"tuairimí.\""

msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Forbhreathnú"

msgid ""
"A view is a \"type\" of web page in your Django application that generally "
"serves a specific function and has a specific template. For example, in a "
"blog application, you might have the following views:"
msgstr ""
"Is éard is dearcadh ann ná \"cineál\" de leathanach gréasáin i d'iarratas "
"Django a fhreastalaíonn go ginearálta ar fheidhm shonrach agus a bhfuil "
"teimpléad ar leith aige. Mar shampla, in iarratas blag, b’fhéidir go mbeadh "
"na tuairimí seo a leanas agat:"

msgid "Blog homepage -- displays the latest few entries."
msgstr "Leathanach baile blag -- taispeánann sé na hiontrálacha is déanaí."

msgid "Entry \"detail\" page -- permalink page for a single entry."
msgstr ""
"Iontráil \"mionsonraí\" leathanach -- leathanach permalink le haghaidh "
"iontráil amháin."

msgid ""
"Year-based archive page -- displays all months with entries in the given "
"year."
msgstr ""
"Leathanach cartlainne bunaithe ar bhliain -- taispeánann sé gach mí le "
"hiontrálacha sa bhliain ar leith."

msgid ""
"Month-based archive page -- displays all days with entries in the given "
"month."
msgstr ""
"Leathanach cartlainne bunaithe ar mhí -- taispeánann sé gach lá le "
"hiontrálacha sa mhí ar leith."

msgid "Day-based archive page -- displays all entries in the given day."
msgstr ""
"Leathanach cartlainne bunaithe ar an lá -- taispeánann sé gach iontráil sa "
"lá ar leith."

msgid "Comment action -- handles posting comments to a given entry."
msgstr "Gníomh tráchta -- Láimhseálann postáil tuairimí chuig iontráil tugtha."

msgid "In our poll application, we'll have the following four views:"
msgstr ""
"In ár n-iarratas vótaíochta, beidh na ceithre radharc seo a leanas againn:"

msgid "Question \"index\" page -- displays the latest few questions."
msgstr "Ceist \"innéacs\" leathanach - taispeánann sé na ceisteanna is déanaí."

msgid ""
"Question \"detail\" page -- displays a question text, with no results but "
"with a form to vote."
msgstr ""
"Leathanach \"mionsonraí\" Ceist -- taispeánann sé téacs ceiste, gan torthaí "
"ach le foirm vótála."

msgid ""
"Question \"results\" page -- displays results for a particular question."
msgstr ""
"Ceist \"torthaí\" leathanach -- taispeánann torthaí do cheist ar leith."

msgid ""
"Vote action -- handles voting for a particular choice in a particular "
"question."
msgstr ""
"Vóta caingean - láimhseálann vótáil do rogha ar leith i gceist ar leith."

msgid ""
"In Django, web pages and other content are delivered by views. Each view is "
"represented by a Python function (or method, in the case of class-based "
"views). Django will choose a view by examining the URL that's requested (to "
"be precise, the part of the URL after the domain name)."
msgstr ""
"In Django, déantar leathanaigh ghréasáin agus ábhar eile a sheachadadh trí "
"radharcanna. Léirítear gach radharc le feidhm Python (nó modh, i gcás "
"radhairc rangbhunaithe). Roghnóidh Django radharc tríd an URL a iarrtar a "
"scrúdú (le bheith beacht, an chuid den URL tar éis an ainm fearainn)."

msgid ""
"Now in your time on the web you may have come across such beauties as ``ME2/"
"Sites/dirmod.htm?sid=&type=gen&mod=Core+Pages&gid=A6CD4967199A42D9B65B1B``. "
"You will be pleased to know that Django allows us much more elegant *URL "
"patterns* than that."
msgstr ""
"Anois agus tú i do chuid ama ar an ngréasán b'fhéidir gur tháinig tú trasna "
"ar áilleachta mar ``ME2/Sites/dirmod.htm?"
"sid=&type=gen&mod=Core+Pages&gid=A6CD4967199A42D9B65B1B``. Beidh tú sásta a "
"fhios go gceadaíonn Django patrúin * URL * i bhfad níos galánta dúinn ná sin."

msgid ""
"A URL pattern is the general form of a URL - for example: ``/newsarchive/"
"<year>/<month>/``."
msgstr ""
"Foirm ghinearálta URL is ea patrún URL - mar shampla: ``/newsarchive/<year>/"
"<month>/``."

msgid ""
"To get from a URL to a view, Django uses what are known as 'URLconfs'. A "
"URLconf maps URL patterns to views."
msgstr ""
"Chun dul ó URL go radharc, úsáideann Django rud ar a dtugtar 'URLconfs'. "
"Léarscáilíonn URLconf patrúin URL chun amharc orthu."

msgid ""
"This tutorial provides basic instruction in the use of URLconfs, and you can "
"refer to :doc:`/topics/http/urls` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn an rang teagaisc seo treoir bhunúsach maidir le húsáid "
"URLconfs, agus is féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh do :doc:`/topics/http/urls` "
"le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais."

msgid "Writing more views"
msgstr "Tuilleadh tuairimí á scríobh"

msgid ""
"Now let's add a few more views to ``polls/views.py``. These views are "
"slightly different, because they take an argument:"
msgstr ""
"Anois cuirimis cúpla radharc eile le ``vótaíocht/views.py``. Tá na tuairimí "
"seo beagán difriúil, toisc go nglacann siad argóint:"

msgid ""
"Wire these new views into the ``polls.urls`` module by adding the "
"following :func:`~django.urls.path` calls:"
msgstr ""
"Sreangaigh na radharcanna nua seo isteach sa mhodúl ``polls.urls`` tríd an "
"méid seo a leanas a chur leis :func: glaonna `~ django.urls.path`:"

msgid ""
"Take a look in your browser, at \"/polls/34/\". It'll run the ``detail()`` "
"function and display whatever ID you provide in the URL. Try \"/polls/34/"
"results/\" and \"/polls/34/vote/\" too -- these will display the placeholder "
"results and voting pages."
msgstr ""
"Féach i do bhrabhsálaí, ag \"/polls/34/\". Rithfidh sé an fheidhm "
"``detail()`` agus taispeánfaidh sé cibé aitheantas a sholáthraíonn tú san "
"URL. Bain triail as \"/polls/34/results/\" agus \"/polls/34/vote/\" freisin "
"-- taispeánfaidh siad seo torthaí an tsealbhóra ionad agus na leathanaigh "
"vótála."

msgid ""
"When somebody requests a page from your website -- say, \"/polls/34/\", "
"Django will load the ``mysite.urls`` Python module because it's pointed to "
"by the :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF` setting. It finds the variable named "
"``urlpatterns`` and traverses the patterns in order. After finding the match "
"at ``'polls/'``, it strips off the matching text (``\"polls/\"``) and sends "
"the remaining text -- ``\"34/\"`` -- to the 'polls.urls' URLconf for further "
"processing. There it matches ``'<int:question_id>/'``, resulting in a call "
"to the ``detail()`` view like so:"
msgstr ""
"Nuair a iarrann duine éigin leathanach ó do shuíomh Gréasáin -- abair, \"/"
"polls/34/\", lódálfaidh Django an modúl Python ``mysite.urls`` toisc go "
"bhfuil sé dírithe ag an socrú :setting:`ROOT_URLCONF`. Faigheann sé an "
"athróg darb ainm ``urlpatterns`` agus trasnaíonn sé na patrúin in ord. Tar "
"éis dó an meaits a aimsiú ag ``` pobalbhreith/'``, scriosann sé an téacs "
"meaitseála (``\" pobalbhreith / \"``) agus seolann sé an téacs atá fágtha -- "
"`` \"34/\"`` -- chuig an ' URLconf polls.urls le haghaidh tuilleadh "
"próiseála. Is amhlaidh a mheaitseálann sé ``' <int:question_id>/'``, agus "
"glao ar an radharc ``detail()`` mar seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"The ``question_id=34`` part comes from ``<int:question_id>``. Using angle "
"brackets \"captures\" part of the URL and sends it as a keyword argument to "
"the view function. The ``question_id`` part of the string defines the name "
"that will be used to identify the matched pattern, and the ``int`` part is a "
"converter that determines what patterns should match this part of the URL "
"path. The colon (``:``) separates the converter and pattern name."
msgstr ""
"Tagann an chuid ``question_id=34`` ó `` <int:question_id>``. Ag baint úsáide "
"as lúibíní uillinn \"gabhálann\" cuid den URL agus seolann sé mar argóint "
"eochairfhocal chuig an bhfeidhm radhairc. Sainmhíníonn an chuid "
"``question_id`` den teaghrán an t-ainm a úsáidfear chun an patrún "
"comhoiriúnaithe a shainaithint, agus is tiontaire é an chuid ``int`` a "
"shocraíonn cé na patrúin ba cheart a bheith ag teacht leis an gcuid seo den "
"chonair URL. Scarann ​​an colon (``:``) an t-ainm tiontaire agus patrún."

msgid "Write views that actually do something"
msgstr "Scríobh tuairimí a dhéanann rud éigin i ndáiríre"

msgid ""
"Each view is responsible for doing one of two things: returning "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse` object containing the content for the "
"requested page, or raising an exception such as :exc:`~django.http.Http404`. "
