msgstr ""
"Tugann ``F (\"vótaí\") + 1`` :ref:` treoir don bhunachar sonraí <avoiding-"
"race-conditions-using-f>` líon na vótaí a mhéadú faoi 1."

msgid ""
"After incrementing the choice count, the code returns "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` rather than a "
"normal :class:`~django.http.HttpResponse`. :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` "
"takes a single argument: the URL to which the user will be redirected (see "
"the following point for how we construct the URL in this case)."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis an comhaireamh rogha a mhéadú, cuireann an cód ar "
"ais :rang:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` seachas "
"gnáth:rang:`~django.http.HttpResponse`. :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` "
"a thógann argóint amháin: an URL a mbeidh an t-úsáideoir a atreorú (féach an "
"pointe seo a leanas le haghaidh conas a dhéanfaimid an URL sa chás seo)."

msgid ""
"As the Python comment above points out, you should always return "
"an :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` after successfully dealing "
"with POST data. This tip isn't specific to Django; it's good web development "
"practice in general."
msgstr ""
"Mar a léiríonn an trácht Python thuas, ba cheart "
"duit :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` a chur ar ais i gcónaí tar "
"éis déileáil go rathúil le sonraí POST. Ní bhaineann an leid seo go sonrach "
"le Django; is dea-chleachtas forbartha gréasáin é go ginearálta."

msgid ""
"We are using the :func:`~django.urls.reverse` function in "
"the :class:`~django.http.HttpResponseRedirect` constructor in this example. "
"This function helps avoid having to hardcode a URL in the view function. It "
"is given the name of the view that we want to pass control to and the "
