msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo beagnach díreach mar a chéile leis an radharc ``detail()``ó :doc: "
"`Teagasc 3 </intro/tutorial03>`. Is é an t-aon difríocht ná an t-ainm "
"teimpléad. Déanfaimid an iomarcaíocht seo a réiteach níos déanaí."

msgid "Use generic views: Less code is better"
msgstr "Úsáid tuairimí cineálach: Is fearr níos lú cód"

msgid ""
"The ``detail()`` (from :doc:`Tutorial 3 </intro/tutorial03>`) and "
"``results()`` views are very short -- and, as mentioned above, redundant. "
"The ``index()`` view, which displays a list of polls, is similar."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo beagnach díreach mar a chéile leis an radharc ``detail()``ó :doc: "
"`Teagasc 3 </intro/tutorial03>`. Is é an t-aon difríocht ná an t-ainm "
"teimpléad. Déanfaimid an iomarcaíocht seo a réiteach níos déanaí."

msgid ""
"These views represent a common case of basic web development: getting data "
"from the database according to a parameter passed in the URL, loading a "
"template and returning the rendered template. Because this is so common, "
"Django provides a shortcut, called the \"generic views\" system."
msgstr ""
"Is ionann na tuairimí seo agus cás coiteann d'fhorbairt bhunúsach gréasáin: "
"sonraí a fháil ón mbunachar sonraí de réir paraiméadar a ritheadh ​​san URL, "
"teimpléad a lódáil agus an teimpléad rindreáilte a sheoladh ar ais. Toisc go "
"bhfuil sé seo chomh coitianta, soláthraíonn Django aicearra, ar a dtugtar an "
"córas \"tuairimí cineálacha\"."

msgid ""
"Generic views abstract common patterns to the point where you don't even "
"need to write Python code to write an app. For example, "
"the :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView` "
"and :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` generic views abstract "
"the concepts of \"display a list of objects\" and \"display a detail page "
"for a particular type of object\" respectively."
msgstr ""
"Teibríonn tuairimí cineálacha patrúin choitianta go dtí an pointe nach gá "
"duit fiú cód Python a scríobh chun aip a scríobh. Mar shampla, déanann "
"an :rang:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView` "
"agus :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` tuairimí cineálacha a "
"achoimríonn na coincheapa \"taispeáin liosta réad\" agus\" taispeáin "
"leathanach mionsonraí do chineál áirithe réad\" faoi seach."

msgid ""
"Let's convert our poll app to use the generic views system, so we can delete "
"a bunch of our own code. We'll have to take a few steps to make the "
"conversion. We will:"
msgstr ""
"Déanaimis ár n-aip vótaíochta a thiontú chun an córas tuairimí cineálach a "
"úsáid, ionas gur féidir linn ár gcód féin a scriosadh. Beidh orainn a "
"ghlacadh roinnt céimeanna a dhéanamh ar an chomhshó. Déanfaimid:"

msgid "Convert the URLconf."
msgstr "Tiontaigh URLconf."

msgid "Delete some of the old, unneeded views."
msgstr "Scrios cuid de na seanamharcanna nach bhfuil ag teastáil."

msgid "Introduce new views based on Django's generic views."
msgstr "Tabhair isteach tuairimí nua bunaithe ar thuairimí cineálacha Django."

msgid "Read on for details."
msgstr "Léigh ar aghaidh le haghaidh sonraí."

msgid "Why the code-shuffle?"
msgstr "Cén fáth an cód-shuffle?"

msgid ""
"Generally, when writing a Django app, you'll evaluate whether generic views "
"are a good fit for your problem, and you'll use them from the beginning, "
"rather than refactoring your code halfway through. But this tutorial "
"intentionally has focused on writing the views \"the hard way\" until now, "
"to focus on core concepts."
msgstr ""
"Go ginearálta, agus aip Django á scríobh agat, déanfaidh tú meastóireacht ar "
"cé acu an n-oireann tuairimí cineálacha go maith do d’fhadhb, agus úsáidfidh "
"tú iad ón tús, seachas do chód a athmhacrú leath bealaigh tríd. Ach dhírigh "
"an teagasc seo go hintinneach ar na tuairimí \"an bealach crua\" a scríobh "
"go dtí seo, chun díriú ar chroí-choincheapa."

msgid "You should know basic math before you start using a calculator."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir go mbeadh a fhios agat matamaitic bhunúsach sula dtosaíonn tú ag "
"úsáid áireamhán."

msgid "Amend URLconf"
msgstr "Leasaigh URLconf"

msgid "First, open the ``polls/urls.py`` URLconf and change it like so:"
msgstr "Ar dtús, oscail an URLconf `` polls/urls.py`` agus athraigh é mar sin:"

msgid ""
"Note that the name of the matched pattern in the path strings of the second "
"and third patterns has changed from ``<question_id>`` to ``<pk>``. This is "
"necessary because we'll use "
"the :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` generic view to replace "
"our ``detail()`` and ``results()`` views, and it expects the primary key "
"value captured from the URL to be called ``\"pk\"``."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil ainm an phatrúin chomhoiriúnaithe i teaghráin "
"chosáin an dara agus an tríú patrún athraithe ó ``<question_id>`` go "
"``<pk>``. Tá sé seo riachtanach toisc go n-úsáidfimid an radharc "
"cineálach :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` chun ár "
"radharcanna ``detail()`` agus ``torthaí()`` a chur in ionad ár n-amharc "
"``detail()`` agus ``torthaí ()``, agus tá sé ag súil leis na radharcanna "
"príomhluach eochrach a gabhadh ón URL ar a dtabharfar ``\"pk\"``."

msgid "Amend views"
msgstr "Leasú ar radharcanna"

msgid ""
"Next, we're going to remove our old ``index``, ``detail``, and ``results`` "
"views and use Django's generic views instead. To do so, open the ``polls/"
"views.py`` file and change it like so:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, bainfimid ár seanamharcanna `` index``, ``sonraí``, agus ``torthaí`` "
"agus úsáidfimid radharcanna cineálacha Django ina ionad sin. Chun é sin a "
"dhéanamh, oscail an comhad ``vótaíocht/views.py`` agus athraigh é mar a "
"leanas:"

msgid ""
"Each generic view needs to know what model it will be acting upon. This is "
"provided using either the ``model`` attribute (in this example, ``model = "
"Question`` for  ``DetailView`` and ``ResultsView``) or by defining "
"the :meth:`~django.views.generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin.get_queryset` "
"method (as shown in ``IndexView``)."
msgstr ""
"Ní mór go mbeadh a fhios ag gach dearcadh cineálach cén samhail a mbeidh sé "
"ag feidhmiú air. Soláthraítear é seo trí úsáid a bhaint as an aitreabúid "
"``model`` (sa sampla seo, `` model = Ceist`` le haghaidh ``DetailView`` agus "
"``ResultsView``) nó trí na :meth:`~django.views a shainmhíniú. modh "
"generic.list.MultipleObjectMixin.get_queryset` (mar a thaispeántar in "
"``IndexView``)."

msgid ""
"By default, the :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` generic "
"view uses a template called ``<app name>/<model name>_detail.html``. In our "
"case, it would use the template ``\"polls/question_detail.html\"``. The "
"``template_name`` attribute is used to tell Django to use a specific "
"template name instead of the autogenerated default template name. We also "
"specify the ``template_name`` for the ``results`` list view -- this ensures "
"that the results view and the detail view have a different appearance when "
"rendered, even though they're both "
"a :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, úsáideann an t-amharc "
"cineálach :class:`~django.views.generic.detail.DetailView` teimpléad darb "
"ainm `` <ainm an fheidhmchláir>/<ainm an mhúnla>_detail.html``. Inár gcás, "
"d'úsáidfeadh sé an teimpléad ``\"vótaíocht/question_detail.html\"``. "
"Úsáidtear an aitreabúid ``template_name`` chun a rá le Django ainm teimpléid "
"ar leith a úsáid in ionad ainm an teimpléid réamhshocraithe uathghinte. "
"Sonraimid freisin an ``ainm_teimpléad`` don amharc liosta ``torthaí`` -- "
"cinntíonn sé seo go mbíonn cuma dhifriúil ar amharc na dtorthaí agus ar an "
"mionradharc nuair a rindreáiltear iad, cé gur :class:`~django iad "
"araon .views.generic.detail.DetailView` taobh thiar de na radhairc."

msgid ""
"Similarly, the :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView` generic view "
"uses a default template called ``<app name>/<model name>_list.html``; we use "
"``template_name`` to tell :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView` to "
"use our existing ``\"polls/index.html\"`` template."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gcaoi chéanna, úsáideann an t-amharc "
"cineálach :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView` teimpléad "
"réamhshocraithe ar a dtugtar `` <ainm an fheidhmchláir>/<ainm "
"samhail>_list.html``; úsáidimid ``template_name`` "
"chun :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView` a insint chun ár teimpléad "
"reatha ``\"vótaíocht/index.html\"`` a úsáid."

msgid ""
"In previous parts of the tutorial, the templates have been provided with a "
"context that contains the ``question`` and ``latest_question_list`` context "
"variables. For ``DetailView`` the ``question`` variable is provided "
"automatically -- since we're using a Django model (``Question``), Django is "
"able to determine an appropriate name for the context variable. However, for "
"ListView, the automatically generated context variable is ``question_list``. "
"To override this we provide the ``context_object_name`` attribute, "
"specifying that we want to use ``latest_question_list`` instead. As an "
"alternative approach, you could change your templates to match the new "
"default context variables -- but it's a lot easier to tell Django to use the "
"variable you want."
msgstr ""
"I gcodanna roimhe seo den rang teagaisc, cuireadh comhthéacs ar fáil do na "
"teimpléid ina bhfuil na hathróga comhthéacs ``ceist`` agus `` is "
"déanaí_cheist_liosta``. I gcás ``DetailView`` cuirtear an athróg ``ceist`` "
"ar fáil go huathoibríoch -- ós rud é go bhfuil múnla Django in úsáid againn "
"(`` Ceist``), tá Django in ann ainm oiriúnach a chinneadh don athróg "
"comhthéacs. I gcás ListView, áfach, is é ``question_list`` an athróg "
"comhthéacs a ghintear go huathoibríoch. Chun é seo a shárú, cuirimid an "
"aitreabúid ``context_object_name`` ar fáil, ag sonrú go dteastaíonn uainn "
"``liosta_ceisteanna_is déanaí`` a úsáid ina ionad sin. Mar chur chuige eile, "
"d'fhéadfá do theimpléid a athrú chun na hathróga comhthéacs réamhshocraithe "
"nua a mheaitseáil -- ach tá sé i bhfad níos éasca a rá le Django an athróg "
"atá uait a úsáid."

msgid "Run the server, and use your new polling app based on generic views."
msgstr ""
"Rith an freastalaí, agus úsáid d'aip vótaíochta nua bunaithe ar radhairc "
"chineálacha."

msgid ""
"For full details on generic views, see the :doc:`generic views documentation "
"</topics/class-based-views/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Chun sonraí iomlána a fháil ar thuairimí cineálacha, féach "
"an :doc:`doiciméadú tuairimí cineálach </topics/class-based-views/index>`."

msgid ""
"When you're comfortable with forms and generic views, read :doc:`part 5 of "
"this tutorial</intro/tutorial05>` to learn about testing our polls app."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ar do chompord le foirmeacha agus le tuairimí cineálacha, "
"léigh :doc: `cuid 5 den rang teagaisc seo</intro/tutorial05>` chun foghlaim "
"faoinár bhfeidhmchlár pobalbhreithe a thástáil."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 5"
msgstr "Do chéad aip Django a scríobh, cuid 5"

msgid ""
"This tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 4 </intro/tutorial04>` left off. "
"We've built a web-poll application, and we'll now create some automated "
"tests for it."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an rang teagaisc seo nuair a d'fhág :doc:`Tutorial 4 </intro/"
"tutorial04>` as. Tá feidhmchlár vótaíochta gréasáin tógtha againn, agus "
"cruthóimid roinnt tástálacha uathoibrithe dó anois."

msgid "Introducing automated testing"
msgstr "Tástáil uathoibrithe a thabhairt isteach"

msgid "What are automated tests?"
msgstr "Cad is tástálacha uathoibrithe ann?"

msgid "Tests are routines that check the operation of your code."
msgstr "Is gnáthaimh iad tástálacha a sheiceálann oibriú do chóid."

msgid ""
"Testing operates at different levels. Some tests might apply to a tiny "
"detail (*does a particular model method return values as expected?*) while "
"others examine the overall operation of the software (*does a sequence of "
"user inputs on the site produce the desired result?*). That's no different "
"from the kind of testing you did earlier in :doc:`Tutorial 2 </intro/"
"tutorial02>`, using the :djadmin:`shell` to examine the behavior of a "
"method, or running the application and entering data to check how it behaves."
msgstr ""
"Feidhmíonn an tástáil ag leibhéil éagsúla. B’fhéidir go mbainfeadh roinnt "
"tástálacha le mionsonra beag (*an dtugann modh múnla ar leith luachanna mar "
"a bhíothas ag súil leis?*) agus scrúdaíonn cinn eile oibriú iomlán na "
"mbogearraí (*an dtugann seicheamh ionchuir úsáideora ar an suíomh an toradh "
"inmhianaithe?*). Níl sé sin difriúil ón gcineál tástála a rinne tú níos "
"luaithe i :doc:`Teagasc 2 </intro/tutorial02>`, ag baint úsáide as "
"an :djadmin:`shell` chun iompar modha a scrúdú, nó an feidhmchlár a rith "
"agus sonraí a chur isteach chuig seiceáil conas a iompraíonn sé."

msgid ""
"What's different in *automated* tests is that the testing work is done for "
"you by the system. You create a set of tests once, and then as you make "
"changes to your app, you can check that your code still works as you "
"originally intended, without having to perform time consuming manual testing."
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud atá difriúil i dtrialacha *uathoibrithe* ná go ndéanann an córas "
"an obair thástála duitse. Cruthaíonn tú sraith tástálacha uair amháin, agus "
"ansin de réir mar a dhéanann tú athruithe ar d’aip, is féidir leat a "
"sheiceáil go n-oibríonn do chód fós mar a bhí beartaithe agat ar dtús, gan "
"tástáil láimhe am-íditheach a dhéanamh."

msgid "Why you need to create tests"
msgstr "Cén fáth ar gá duit tástálacha a chruthú"

msgid "So why create tests, and why now?"
msgstr "Mar sin cén fáth tástálacha a chruthú, agus cén fáth anois?"

msgid ""
"You may feel that you have quite enough on your plate just learning Python/"
"Django, and having yet another thing to learn and do may seem overwhelming "
"and perhaps unnecessary. After all, our polls application is working quite "
"happily now; going through the trouble of creating automated tests is not "
"going to make it work any better. If creating the polls application is the "
"last bit of Django programming you will ever do, then true, you don't need "
"to know how to create automated tests. But, if that's not the case, now is "
"an excellent time to learn."
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir go mbraitheann tú go bhfuil do dhóthain ar do phláta díreach ag "
"foghlaim Python/Django, agus b'fhéidir go bhfuil cuma ró-mhór agus b'fhéidir "
"nach bhfuil gá le rud eile le foghlaim agus le déanamh. Tar éis an tsaoil, "
"tá ár n-iarratas vótaíochta ag obair go sona sásta anois; ní éireoidh níos "
"fearr leis an deacracht a bhaineann le tástálacha uathoibrithe a chruthú. "
"Más é cruthú an fheidhmchláir vótaíochta an píosa deireanach de ríomhchlárú "
"Django a dhéanfaidh tú riamh, mar sin de, ní gá go mbeadh a fhios agat conas "
"tástálacha uathoibrithe a chruthú. Ach, murab é sin an cás, is am iontach é "
"anois le foghlaim."

msgid "Tests will save you time"
msgstr "Sábhálfaidh tástálacha am duit"

msgid ""
"Up to a certain point, 'checking that it seems to work' will be a "
"satisfactory test. In a more sophisticated application, you might have "
"dozens of complex interactions between components."
msgstr ""
"Go dtí pointe áirithe, beidh 'seiceáil go ndealraíonn sé go n-oibríonn sé' "
"ina thástáil shásúil. I bhfeidhmchlár níos sofaisticiúla, b'fhéidir go "
"mbeadh mórán idirghníomhaíochtaí casta agat idir comhpháirteanna."

msgid ""
"A change in any of those components could have unexpected consequences on "
"the application's behavior. Checking that it still 'seems to work' could "
"mean running through your code's functionality with twenty different "
"variations of your test data to make sure you haven't broken something - not "
"a good use of your time."
msgstr ""
"D’fhéadfadh iarmhairtí gan choinne a bheith ag athrú ar aon cheann de na "
"comhpháirteanna sin ar iompar an fheidhmchláir. D'fhéadfadh sé go gciallódh "
"seiceáil go bhfuil an chuma air go bhfuil sé fós ag obair trí fheidhmiúlacht "
"do chóid le fiche athrú éagsúil ar do shonraí tástála chun a chinntiú nach "
"bhfuil rud éigin briste agat - ní úsáid mhaith é do chuid ama."

msgid ""
"That's especially true when automated tests could do this for you in "
"seconds. If something's gone wrong, tests will also assist in identifying "
"the code that's causing the unexpected behavior."
msgstr ""
"Tá sé sin fíor go háirithe nuair a d'fhéadfadh tástálacha uathoibrithe é seo "
"a dhéanamh duit i soicindí. Má tá rud éigin mícheart, cabhróidh tástálacha "
"freisin chun an cód is cúis leis an iompar gan choinne a aithint."

msgid ""
"Sometimes it may seem a chore to tear yourself away from your productive, "
"creative programming work to face the unglamorous and unexciting business of "
"writing tests, particularly when you know your code is working properly."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta, b’fhéidir go mbeadh an chuma air go mbeadh sé ina chontúirt tú "
"féin a stróiceadh ó do chuid oibre táirgiúla, chruthaitheacha ar "
"chlársceidealú chun aghaidh a thabhairt ar ghnó neamhghlamourous unexciting "
"na dtrialacha scríbhneoireachta, go háirithe nuair a bhíonn a fhios agat go "
"bhfuil do chód ag oibriú i gceart."

msgid ""
"However, the task of writing tests is a lot more fulfilling than spending "
"hours testing your application manually or trying to identify the cause of a "
"newly-introduced problem."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin féin, tá an tasc a bhaineann le tástálacha a scríobh i bhfad níos "
"sásúla ná uaireanta a chaitheamh ag tástáil d'iarratas de láimh nó ag "
"iarraidh cúis na faidhbe nua-thagtha a aithint."

msgid "Tests don't just identify problems, they prevent them"
msgstr ""
"Ní hamháin go n-aithníonn tástálacha fadhbanna, cuireann siad cosc ​​orthu"

msgid ""
"It's a mistake to think of tests merely as a negative aspect of development."
msgstr ""
"Is botún é smaoineamh ar thástálacha mar ghné dhiúltach den fhorbairt amháin."

msgid ""
"Without tests, the purpose or intended behavior of an application might be "
"rather opaque. Even when it's your own code, you will sometimes find "
"yourself poking around in it trying to find out what exactly it's doing."
msgstr ""
"Gan tástálacha, d’fhéadfadh cuspóir nó iompar beartaithe feidhmchlár a "
"bheith sách teimhneach. Fiú nuair is é do chód féin é, uaireanta beidh tú ag "
"sníomh timpeall ann ag iarraidh a fháil amach cad go díreach atá ar siúl "
"aige."

msgid ""
"Tests change that; they light up your code from the inside, and when "
"something goes wrong, they focus light on the part that has gone wrong - "
"*even if you hadn't even realized it had gone wrong*."
msgstr ""
"Athraíonn tástálacha go; lasann siad do chód ón taobh istigh, agus nuair a "
"théann rud éigin mícheart, díríonn siad solas ar an gcuid a chuaigh mícheart "
"- *fiú murar thuig tú fiú go raibh sé imithe amú*."

msgid "Tests make your code more attractive"
msgstr "Déanann tástálacha do chód níos tarraingtí"

msgid ""
"You might have created a brilliant piece of software, but you will find that "
"many other developers will refuse to look at it because it lacks tests; "
"without tests, they won't trust it. Jacob Kaplan-Moss, one of Django's "
"original developers, says \"Code without tests is broken by design.\""
msgstr ""
"B'fhéidir gur chruthaigh tú píosa bogearraí iontach, ach gheobhaidh tú go "
"ndiúltóidh go leor forbróirí eile breathnú air toisc nach bhfuil tástálacha "
"ann; gan tástálacha, ní bheidh muinín acu ann. Deir Jacob Kaplan-Moss, ceann "
"de na forbróirí bunaidh Django, \"Tá Cód gan tástálacha briste de réir "
"dearadh.\""

msgid ""
"That other developers want to see tests in your software before they take it "
"seriously is yet another reason for you to start writing tests."
msgstr ""
"Is cúis eile fós é gur mian le forbróirí eile tástálacha a fheiceáil i do "
"bhogearraí sula nglacfaidh siad dáiríre é chun tús a chur le tástálacha a "
"scríobh."

msgid "Tests help teams work together"
msgstr "Cuidíonn tástálacha le foirne oibriú le chéile"

msgid ""
"The previous points are written from the point of view of a single developer "
"maintaining an application. Complex applications will be maintained by "
"teams. Tests guarantee that colleagues don't inadvertently break your code "
"(and that you don't break theirs without knowing). If you want to make a "
"living as a Django programmer, you must be good at writing tests!"
msgstr ""
"Scríobhtar na pointí roimhe seo ó thaobh forbróra amháin a choinníonn "
"iarratas. Coinneoidh foirne iarratais chasta. Cinntíonn tástálacha nach "
"mbriseann comhghleacaithe do chód de thaisme (agus nach mbriseann tú a gcód "
"i ngan fhios). Más mian leat slí bheatha a dhéanamh mar ríomhchláraitheoir "
"Django, caithfidh tú a bheith go maith ag scríobh trialacha!"

msgid "Basic testing strategies"
msgstr "Straitéisí bunúsacha tástála"

msgid "There are many ways to approach writing tests."
msgstr "Tá go leor bealaí ann le tabhairt faoi thrialacha scríbhneoireachta."

msgid ""
"Some programmers follow a discipline called \"`test-driven development`_\"; "
"they actually write their tests before they write their code. This might "
"seem counterintuitive, but in fact it's similar to what most people will "
"often do anyway: they describe a problem, then create some code to solve it. "
"Test-driven development formalizes the problem in a Python test case."
msgstr ""
"Leanann roinnt ríomhchláraitheoirí disciplín ar a dtugtar \"`forbairt "
"bunaithe ar thástáil`_\"; scríobhann siad a gcuid tástálacha sula scríobhann "
"siad a gcód. D'fhéadfadh sé seo cosúil go míthuigthe, ach i ndáiríre tá sé "
"cosúil leis an méid a bheidh daoine is minic a dhéanamh ar aon nós: siad cur "
"síos ar fhadhb, ansin a chruthú roinnt cód chun é a réiteach. Déanann "
"forbairt tástála-tiomáinte an fhadhb a fhoirmiú i gcás tástála Python."

msgid ""
"More often, a newcomer to testing will create some code and later decide "
"that it should have some tests. Perhaps it would have been better to write "
"some tests earlier, but it's never too late to get started."
msgstr ""
"Níos minice, cruthóidh núíosach sa tástáil roinnt cód agus cinnfidh sé níos "
"déanaí gur chóir go mbeadh roinnt tástálacha ann. B'fhéidir go mbeadh sé "
"níos fearr roinnt tástálacha a scríobh níos luaithe, ach ní bhíonn sé ró-"
"dhéanach chun tús a chur leis."

msgid ""
"Sometimes it's difficult to figure out where to get started with writing "
"tests. If you have written several thousand lines of Python, choosing "
"something to test might not be easy. In such a case, it's fruitful to write "
"your first test the next time you make a change, either when you add a new "
"feature or fix a bug."
msgstr ""
"Uaireanta bíonn sé deacair a dhéanamh amach cá háit le tosú ar thrialacha "
"scríbhneoireachta. Má tá na mílte línte de Python scríofa agat, seans nach "
"mbeadh sé éasca rud éigin a thástáil. I gcás den sórt sin, tá sé torthúil do "
"chéad thástáil a scríobh an chéad uair eile a dhéanann tú athrú, nuair a "
"chuireann tú gné nua leis nó nuair a shocraíonn tú fabht."

msgid "So let's do that right away."
msgstr "Mar sin déanaimis é sin láithreach."

msgid "Writing our first test"
msgstr "Ag scríobh ár gcéad triail"

msgid "We identify a bug"
msgstr "Aithnímid fabht"

msgid ""
"Fortunately, there's a little bug in the ``polls`` application for us to fix "
"right away: the ``Question.was_published_recently()`` method returns "
"``True`` if the ``Question`` was published within the last day (which is "
"correct) but also if the ``Question``’s ``pub_date`` field is in the future "
"(which certainly isn't)."
msgstr ""
"Ar ámharaí an tsaoil, tá fabht beag san fheidhmchlár ``vótaíocht`` atá le "
"réiteach againn ar an bpointe boise: foilsíodh an modh ``Ceist._foilsithe_le "
"déanaí()`` ar ais ``True`` má fhoilsítear an ``Ceist`` laistigh den cheann "
"deireanach lá (atá ceart) ach freisin má tá an réimse ``Question``'s `` "
"pub_date`` amach anseo (rud nach bhfuil cinnte)."

msgid ""
"Confirm the bug by using the :djadmin:`shell` to check the method on a "
"question whose date lies in the future:"
msgstr ""
"Deimhnigh an fabht tríd an :djadmin:`shell` a úsáid chun an modh a sheiceáil "
"ar cheist a bhfuil a dáta sa todhchaí:"

msgid "Since things in the future are not 'recent', this is clearly wrong."
msgstr ""
"Ós rud é nach bhfuil rudaí sa todhchaí 'le déanaí', is léir go bhfuil sé seo "
"mícheart."

msgid "Create a test to expose the bug"
msgstr "Cruthaigh tástáil chun an fabht a nochtadh"

msgid ""
"What we've just done in the :djadmin:`shell` to test for the problem is "
"exactly what we can do in an automated test, so let's turn that into an "
"automated test."
msgstr ""
"Is é an rud atá díreach déanta againn sa :djadmin:`shell` chun tástáil a "
"dhéanamh ar an bhfadhb ná an rud go díreach is féidir linn a dhéanamh i "
"dtástáil uathoibrithe, mar sin déanaimis tástáil uathoibrithe air sin."

msgid ""
"A conventional place for an application's tests is in the application's "
"``tests.py`` file; the testing system will automatically find tests in any "
"file whose name begins with ``test``."
msgstr ""
"Gnátháit do thástálacha feidhmchláir is ea comhad ``tests.py`` an "
"fheidhmchláir; Gheobhaidh an córas tástála tástálacha go huathoibríoch in "
"aon chomhad a dtosaíonn a ainm le ``tástáil``."

msgid ""
"Put the following in the ``tests.py`` file in the ``polls`` application:"
msgstr ""
"Cuir iad seo a leanas sa chomhad ``tests.py`` san fheidhmchlár ``polls``:"

msgid "``polls/tests.py``"
msgstr "``polls/tests.py``"

msgid ""
"Here we have created a :class:`django.test.TestCase` subclass with a method "
"that creates a ``Question`` instance with a ``pub_date`` in the future. We "
"then check the output of ``was_published_recently()`` - which *ought* to be "
"False."
msgstr ""
"Tá fo-aicme :class:`django.test.TestCase` cruthaithe againn anseo le modh a "
"chruthaíonn sampla ``Ceist`` le ``dáta_ tábhairne`` sa todhchaí. Déanaimid "
"seiceáil ansin ar aschur ``foilsíodh_le déanaí()`` - ar cheart * a bheith "
"Bréagach."

msgid "Running tests"
msgstr "Rith tástálacha"

msgid "In the terminal, we can run our test:"
msgstr "Sa chríochfort, is féidir linn ár dtástáil a rith:"

msgid "and you'll see something like:"
msgstr "agus feicfidh tú rud éigin mar:"

msgid "Different error?"
msgstr "Earráid dhifriúil?"

msgid ""
"If instead you're getting a ``NameError`` here, you may have missed a step "
"in :ref:`Part 2 <tutorial02-import-timezone>` where we added imports of "
"``datetime`` and ``timezone`` to ``polls/models.py``. Copy the imports from "
"that section, and try running your tests again."
msgstr ""
"Más rud é ina ionad sin go bhfuil ``Earráid Ainm`` á fháil agat anseo, seans "
"gur chaill tú céim i :ref:`Cuid 2 <tutorial02-import-timezone>` inar "
"chuireamar iompórtálacha de ``datetime`` agus ``timezone` `go dtí``vótaíocht/"
"samhlacha.py``. Cóipeáil na hiompórtálacha ón rannán sin, agus bain triail "
"as do thástálacha a rith arís."

msgid "What happened is this:"
msgstr "Cad a tharla é seo:"

msgid "``manage.py test polls`` looked for tests in the ``polls`` application"
msgstr ""
"D'fhéach ``manage.py test polls`` tástálacha san fheidhmchlár ``polls``"

msgid "it found a subclass of the :class:`django.test.TestCase` class"
msgstr "fuair sé fo-aicme den rang :rang:`django.test.TestCase`"

msgid "it created a special database for the purpose of testing"
msgstr "chruthaigh sé bunachar sonraí speisialta chun críche tástála"

msgid "it looked for test methods - ones whose names begin with ``test``"
msgstr ""
"d'fhéach sé le haghaidh modhanna tástála - cinn a bhfuil a n-ainmneacha tús "
"le ``test``"

msgid ""
"in ``test_was_published_recently_with_future_question`` it created a "
"``Question`` instance whose ``pub_date`` field is 30 days in the future"
msgstr ""
"i ``tástáil_foilsithe_le_déanaí_le_cheist_future_`` chruthaigh sé ``Ceist`` "
"a bhfuil réimse `` pub_date`` 30 lá sa todhchaí"

msgid ""
"... and using the ``assertIs()`` method, it discovered that its "
"``was_published_recently()`` returns ``True``, though we wanted it to return "
"``False``"
msgstr ""
"... agus úsáid á baint as an modh ``assertIs()``, fuair sé amach go dtagann "
"``True`` ar ais lena ``was_published_recently()``, cé gur theastaigh uainn "
"go dtabharfadh sé ``False`"

msgid ""
"The test informs us which test failed and even the line on which the failure "
"occurred."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann an tástáil in iúl dúinn cén tástáil ar theip uirthi agus fiú an "
"líne ar ar tharla an teip."

msgid "Fixing the bug"
msgstr "An fabht a shocrú"

msgid ""
"We already know what the problem is: ``Question.was_published_recently()`` "
"should return ``False`` if its ``pub_date`` is in the future. Amend the "
"method in ``models.py``, so that it will only return ``True`` if the date is "
"also in the past:"
msgstr ""
"Tá a fhios againn cheana féin cad é an fhadhb: "
"``Question.was_published_recently()`` ba cheart ``False`` a thabhairt ar ais "
"má tá a ``dpub_date`` amach anseo. Leasaigh an modh i ``models.py``, ionas "
"nach dtabharfaidh sé ar ais ``True`` ach amháin má tá an dáta san am atá "
"caite freisin:"

msgid "and run the test again:"
msgstr "agus rith an triail arís:"

msgid ""
"After identifying a bug, we wrote a test that exposes it and corrected the "
"bug in the code so our test passes."
msgstr ""
"Tar éis fabht a aithint, scríobhamar tástáil a nochtar é agus cheartaigh "
"muid an fabht sa chód ionas go n-éireoidh linn ár dtástáil."

msgid ""
"Many other things might go wrong with our application in the future, but we "
"can be sure that we won't inadvertently reintroduce this bug, because "
"running the test will warn us immediately. We can consider this little "
"portion of the application pinned down safely forever."
msgstr ""
"D’fhéadfadh go n-imeodh go leor rudaí eile lenár n-iarratas amach anseo, ach "
"is féidir linn a bheith cinnte nach dtabharfaimid an fabht seo isteach arís "
"go neamhaireach, mar go dtabharfaidh rith na tástála rabhadh dúinn "
"láithreach. Is féidir linn a mheas go bhfuil an chuid bheag seo den iarratas "
"pinn síos go sábháilte go deo."

msgid "More comprehensive tests"
msgstr "Tástálacha níos cuimsithí"

msgid ""
"While we're here, we can further pin down the ``was_published_recently()`` "
"method; in fact, it would be positively embarrassing if in fixing one bug we "
"had introduced another."
msgstr ""
"Agus muid anseo, is féidir linn an modh ``foilsíodh_le déanaí()``; go "
"deimhin, bheadh ​​sé ina náire dearfach dá mbeadh fabht amháin tugtha isteach "
"againn agus fabht amháin á réiteach."

msgid ""
"Add two more test methods to the same class, to test the behavior of the "
"method more comprehensively:"
msgstr ""
"Cuir dhá mhodh tástála eile leis an rang céanna, chun iompar an mhodha a "
"thástáil ar bhealach níos cuimsithí:"

msgid ""
"And now we have three tests that confirm that "
"``Question.was_published_recently()`` returns sensible values for past, "
"recent, and future questions."
msgstr ""
"Agus anois tá trí thástáil againn a dheimhníonn go dtugann "
"``Question.was_published_recently()`` luachanna ciallmhara do cheisteanna "
"san am a chuaigh thart, do cheisteanna le déanaí agus don todhchaí."

msgid ""
"Again, ``polls`` is a minimal application, but however complex it grows in "
"the future and whatever other code it interacts with, we now have some "
"guarantee that the method we have written tests for will behave in expected "
"ways."
msgstr ""
"Arís, is feidhmchlár íosta é ``vótaíocht``, ach cé chomh casta a fhásann sé "
"sa todhchaí agus cibé cód eile a n-idirghníomhaíonn sé leis, tá ráthaíocht "
"éigin againn anois go n-iomprófar an modh a bhfuil trialacha scríofa againn "
"dó ar bhealaí ionchais."

msgid "Test a view"
msgstr "Tástáil radharc"

msgid ""
"The polls application is fairly undiscriminating: it will publish any "
"question, including ones whose ``pub_date`` field lies in the future. We "
"should improve this. Setting a ``pub_date`` in the future should mean that "
"the Question is published at that moment, but invisible until then."
msgstr ""
"Tá an t-iarratas pobalbhreithe cothrom neamh-idirdhealaitheach: foilseoidh "
"sé aon cheist, lena n-áirítear na cinn a bhfuil a réimse ``pub_date`` suite "
"amach anseo. Ba cheart dúinn é seo a fheabhsú. Ba cheart go gciallódh socrú "
"``pub_date`` amach anseo go bhfoilseofar an Cheist ag an nóiméad sin, ach "
"dofheicthe go dtí sin."

msgid "A test for a view"
msgstr "Tástáil le haghaidh radharc"

msgid ""
"When we fixed the bug above, we wrote the test first and then the code to "
"fix it. In fact that was an example of test-driven development, but it "
"doesn't really matter in which order we do the work."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a shocraíomar an fabht thuas, scríobhamar an tástáil ar dtús agus "
"ansin an cód chun é a shocrú. Le fírinne ba shampla é sin d’fhorbairt a bhí "
"tiomáinte ag tástáil, ach is cuma i ndáiríre cén ord ina ndéanaimid an obair."

msgid ""
"In our first test, we focused closely on the internal behavior of the code. "
"For this test, we want to check its behavior as it would be experienced by a "
"user through a web browser."
msgstr ""
"In ár gcéad tástáil, dhíríomar go dlúth ar iompar inmheánach an chóid. Don "
"tástáil seo, ba mhaith linn a iompar a sheiceáil mar a bheadh ​​taithí ag "
"úsáideoir air trí bhrabhsálaí gréasáin."

msgid ""
"Before we try to fix anything, let's have a look at the tools at our "
"disposal."
msgstr ""
"Sula ndéanaimid iarracht rud ar bith a shocrú, caithfimid féachaint ar na "
"huirlisí atá ar fáil dúinn."

msgid "The Django test client"
msgstr "Django cliant tástála"

msgid ""
"Django provides a test :class:`~django.test.Client` to simulate a user "
"interacting with the code at the view level.  We can use it in ``tests.py`` "
"or even in the :djadmin:`shell`."
msgstr ""
"Soláthraíonn Django tástáil :rang:`~django.test.Client` chun úsáideoir a "
"idirghníomhaíonn leis an gcód ag an leibhéal radhairc a insamhail. Is féidir "
"linn é a úsáid i ``tests.py`` nó fiú sa :djadmin:`shell`."

msgid ""
"We will start again with the :djadmin:`shell`, where we need to do a couple "
"of things that won't be necessary in ``tests.py``. The first is to set up "
"the test environment in the :djadmin:`shell`:"
msgstr ""
"Tosóimid arís leis an :djadmin:`shell`, áit a mbeidh orainn cúpla rud a "
"dhéanamh nach mbeidh riachtanach i ``tests.py``. Is é an chéad cheann ná an "
"timpeallacht tástála a shocrú sa :djadmin:`shell`:"

msgid ""
":meth:`~django.test.utils.setup_test_environment` installs a template "
"renderer which will allow us to examine some additional attributes on "
"responses such as ``response.context`` that otherwise wouldn't be available. "
"Note that this method *does not* set up a test database, so the following "
"will be run against the existing database and the output may differ slightly "
"depending on what questions you already created. You might get unexpected "
"results if your ``TIME_ZONE`` in ``settings.py`` isn't correct. If you don't "
"remember setting it earlier, check it before continuing."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~django.test.utils.setup_test_environment` suiteáil rindreálaí "
"teimpléid a ligfidh dúinn scrúdú a dhéanamh ar roinnt tréithe breise ar "
"fhreagraí ar nós ``response.context`` nach mbeadh ar fáil murach sin. "
"Tabhair faoi deara nach mbunaíonn an modh seo ** bunachar sonraí tástála, "
"mar sin cuirfear an méid seo a leanas i gcomparáid leis an mbunachar sonraí "
"atá ann cheana féin agus d’fhéadfadh go mbeadh difríocht bheag idir an t-"
"aschur ag brath ar na ceisteanna a chruthaigh tú cheana féin. Seans go "
"bhfaighidh tú torthaí gan choinne mura bhfuil do ``TIME_ZONE`` i "
"``settings.py`` ceart. Mura cuimhin leat é a shocrú níos luaithe, seiceáil é "
"sula leanann tú ar aghaidh."

msgid ""
"Next we need to import the test client class (later in ``tests.py`` we will "
"use the :class:`django.test.TestCase` class, which comes with its own "
"client, so this won't be required):"
msgstr ""
"Ansin ní mór dúinn an rang cliant tástála a iompórtáil (níos déanaí i "
"``tests.py`` úsáidfimid an rang ::`django.test.TestCase`, a thagann lena "
"cliant féin, mar sin ní bheidh sé seo ag teastáil) :"

msgid "With that ready, we can ask the client to do some work for us:"
msgstr ""
"Agus é sin réidh, is féidir linn iarraidh ar an gcliant roinnt oibre a "
"dhéanamh dúinn:"

msgid "Improving our view"
msgstr "Ár dtuairim a fheabhsú"

msgid ""
"The list of polls shows polls that aren't published yet (i.e. those that "
"have a ``pub_date`` in the future). Let's fix that."
msgstr ""
"Léiríonn liosta na pobalbhreithe pobalbhreith nach bhfuil foilsithe fós "
"(i.e. iad siúd a mbeidh ``dáta_ tábhairne`` acu amach anseo). Déanaimis é "
"sin a shocrú."

msgid ""
"In :doc:`Tutorial 4 </intro/tutorial04>` we introduced a class-based view, "
"based on :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView`:"
msgstr ""
"In :doc:`Teagasc 4 </intro/tutorial04>` thugamar isteach radharc rang-"
"bhunaithe, bunaithe ar :class:`~django.views.generic.list.ListView`:"

msgid ""
"We need to amend the ``get_queryset()`` method and change it so that it also "
"checks the date by comparing it with ``timezone.now()``. First we need to "
"add an import:"
msgstr ""
"Ní mór dúinn an modh ``get_queryset()`` a leasú agus é a athrú ionas go "
"seiceálann sé an dáta freisin trí é a chur i gcomparáid le "
"``timezone.now()``. Ar dtús caithfimid allmhairiú a chur leis:"

msgid "and then we must amend the ``get_queryset`` method like so:"
msgstr "agus ansin caithfimid an modh ``get_queryset`` a leasú mar seo:"

msgid ""
"``Question.objects.filter(pub_date__lte=timezone.now())`` returns a queryset "
"containing ``Question``\\s whose ``pub_date`` is less than or equal to - "
"that is, earlier than or equal to - ``timezone.now()``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing our new view"
msgstr "Ár radharc nua a thástáil"

msgid ""
"Now you can satisfy yourself that this behaves as expected by firing up "
"``runserver``, loading the site in your browser, creating a few ``Question`` "
"entries with dates in the past and future, and checking that only those that "
"have been published are listed. You don't want to have to do that *every "
"single time you make any change that might affect this* - so let's also "
"create a test, based on our :djadmin:`shell` session above."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the following to ``polls/tests.py``:"
msgstr "Cuir iad seo a leanas le ``polls/tests.py``:"

msgid ""
"and we'll create a shortcut function to create questions as well as a new "
"test class:"
msgstr ""
"agus cruthóimid feidhm aicearra chun ceisteanna a chruthú chomh maith le "
"rang tástála nua:"

msgid "Let's look at some of these more closely."
msgstr "Breathnaímis ar chuid acu seo níos mine."

msgid ""
"First is a question shortcut function, ``create_question``, to take some "
"repetition out of the process of creating questions."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús tá feidhm aicearra ceisteanna, ``cruthaigh_cheist``, chun roinnt "
"athrá a bhaint as an bpróiseas chun ceisteanna a chruthú."

msgid ""
"``test_no_questions`` doesn't create any questions, but checks the message: "
"\"No polls are available.\" and verifies the ``latest_question_list`` is "
"empty. Note that the :class:`django.test.TestCase` class provides some "
"additional assertion methods. In these examples, we "
"use :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertContains()` "
"and :meth:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.assertQuerySetEqual()`."
msgstr ""
"Ní chruthaíonn ``test_no_questions`` aon cheist, ach seiceálann sé an "
"teachtaireacht: \"Níl aon pobalbhreith ar fáil.\" agus fíoraíonn sé go "
"bhfuil ``liosta_ceisteanna_is déanaí`` folamh. Tabhair faoi deara go "
"soláthraíonn an rang :rang:`django.test.TestCase` roinnt modhanna "
"dearbhaithe breise. Sna samplaí seo, "
"úsáidimid :meth:`~django.test.SimpleTestCase.assertContains()` "
"agus :meth:`~django.test.TransactionTestCase.assertQuerySetEqual()`."

msgid ""
"In ``test_past_question``, we create a question and verify that it appears "
"in the list."
msgstr ""
"In ``test_past_question``, cruthaímid ceist agus deimhnímid go bhfuil sé le "
"feiceáil ar an liosta."

msgid ""
"In ``test_future_question``, we create a question with a ``pub_date`` in the "
"future. The database is reset for each test method, so the first question is "
"no longer there, and so again the index shouldn't have any questions in it."
msgstr ""
"I ``test_future_question``, cruthaímid ceist le ``dáta_tábhairne`` amach "
"anseo. Athshocraítear an bunachar sonraí do gach modh tástála, mar sin níl "
"an chéad cheist ann a thuilleadh, agus mar sin arís níor cheart go mbeadh "
"aon cheist san innéacs."

msgid ""
"And so on. In effect, we are using the tests to tell a story of admin input "
"and user experience on the site, and checking that at every state and for "
"every new change in the state of the system, the expected results are "
"published."
msgstr ""
"Agus mar sin de. I ndáiríre, táimid ag baint úsáide as na tástálacha chun "
"scéal ionchur admin agus taithí úsáideora ar an suíomh a insint, agus ag "
"seiceáil go bhfuil ag gach stát agus le haghaidh gach athrú nua ar staid an "
"chórais, foilsítear na torthaí ionchais."

msgid "Testing the ``DetailView``"
msgstr "Ag tástáil an ``DetailView``"

msgid ""
"What we have works well; however, even though future questions don't appear "
"in the *index*, users can still reach them if they know or guess the right "
"URL. So we need to add a similar  constraint to ``DetailView``:"
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn an méid atá againn go maith; ach, cé nach bhfuil ceisteanna amach "
"anseo le feiceáil san *innéacs*, is féidir le húsáideoirí iad a bhaint amach "
"má tá an URL ceart ar eolas acu nó má dhéanann siad buille faoi thuairim. "
"Mar sin caithfimid srian den chineál céanna a chur le ``DetailView``:"

msgid ""
"We should then add some tests, to check that a ``Question`` whose "
"``pub_date`` is in the past can be displayed, and that one with a "
"``pub_date`` in the future is not:"
msgstr ""
"Ba cheart dúinn roinnt tástálacha a chur leis ansin, lena chinntiú gur "
"féidir ``Ceist`` a bhfuil a ``dáta_ tábhairne`` san am a chuaigh thart a "
"thaispeáint, agus nach bhfuil ceann le ``dáta_ tábhairne`` amach anseo:"

msgid "Ideas for more tests"
msgstr "Smaointe le haghaidh tástálacha níos mó"

msgid ""
"We ought to add a similar ``get_queryset`` method to ``ResultsView`` and "
"create a new test class for that view. It'll be very similar to what we have "
"just created; in fact there will be a lot of repetition."
msgstr ""
"Ba chóir dúinn modh cosúil le ``get_queryset`` a chur le ``ResultsView`` "
"agus rang tástála nua a chruthú don amharc sin. Beidh sé an-chosúil leis an "
"rud atá díreach cruthaithe againn; i ndáiríre beidh go leor athrá."

msgid ""
"We could also improve our application in other ways, adding tests along the "
"way. For example, it's pointless that a ``Question`` with no related "
"``Choice`` can be published on the site. So, our views could check for this, "
"and exclude such ``Question`` objects. Our tests would create a ``Question`` "
"without a ``Choice``, and then test that it's not published, as well as "
"create a similar ``Question`` *with* at least one ``Choice``, and test that "
"it *is* published."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Perhaps logged-in admin users should be allowed to see unpublished "
"``Question`` entries, but not ordinary visitors. Again: whatever needs to be "
"added to the software to accomplish this should be accompanied by a test, "
"whether you write the test first and then make the code pass the test, or "
"work out the logic in your code first and then write a test to prove it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At a certain point you are bound to look at your tests and wonder whether "
"your code is suffering from test bloat, which brings us to:"
msgstr ""
"Ag pointe áirithe caithfidh tú breathnú ar do thástálacha agus smaoineamh an "
"bhfuil do chód thíos le bloat tástála, rud a thugann dúinn:"

msgid "When testing, more is better"
msgstr "Nuair a dhéantar tástáil, tá níos mó níos fearr"

msgid ""
"It might seem that our tests are growing out of control. At this rate there "
"will soon be more code in our tests than in our application, and the "
"repetition is unaesthetic, compared to the elegant conciseness of the rest "
"of our code."
msgstr ""
"D’fhéadfadh sé a bheith cosúil go bhfuil ár gcuid tástálacha ag éirí as "
"smacht. Ag an ráta seo ní fada go mbeidh níos mó cód inár dtástálacha ná mar "
"atá inár bhfeidhmchlár, agus ní bheidh an t-athrá athrá, i gcomparáid le "
"beacht galánta an chuid eile dár gcód."

msgid ""
"**It doesn't matter**. Let them grow. For the most part, you can write a "
"test once and then forget about it. It will continue performing its useful "
"function as you continue to develop your program."
msgstr ""
"**Is cuma**. Lig dóibh fás. Don chuid is mó, is féidir leat triail a scríobh "
"uair amháin agus ansin déan dearmad faoi. Leanfaidh sé ag feidhmiú a fheidhm "
"úsáideach de réir mar a leanann tú ar aghaidh ag forbairt do chláir."

msgid ""
"Sometimes tests will need to be updated. Suppose that we amend our views so "
"that only ``Question`` entries with associated ``Choice`` instances are "
"published. In that case, many of our existing tests will fail - *telling us "
"exactly which tests need to be amended to bring them up to date*, so to that "
"extent tests help look after themselves."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At worst, as you continue developing, you might find that you have some "
"tests that are now redundant. Even that's not a problem; in testing "
"redundancy is a *good* thing."
msgstr ""
"Ar an gceann is measa, agus tú ag leanúint ar aghaidh ag forbairt, b’fhéidir "
"go bhfaighidh tú amach go bhfuil roinnt tástálacha agat nach bhfuil gá leo "
"anois. Fiú ní fadhb í sin; is rud *mhaith* é iomarcaíocht a thástáil."

msgid ""
"As long as your tests are sensibly arranged, they won't become unmanageable. "
"Good rules-of-thumb include having:"
msgstr ""
"Chomh fada agus a bheidh do thástálacha socraithe go ciallmhar, ní bheidh "
"siad inbhainistithe. I measc na rialacha maithe tá:"

msgid "a separate ``TestClass`` for each model or view"
msgstr "``TestClass`` ar leith do gach samhail nó radharc"

msgid "a separate test method for each set of conditions you want to test"
msgstr ""
"modh tástála ar leith do gach sraith coinníollacha is mian leat a thástáil"

msgid "test method names that describe their function"
msgstr "ainmneacha modhanna tástála a chuireann síos ar a bhfeidhm"

msgid "Further testing"
msgstr "Tástáil bhreise"

msgid ""
"This tutorial only introduces some of the basics of testing. There's a great "
"deal more you can do, and a number of very useful tools at your disposal to "
"achieve some very clever things."
msgstr ""
"Ní thugann an rang teagaisc seo isteach ach cuid de bhunghnéithe na tástála. "
"Tá i bhfad níos mó is féidir leat a dhéanamh, agus roinnt uirlisí an-"
"úsáideach ar fáil duit chun roinnt rudaí an-chliste a bhaint amach."

msgid ""
"For example, while our tests here have covered some of the internal logic of "
"a model and the way our views publish information, you can use an \"in-"
"browser\" framework such as Selenium_ to test the way your HTML actually "
"renders in a browser. These tools allow you to check not just the behavior "
"of your Django code, but also, for example, of your JavaScript. It's quite "
"something to see the tests launch a browser, and start interacting with your "
"site, as if a human being were driving it! Django "
"includes :class:`~django.test.LiveServerTestCase` to facilitate integration "
"with tools like Selenium."
msgstr ""
"Mar shampla, cé gur chlúdaigh ár dtástálacha anseo cuid de loighic "
"inmheánach múnla agus an chaoi a bhfoilsíonn ár dtuairimí faisnéis, is "
"féidir leat creat \"i-bhrabhsálaí\" a úsáid mar Selenium_ chun an bealach a "
"rindreálann do HTML i mbrabhsálaí a thástáil. Ligeann na huirlisí seo duit "
"ní hamháin iompar do chód Django a sheiceáil, ach freisin, mar shampla, do "
"JavaScript. Is fiú go mór na tástálacha a fheiceáil ag seoladh brabhsálaí, "
"agus tosú ag idirghníomhú le do shuíomh, amhail is dá mba duine daonna é! "
"Áirítear le Django :rang:`~django.test.LiveServerTestCase` chun comhtháthú "
"le huirlisí cosúil le Seiléiniam a éascú."

msgid ""
"If you have a complex application, you may want to run tests automatically "
"with every commit for the purposes of `continuous integration`_, so that "
"quality control is itself - at least partially - automated."
msgstr ""
"Má tá feidhmchlár casta agat, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat tástálacha a rith go "
"huathoibríoch le gach gealltanas chun críocha `comhtháthú leanúnach`_, ionas "
"go mbeidh rialú cáilíochta ann féin - go páirteach ar a laghad - "
"uathoibrithe."

msgid ""
"A good way to spot untested parts of your application is to check code "
"coverage. This also helps identify fragile or even dead code. If you can't "
"test a piece of code, it usually means that code should be refactored or "
"removed. Coverage will help to identify dead code. See :ref:`topics-testing-"
"code-coverage` for details."
msgstr ""
"Bealach maith le codanna de d’iarratas nár tástáladh a fheiceáil ná clúdach "
"an chóid a sheiceáil. Cuidíonn sé seo freisin le cód leochaileach nó fiú "
"marbh a aithint. Mura bhfuil tú in ann píosa cód a thástáil, is gnách go "
"gciallaíonn sé gur cheart an cód a athmhacrú nó a bhaint. Cabhróidh clúdach "
"le cód marbh a aithint. Féach :tag:`topics-testing-code-coverage` le "
"haghaidh sonraí."

msgid ""
":doc:`Testing in Django </topics/testing/index>` has comprehensive "
"information about testing."
msgstr ""
":doc:`Testing in Django </topics/testing/index>` tá faisnéis chuimsitheach "
"faoi thástáil."

msgid "What's next?"
msgstr "Cad atá romhainn?"

msgid ""
"For full details on testing, see :doc:`Testing in Django </topics/testing/"
"index>`."
msgstr ""
"Chun sonraí iomlána na tástála a fháil, féach :doc:`Testing in Django </"
"topics/testing/index>`."

msgid ""
"When you're comfortable with testing Django views, read :doc:`part 6 of this "
"tutorial</intro/tutorial06>` to learn about static files management."
msgstr ""
"Agus tú ar do chompord le tuairimí Django a thástáil, léigh :doc:`cuid 6 den "
"rang teagaisc seo</intro/tutorial06>` chun foghlaim faoi bhainistiú comhad "
"statach."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 6"
msgstr "Do chéad aip Django a scríobh, cuid 6"

msgid ""
"This tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 5 </intro/tutorial05>` left off. "
"We've built a tested web-poll application, and we'll now add a stylesheet "
"and an image."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an rang teagaisc seo nuair a d'fhág :doc:`Tutorial 5 </intro/"
"tutorial05>` as. Tá feidhmchlár tástála vótaíochta déanta againn, agus "
"cuirfimid stílbhileog agus íomhá leis anois."

msgid ""
"Aside from the HTML generated by the server, web applications generally need "
"to serve additional files — such as images, JavaScript, or CSS — necessary "
"to render the complete web page. In Django, we refer to these files as "
"\"static files\"."
msgstr ""
"Seachas an HTML a ghineann an freastalaí, is gnách go gcaithfidh "
"feidhmchláir ghréasáin comhaid bhreise a sheirbheáil - mar íomhánna, "
"JavaScript, nó CSS ​​- atá riachtanach chun an leathanach gréasáin iomlán a "
"sholáthar. I Django, déanaimid tagairt do na comhaid seo mar \"comhaid "
"statacha\"."

msgid ""
"For small projects, this isn't a big deal, because you can keep the static "
"files somewhere your web server can find it. However, in bigger projects -- "
"especially those comprised of multiple apps -- dealing with the multiple "
"sets of static files provided by each application starts to get tricky."
msgstr ""
"Maidir le tionscadail bheaga, ní mór é seo, mar is féidir leat na comhaid "
"statacha a choinneáil áit éigin ar féidir le do fhreastalaí gréasáin é a "
"aimsiú. Mar sin féin, i dtionscadail mhóra -- go háirithe iad siúd atá "
"comhdhéanta d' aipeanna iolracha -- ní bhíonn sé deacair déileáil leis na "
"tacair iolracha de chomhaid statacha a sholáthraíonn gach feidhmchlár."

msgid ""
"That's what ``django.contrib.staticfiles`` is for: it collects static files "
"from each of your applications (and any other places you specify) into a "
"single location that can easily be served in production."
msgstr ""
"Sin a bhfuil i gceist le ``django.contrib.staticfiles``: bailíonn sé comhaid "
"statacha ó gach ceann de d'fheidhmchláir (agus aon áiteanna eile a "
"shonraíonn tú) in aon áit amháin ar féidir freastal orthu go héasca i "
"dtáirgeadh."

msgid "Customize your *app's* look and feel"
msgstr "Saincheap cuma agus mothú do *app's*"

msgid ""
"First, create a directory called ``static`` in your ``polls`` directory. "
"Django will look for static files there, similarly to how Django finds "
"templates inside ``polls/templates/``."
msgstr ""
"Ar dtús, cruthaigh eolaire ar a dtugtar ``static`` i do eolaire `` "
"pobalbhreith``. Féachfaidh Django le haghaidh comhaid statacha ann, mar an "
"gcéanna leis an gcaoi a bhfaighidh Django teimpléid taobh istigh de `` "
"pobalbhreith / teimpléid / ``."

msgid ""
"Django's :setting:`STATICFILES_FINDERS` setting contains a list of finders "
"that know how to discover static files from various sources. One of the "
"defaults is ``AppDirectoriesFinder`` which looks for a \"static\" "
"subdirectory in each of the :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS`, like the one in "
"``polls`` we just created. The admin site uses the same directory structure "
"for its static files."
msgstr ""
"Tá liosta aimsitheoirí i suíomh Django:`STATICFILES_FINDERS` a bhfuil a "
"fhios acu conas comhaid statacha a aimsiú ó fhoinsí éagsúla. Is é ceann de "
"na réamhshocruithe ná ``AppDirectoriesFinder`` a lorgaíonn fochomhadlann "
"\"statach\" i ngach ceann de na :socrú:`INSTALLED_APPS`, cosúil leis an "
"gceann i `` pobalbhreith `` a chruthaigh muid díreach. Úsáideann an "
"láithreán riaracháin an struchtúr eolaire céanna dá chomhaid statacha."

msgid ""
"Within the ``static`` directory you have just created, create another "
"directory called ``polls`` and within that create a file called "
"``style.css``. In other words, your stylesheet should be at ``polls/static/"
"polls/style.css``. Because of how the ``AppDirectoriesFinder`` staticfile "
"finder works, you can refer to this static file in Django as ``polls/"
"style.css``, similar to how you reference the path for templates."
msgstr ""
"Laistigh den eolaire ``static`` atá díreach cruthaithe agat, cruthaigh "
"eolaire eile ar a dtugtar `` pobalbhreith`` agus taobh istigh de sin "
"cruthaigh comhad ar a dtugtar ``style.css``. Is é sin le rá, ba chóir go "
"mbeadh do stílbhileog ag ``vótaíocht/statach/toghcháin/stíl.css``. Mar "
"gheall ar an gcaoi a n-oibríonn an aimsitheoir comhad statach `` "
"AppDirectoriesFinder`, is féidir leat tagairt a dhéanamh don chomhad statach "
"seo in Django mar `` pobalbhreith / style.css``, cosúil leis an gcaoi a "
"ndéanann tú tagairt don chonair do theimpléid."

msgid "Static file namespacing"
msgstr "Spásáil ainmneacha comhad statach"

msgid ""
"Just like templates, we *might* be able to get away with putting our static "
"files directly in ``polls/static`` (rather than creating another ``polls`` "
"subdirectory), but it would actually be a bad idea. Django will choose the "
"first static file it finds whose name matches, and if you had a static file "
"with the same name in a *different* application, Django would be unable to "
"distinguish between them. We need to be able to point Django at the right "
"one, and the best way to ensure this is by *namespacing* them. That is, by "
"putting those static files inside *another* directory named for the "
"application itself."
msgstr ""
"Díreach cosúil le teimpléid, * d'fhéadfadh * * a bheith in ann a fháil amach "
"lenár comhaid statach a chur go díreach i `` pobalbhreith / statach`` "
"(seachas a chruthú eile `` pobalbhreith `` fochomhadlann), ach bheadh ​​​​sé i "
"ndáiríre droch-smaoineamh. Roghnóidh Django an chéad chomhad statach a "
"aimsíonn sé a bhfuil a ainm ag teacht leis, agus dá mbeadh comhad statach "
"agat leis an ainm céanna in iarratas *difriúil*, ní bheadh ​​Django in ann "
"idirdhealú a dhéanamh eatarthu. Ní mór dúinn a bheith in ann Django a dhíriú "
"ar an gceann ceart, agus is é an bealach is fearr lena chinntiú ná *spásáil "
"* orthu. Is é sin, trí na comhaid statacha sin a chur taobh istigh de * "
"eolaire * eile atá ainmnithe don fheidhmchlár féin."

msgid ""
"Put the following code in that stylesheet (``polls/static/polls/style.css``):"
msgstr ""
"Cuir an cód seo a leanas sa stílbhileog sin (``polls/static/polls/"
"style.css``):"

msgid "``polls/static/polls/style.css``"
msgstr "``polls/static/polls/style.css``"

msgid ""
"Next, add the following at the top of ``polls/templates/polls/index.html``:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cuir an méid seo a leanas leis ag barr ``polls/templates/polls/"
"index.html``:"

msgid ""
"The ``{% static %}`` template tag generates the absolute URL of static files."
msgstr ""
"Gineann an chlib teimpléid ``{ % static %}`` URL iomlán na gcomhad statacha."

msgid "That's all you need to do for development."
msgstr "Sin go léir is gá duit a dhéanamh le haghaidh forbartha."

msgid "Start the server (or restart it if it's already running):"
msgstr "Tosaigh an freastalaí (nó atosú má tá sé ag rith cheana):"

msgid ""
"Reload ``http://localhost:8000/polls/`` and you should see that the question "
"links are green (Django style!) which means that your stylesheet was "
"properly loaded."
msgstr ""
"Athlódáil `` http://localhost:8000/polls/`` agus ba chóir duit a fheiceáil "
"go bhfuil na naisc cheist glas (stíl Django!) a chiallaíonn go raibh do "
"stílbhileog luchtaithe i gceart."

msgid "Adding a background-image"
msgstr "Íomhá chúlra á cur leis"

msgid ""
"Next, we'll create a subdirectory for images. Create an ``images`` "
"subdirectory in the ``polls/static/polls/`` directory. Inside this "
"directory, add any image file that you'd like to use as a background. For "
"the purposes of this tutorial, we're using a file named ``background.png``, "
"which will have the full path ``polls/static/polls/images/background.png``."
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cruthóimid fochomhadlann le haghaidh íomhánna. Cruthaigh "
"fochomhadlann ``images`` san eolaire `` polls/static/polls/ ``. Taobh istigh "
"den eolaire seo, cuir aon chomhad íomhá ar mhaith leat a úsáid mar chúlra. "
"Chun críocha an teagaisc seo, táimid ag baint úsáide as comhad darb ainm "
"``background.png``, a mbeidh an cosán iomlán aige ``polls/static/polls/"
"images/background.png``."

msgid ""
"Then, add a reference to your image in your stylesheet (``polls/static/polls/"
"style.css``):"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cuir tagairt do d’íomhá ar do stílbhileog (``polls/static/polls/"
"style.css``):"

msgid ""
"Reload ``http://localhost:8000/polls/`` and you should see the background "
"loaded in the top left of the screen."
msgstr ""
"Athlódáil `` http://localhost:8000/polls/`` agus ba cheart duit an cúlra a "
"fheiceáil luchtaithe ar bharr na láimhe clé den scáileán."

msgid ""
"The ``{% static %}`` template tag is not available for use in static files "
"which aren't generated by Django, like your stylesheet. You should always "
"use **relative paths** to link your static files between each other, because "
"then you can change :setting:`STATIC_URL` (used by the :ttag:`static` "
"template tag to generate its URLs) without having to modify a bunch of paths "
"in your static files as well."
msgstr ""
"Níl an chlib teimpléid ``{ % static %}`` ar fáil le húsáid i gcomhaid "
"statacha nach bhfuil ginte ag Django, cosúil le do stílbhileog. Ba cheart "
"duit **cosáin choibhneasta** a úsáid i gcónaí chun do chomhaid statacha a "
"nascadh lena chéile, mar ansin is féidir leat :socrú:`STATIC_URL` a athrú "
"(úsáidte ag an gclib teimpléad :ttag:`static` chun a URLanna a ghiniúint) "
"gan gá a dhéanamh. modhnaigh a lán cosáin i do chomhaid statacha freisin."

msgid ""
"These are the **basics**. For more details on settings and other bits "
"included with the framework see :doc:`the static files howto </howto/static-"
"files/index>` and :doc:`the staticfiles reference </ref/contrib/"
"staticfiles>`. :doc:`Deploying static files </howto/static-files/"
"deployment>` discusses how to use static files on a real server."
msgstr ""
"Seo iad na **bunghnéithe**. Le haghaidh tuilleadh sonraí ar shocruithe agus "
"míreanna eile atá san áireamh leis an gcreat féach :doc: `na comhaid "
"statacha howto </howto/static-files/index>` agus :doc: `tagairt na gcomhad "
"statacha </ref/contrib/staticfiles>`. :doc:`Comhaid statacha a imscaradh </"
"howto/static-files/deployment>` pléitear conas comhaid statacha a úsáid ar "
"fhíorfhreastalaí."

msgid ""
"When you're comfortable with the static files, read :doc:`part 7 of this "
"tutorial </intro/tutorial07>` to learn how to customize Django's "
"automatically-generated admin site."
msgstr ""
"Nuair atá tú ar do chompord leis na comhaid statacha, léigh :doc:`cuid 7 den "
"rang teagaisc seo </intro/tutorial07>` chun foghlaim conas suíomh riaracháin "
"Django a ghintear go huathoibríoch a shaincheapadh."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 7"
msgstr "Ag scríobh do chéad aip Django, cuid 7"

msgid ""
"This tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 6 </intro/tutorial06>` left off. "
"We're continuing the web-poll application and will focus on customizing "
"Django's automatically-generated admin site that we first explored "
"in :doc:`Tutorial 2 </intro/tutorial02>`."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an rang teagaisc seo nuair a d'fhág :doc:`Tutorial 6 </intro/"
"tutorial06>` as. Táimid ag leanúint leis an bhfeidhmchlár vótaíochta "
"gréasáin agus díreoimid ar shuíomh riaracháin Django a ghintear go "
"huathoibríoch a shaincheapadh a rinneamar iniúchadh ar dtús i :doc:`Teagasc "
"2 </intro/tutorial02>`."

msgid "Customize the admin form"
msgstr "Saincheap an fhoirm riaracháin"

msgid ""
"By registering the ``Question`` model with "
"``admin.site.register(Question)``, Django was able to construct a default "
"form representation. Often, you'll want to customize how the admin form "
"looks and works. You'll do this by telling Django the options you want when "
"you register the object."
msgstr ""
"Trí mhúnla ``Ceist`` a chlárú le ``admin.site.register(Question)``, bhí "
"Django in ann léiriú réamhshocraithe foirme a chruthú. Go minic, beidh tú ag "
"iarraidh conas a bhreathnaíonn agus a oibríonn an fhoirm riaracháin a "
"shaincheapadh. Déanfaidh tú é seo trí na roghanna atá uait a insint do "
"Django nuair a chláraíonn tú an réad."

msgid ""
"Let's see how this works by reordering the fields on the edit form. Replace "
"the ``admin.site.register(Question)`` line with:"
msgstr ""
"Feicfimid conas a oibríonn sé seo trí na réimsí ar an bhfoirm "
"eagarthóireachta a athordú. Ionadaigh an líne ``admin.site.register(Ceist)`` "
"le:"

msgid ""
"You'll follow this pattern -- create a model admin class, then pass it as "
"the second argument to ``admin.site.register()`` -- any time you need to "
"change the admin options for a model."
msgstr ""
"Leanfaidh tú an patrún seo -- cruthaigh rang admin samhail, ansin cuir ar "
"aghaidh é mar an dara argóint chuig ``admin.site.register()`` -- am ar bith "
"is gá duit na roghanna riaracháin do shamhail a athrú."

msgid ""
"This particular change above makes the \"Publication date\" come before the "
"\"Question\" field:"
msgstr ""
"Fágann an t-athrú áirithe seo thuas go dtagann an \"Publication date\" roimh "
"an réimse \"Question\":"

msgid "Fields have been reordered"
msgstr "Réimsí a athordú"

msgid ""
"This isn't impressive with only two fields, but for admin forms with dozens "
"of fields, choosing an intuitive order is an important usability detail."
msgstr ""
"Níl sé seo go hiontach le dhá réimse, ach i gcás foirmeacha riaracháin ina "
"bhfuil mórán réimsí, is sonraí inúsáidteachta tábhachtach é ordú iomasach a "
"roghnú."

msgid ""
"And speaking of forms with dozens of fields, you might want to split the "
"form up into fieldsets:"
msgstr ""
"Agus foirmeacha ag baint le mórán réimsí, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat an "
"fhoirm a roinnt ina réimsí páirce:"

msgid ""
"The first element of each tuple "
"in :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.fieldsets` is the title of the "
"fieldset. Here's what our form looks like now:"
msgstr ""
"Is é an chéad eilimint de gach tuple "
"in :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.fieldsets` teideal an réimse "
"réimse. Seo an chuma atá ar ár bhfoirm anois:"

msgid "Form has fieldsets now"
msgstr "Tá réimsí réimsí anois ag an bhfoirm"

msgid "Adding related objects"
msgstr "Rudaí gaolmhara a chur leis"

msgid ""
"OK, we have our Question admin page, but a ``Question`` has multiple "
"``Choice``\\s, and the admin page doesn't display choices."
msgstr ""
"Ceart go leor, tá ár leathanach riaracháin ``Question``, againn, ach tá "
"roghanna iolracha ag ``Choice``\\s, agus ní thaispeánann an leathanach "
"riaracháin roghanna."

msgid "Yet."
msgstr "Fós féin."

msgid ""
"There are two ways to solve this problem. The first is to register "
"``Choice`` with the admin just as we did with ``Question``:"
msgstr ""
"Tá dhá bhealach ann chun an fhadhb seo a réiteach. Is é an chéad cheann ná "
"``Choice`` a chlárú leis an riarthóir díreach mar a rinneamar le "
"``Question``:"

msgid ""
"Now \"Choices\" is an available option in the Django admin. The \"Add "
"choice\" form looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Anois tá \"Choices\" ina rogha atá ar fáil sa riarthóir Django. Breathnaíonn "
"an fhoirm \"\"Add choice\" mar seo:"

msgid "Choice admin page"
msgstr "Rogha leathanach riaracháin"

msgid ""
"In that form, the \"Question\" field is a select box containing every "
"question in the database. Django knows that "
"a :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` should be represented in the admin "
"as a ``<select>`` box. In our case, only one question exists at this point."
msgstr ""
"San fhoirm sin, is bosca roghnaithe é an réimse \"Ceist\" ina bhfuil gach "
"ceist sa bhunachar sonraí. Tá a fhios ag Django gur "
"cheart :class:`~django.db.models.ForeignKey` a léiriú sa admin mar bhosca `` "
"<roghnaigh>``. Inár gcás, níl ach ceist amháin ann ag an bpointe seo."

msgid ""
"Also note the \"Add another question\" link next to \"Question.\" Every "
"object with a ``ForeignKey`` relationship to another gets this for free. "
"When you click \"Add another question\", you'll get a popup window with the "
"\"Add question\" form. If you add a question in that window and click "
"\"Save\", Django will save the question to the database and dynamically add "
"it as the selected choice on the \"Add choice\" form you're looking at."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin an nasc \"Cuir ceist eile\" in aice le \"Ceist.\" "
"Faigheann gach réad a bhfuil gaol ``ForeignKey`` aige le duine eile é seo "
"saor in aisce. Nuair a chliceálann tú \"Cuir ceist eile leis\", gheobhaidh "
"tú fuinneog aníos leis an bhfoirm \"Cuir ceist leis\". Má chuireann tú ceist "
"sa bhfuinneog sin agus cliceáil \"Sábháil\", sábhálfaidh Django an cheist sa "
"bhunachar sonraí agus cuirfidh sé go dinimiciúil é mar an rogha roghnaithe "
"ar an bhfoirm \"Cuir rogha leis\" a bhfuil tú ag féachaint air."

msgid ""
"But, really, this is an inefficient way of adding ``Choice`` objects to the "
"system. It'd be better if you could add a bunch of Choices directly when you "
"create the ``Question`` object. Let's make that happen."
msgstr ""
"Ach, i ndáiríre, is bealach neamhéifeachtúil é seo chun réada ``Choice`` a "
"chur leis an gcóras. Bheadh ​​sé níos fearr dá bhféadfá braon Roghanna a chur "
"leis go díreach nuair a chruthaíonn tú an réad ``Ceist``. Déanaimis é sin a "
"tharlóidh."

msgid ""
"Remove the ``register()`` call for the ``Choice`` model. Then, edit the "
"``Question`` registration code to read:"
msgstr ""
"Bain an glao ``clár()`` don tsamhail ``Choice``. Ansin, cuir in eagar an cód "
"clárúcháin ``Ceist`` le léamh:"

msgid ""
"This tells Django: \"``Choice`` objects are edited on the ``Question`` admin "
"page. By default, provide enough fields for 3 choices.\""
msgstr ""
"Insíonn sé seo do Django: \"Cuirtear rudaí ``Choice`` in eagar ar an "
"leathanach riaracháin ``Ceist``. De réir réamhshocraithe, cuir go leor "
"réimsí ar fáil le haghaidh 3 rogha.\""

msgid "Load the \"Add question\" page to see how that looks:"
msgstr ""
"Luchtaigh an leathanach \"Cuir ceist leis\" chun a fheiceáil conas mar atá "
"sé sin:"

msgid "Add question page now has choices on it"
msgstr "Tá roghanna ar an leathanach seo anois"

msgid ""
"It works like this: There are three slots for related Choices -- as "
"specified by ``extra`` -- and each time you come back to the \"Change\" page "
"for an already-created object, you get another three extra slots."
msgstr ""
"Oibríonn sé mar seo: Tá trí shliotán le haghaidh Roghanna gaolmhara -- mar "
"atá sonraithe ag `` breise `` -- agus gach uair a thagann tú ar ais go dtí "
"an leathanach \"Athraigh\" le haghaidh réad a cruthaíodh cheana féin, "
"gheobhaidh tú trí shliotán breise eile."

msgid ""
"At the end of the three current slots you will find an \"Add another "
"Choice\" link.  If you click on it, a new slot will be added. If you want to "
"remove the added slot, you can click on the X to the top right of the added "
"slot. This image shows an added slot:"
msgstr ""
"Ag deireadh na dtrí shliotán reatha gheobhaidh tú nasc \"Cuir Rogha eile "
"leis\". Má chliceálann tú air, cuirfear sliotán nua leis. Más mian leat an "
"sliotán breise a bhaint, is féidir leat cliceáil ar an X ar bharr na sliotán "
"breise. Taispeánann an íomhá seo sliotán breise:"

msgid "Additional slot added dynamically"
msgstr "Sliotán breise curtha leis go dinimiciúil"

msgid ""
"One small problem, though. It takes a lot of screen space to display all the "
"fields for entering related ``Choice`` objects. For that reason, Django "
"offers a tabular way of displaying inline related objects. To use it, change "
"the ``ChoiceInline`` declaration to read:"
msgstr ""
"Fadhb bheag amháin, áfach. Tógann sé go leor spáis scáileáin chun na réimsí "
"go léir a thaispeáint chun rudaí gaolmhara ``Choice`` a iontráil. Ar an "
"ábhar sin, cuireann Django bealach táblach chun rudaí inlíne gaolmhara a "
"thaispeáint. Chun é a úsáid, athraigh an dearbhú ``ChoiceInline`` chun a "
"léamh:"

msgid ""
"With that ``TabularInline`` (instead of ``StackedInline``), the related "
"objects are displayed in a more compact, table-based format:"
msgstr ""
"Leis an ``TabularInline`` sin (in ionad `` StackedInline``), taispeántar na "
"cuspóirí gaolmhara i bhformáid tábla-bhunaithe níos dlúithe:"

msgid "Add question page now has more compact choices"
msgstr "Tá roghanna níos dlúithe le fáil anois ar leathanach na gceisteanna"

msgid ""
"Note that there is an extra \"Delete?\" column that allows removing rows "
"added using the \"Add another Choice\" button and rows that have already "
"been saved."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara go bhfuil breise \"Scrios?\" colún a cheadaíonn "
"sraitheanna a cuireadh leis a bhaint ag baint úsáide as an gcnaipe \"Cuir "
"Rogha eile leis\" agus sraitheanna atá sábháilte cheana féin."

msgid "Customize the admin change list"
msgstr "Saincheap an liosta athraithe admin"

msgid ""
"Now that the Question admin page is looking good, let's make some tweaks to "
"the \"change list\" page -- the one that displays all the questions in the "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Anois go bhfuil cuma mhaith ar leathanach riaracháin na gCeisteanna, "
"déanaimis roinnt tweaks ar an leathanach \"liosta athraithe\" - an ceann a "
"thaispeánann na ceisteanna go léir sa chóras."

msgid "Here's what it looks like at this point:"
msgstr "Seo an chuma atá air ag an bpointe seo:"

msgid ""
"By default, Django displays the ``str()`` of each object. But sometimes it'd "
"be more helpful if we could display individual fields. To do that, use "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display` admin option, "
"which is a list of field names to display, as columns, on the change list "
"page for the object:"
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, taispeánann Django an `` str ()`` de gach réad. Ach "
"uaireanta bheadh ​​sé níos cabhrach dá bhféadfaimis réimsí aonair a "
"thaispeáint. Chun é sin a dhéanamh, bain úsáid as an rogha "
"admin :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display`, arb é liosta "
"ainmneacha páirce é le taispeáint, mar cholúin, ar an leathanach liosta "
"athruithe don réad:"

msgid ""
"For good measure, let's also include the ``was_published_recently()`` method "
"from :doc:`Tutorial 2 </intro/tutorial02>`:"
msgstr ""
"Ar mhaithe le beart maith, cuirimis san áireamh freisin an modh "
"``foilsíodh_le déanaí()`` ó :doc:`Teagasc 2 </intro/tutorial02>`:"

msgid "Now the question change list page looks like this:"
msgstr "Anois tá cuma mar seo ar an leathanach liosta athraithe ceisteanna:"

msgid "Polls change list page, updated"
msgstr "Leathanach liosta athruithe pobalbhreithe, nuashonraithe"

msgid ""
"You can click on the column headers to sort by those values -- except in the "
"case of the ``was_published_recently`` header, because sorting by the output "
"of an arbitrary method is not supported. Also note that the column header "
"for ``was_published_recently`` is, by default, the name of the method (with "
"underscores replaced with spaces), and that each line contains the string "
"representation of the output."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cliceáil ar na ceanntásca colúin chun iad a shórtáil de réir "
"na luachanna sin -- ach amháin i gcás an chinnteidil ``foilsíodh_le "
"déanaí_``, mar ní thacaítear le sórtáil de réir aschur modha treallach. "
"Tabhair faoi deara freisin gurb é ceanntásc an cholúin le haghaidh "
"``foilsíodh_le déanaí``, de réir réamhshocraithe, ainm an mhodha (agus "
"spásanna curtha in ionad na bhfostóirí), agus go bhfuil léiriú teaghrán an "
"aschuir i ngach líne."

msgid ""
"You can improve that by using the :func:`~django.contrib.admin.display` "
"decorator on that method (extending the :file:`polls/models.py` file that "
"was created in :doc:`Tutorial 2 </intro/tutorial02>`), as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat é sin a fheabhsú trí úsáid a bhaint as an "
"maisitheoir :func:`~django.contrib.admin.display` ar an modh sin (ag síneadh "
"leis an gcomhad :comhad:`polls/models.py` a cruthaíodh i :doc:`Teagasc 2</ "
"réamhrá/teagasc02>`), mar a leanas:"

msgid ""
"For more information on the properties configurable via the decorator, "
"see :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display`."
msgstr ""
"Le haghaidh tuilleadh eolais ar na hairíonna is féidir a chumrú tríd an "
"maisitheoir, féach :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display`."

msgid ""
"Edit your :file:`polls/admin.py` file again and add an improvement to the "
"``Question`` change list page: filters using "
"the :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter`. Add the following "
"line to ``QuestionAdmin``::"
msgstr ""
"Cuir do chomhad ::`polls/admin.py` in eagar arís agus cuir feabhas ar an "
"leathanach liosta athruithe ``Ceist``: scagairí ag baint úsáide as "
"an :attr:`~django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter`. Cuir an líne seo a "
"leanas le ``QuestionAdmin``::"

msgid ""
"That adds a \"Filter\" sidebar that lets people filter the change list by "
"the ``pub_date`` field:"
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé sin barra taoibh \"Filter\" leis a ligeann do dhaoine an liosta "
"athruithe a scagadh de réir an réimse `` pub_date``:"

msgid ""
"The type of filter displayed depends on the type of field you're filtering "
"on. Because ``pub_date`` is a :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField`, "
"Django knows to give appropriate filter options: \"Any date\", \"Today\", "
"\"Past 7 days\", \"This month\", \"This year\"."
msgstr ""
"Braitheann an cineál scagaire a thaispeánfar ar an gcineál réimse a bhfuil "
"tú ag scagadh air. Toisc gur :class:`~django.db.models.DateTimeField` é `` "
"pub_date``, tá a fhios ag Django roghanna cuí scagaire a thabhairt: \"Dáta "
"ar bith\", \"Inniu\", \"7 lá anuas\", \"An mhí seo\", \"I mbliana\"."

msgid "This is shaping up well. Let's add some search capability::"
msgstr ""
"Tá sé seo ag múnlú suas go maith. Cuirimis roinnt cumas cuardaigh leis::"

msgid ""
"That adds a search box at the top of the change list. When somebody enters "
"search terms, Django will search the ``question_text`` field. You can use as "
"many fields as you'd like -- although because it uses a ``LIKE`` query "
"behind the scenes, limiting the number of search fields to a reasonable "
"number will make it easier for your database to do the search."
msgstr ""
"Cuireann sé sin bosca cuardaigh ag barr an liosta athruithe. Nuair a "
"chuireann duine téarmaí cuardaigh isteach, déanfaidh Django an réimse "
"``question_text`` a chuardach. Is féidir leat an oiread réimsí agus is mian "
"leat a úsáid -- ach toisc go n-úsáideann sé fiosrú `LIKE`` taobh thiar de na "
"pictiúir, má chuirtear teorainn le líon na réimsí cuardaigh go líon "
"réasúnta, beidh sé níos éasca do do bhunachar sonraí an cuardach a dhéanamh."

msgid ""
"Now's also a good time to note that change lists give you free pagination. "
"The default is to display 100 items per page. :attr:`Change list pagination "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_per_page>`, :attr:`search boxes "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.search_fields>`, :attr:`filters "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_filter>`, :attr:`date-hierarchies "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.date_hierarchy>`, and :attr:`column-header-"
"ordering <django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display>` all work together "
"like you think they should."
msgstr ""
"Is dea-am é anois freisin le tabhairt faoi deara go dtugann liostaí "
"athraithe leathanach saor in aisce duit. Is é an réamhshocrú ná 100 mír a "
"thaispeáint in aghaidh an leathanaigh. :attr:`Athraigh leathanach an liosta "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_per_page>`, :attr:`boscaí cuardaigh "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.search_fields>`, :attr:`scagairí "
"<django.contrib.admin .ModelAdmin.list_filter>`, :attr:`ordlathais dáta "
"<django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.date_hierarchy>`, agus :attr:`column-header-"
"ordering <django.contrib.admin.ModelAdmin.list_display>` ar fad oibriú le "
"chéile mar a cheapann tú ba chóir dóibh."

msgid "Customize the admin look and feel"
msgstr "Saincheap cuma agus mothú an riaracháin"

msgid ""
"Clearly, having \"Django administration\" at the top of each admin page is "
"ridiculous. It's just placeholder text."
msgstr ""
"Is léir gur rud ridiciúil é “riarachán Django” ag barr gach leathanach "
"riaracháin. Níl ann ach téacs áitsealbhóra."

msgid ""
"You can change it, though, using Django's template system. The Django admin "
"is powered by Django itself, and its interfaces use Django's own template "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat é a athrú, áfach, ag baint úsáide as córas teimpléad Django. "
"Tá an riarthóir Django faoi thiomáint ag Django féin, agus úsáideann a "
"chomhéadain córas teimpléid Django féin."

msgid "Customizing your *project's* templates"
msgstr "Saincheapadh do * tionscadail * teimpléid"

msgid ""
"Create a ``templates`` directory in your ``djangotutorial`` directory. "
"Templates can live anywhere on your filesystem that Django can access. "
"(Django runs as whatever user your server runs.) However, keeping your "
"templates within the project is a good convention to follow."
msgstr ""
"Cruthaigh eolaire ``templates`` i do eolaire ``djangotutorial``. Is féidir "
"le teimpléid maireachtáil áit ar bith ar do chóras comhad ar féidir le "
"Django rochtain a fháil air. (Ritheann Django mar cibé úsáideoir a ritheann "
"do fhreastalaí.) Mar sin féin, is dea-ghnás é do theimpléid a choinneáil "
"laistigh den tionscadal."

msgid ""
"Open your settings file (:file:`mysite/settings.py`, remember) and add "
"a :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` option in the :setting:`TEMPLATES` "
"setting:"
msgstr ""
"Oscail do chomhad socruithe (:comhad:`mysite/settings.py`, cuimhnigh) agus "
"cuir rogha :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` leis sa "
"socrú :setting:`TEMPLATES`:"

msgid ""
":setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` is a list of filesystem directories to "
"check when loading Django templates; it's a search path."
msgstr ""
":setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` is ea liosta eolairí córais comhaid le "
"seiceáil agus teimpléid Django á lódáil; is cosán cuardaigh é."

msgid "Organizing templates"
msgstr "Eagrú teimpléid"

msgid ""
"Just like the static files, we *could* have all our templates together, in "
"one big templates directory, and it would work perfectly well. However, "
"templates that belong to a particular application should be placed in that "
"application's template directory (e.g. ``polls/templates``) rather than the "
"project's (``templates``). We'll discuss in more detail in "
"the :doc:`reusable apps tutorial </intro/reusable-apps>` *why* we do this."
msgstr ""
"Díreach cosúil leis na comhaid statacha, * d'fhéadfadh * ár teimpléid go "
"léir a bheith againn le chéile, in aon eolaire teimpléid mór, agus "
"d'oibreodh sé go foirfe. Mar sin féin, ba cheart teimpléid a bhaineann le "
"feidhmchlár ar leith a chur in eolaire teimpléid an fheidhmchláir sin (m.sh. "
"``vótaíocht/teimpléid``) seachas in eolaire an tionscadail (``templates``). "
"Déanfaimid plé níos mine sa :doc:`teagasc maidir le haipeanna ath-inúsáidte "
"</intro/reusable-apps>` *cén fáth* a ndéanaimid é seo."

msgid ""
"Now create a directory called ``admin`` inside ``templates``, and copy the "
"template ``admin/base_site.html`` from within the default Django admin "
"template directory in the source code of Django itself (:source:`django/"
"contrib/admin/templates`) into that directory."
msgstr ""
"Anois cruthaigh eolaire darb ainm `` admin`` taobh istigh de `` teimpléid``, "
"agus cóipeáil an teimpléad `` admin/base_site.html`` ón eolaire "
"réamhshocraithe teimpléid admin Django i gcód foinse Django féin (: foinse:` "
"django/contrib/admin/templates`) isteach san eolaire sin."

msgid "Where are the Django source files?"
msgstr "Cá bhfuil na comhaid foinse Django?"

msgid ""
"If you have difficulty finding where the Django source files are located on "
"your system, run the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá deacracht agat a fháil amach cá bhfuil na comhaid foinse Django suite "
"ar do chóras, rith an t-ordú seo a leanas:"

msgid ""
"Then, edit the file and replace ``{{ site_header|default:_('Django "
"administration') }}`` (including the curly braces) with your own site's name "
"as you see fit. You should end up with a section of code like:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, cuir an comhad in eagar agus cuir ainm do shuímh féin in áit "
"``{{ site_header|réamhshocraithe:_('Riarachán Django') }}`` (lena n-áirítear "
"na braces curly) mar is cuí leat. Ba chóir go mbeadh roinn de chód mar:"

msgid ""
"We use this approach to teach you how to override templates. In an actual "
"project, you would probably use "
"the :attr:`django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_header` attribute to more "
"easily make this particular customization."
msgstr ""
"Bainimid úsáid as an gcur chuige seo chun tú a mhúineadh conas teimpléid a "
"shárú. I dtionscadal iarbhír, is dócha go n-úsáidfeá an "
"tréith :attr:`django.contrib.admin.AdminSite.site_header` chun an "
"saincheapadh áirithe seo a dhéanamh níos éasca."

msgid ""
"This template file contains lots of text like ``{% block branding %}`` and "
"``{{ title }}``. The ``{%`` and ``{{`` tags are part of Django's template "
"language. When Django renders ``admin/base_site.html``, this template "
"language will be evaluated to produce the final HTML page, just like we saw "
"in :doc:`Tutorial 3 </intro/tutorial03>`."
msgstr ""
"Tá go leor téacs sa chomhad teimpléad seo ar nós ``{% brandáil bloc %}`` "
"agus ``{{ title }}``. Is cuid de theanga teimpléid Django iad na clibeanna "
"``{%`` agus ``{{``. Nuair a dhéanann Django ``admin/base_site.html``, "
"déanfar an teanga teimpléid seo a mheas chun an leathanach HTML deiridh a "
"tháirgeadh, díreach mar a chonaic muid i :doc:`Teagasc 3 </intro/"
"tutorial03>`."

msgid ""
"Note that any of Django's default admin templates can be overridden. To "
"override a template, do the same thing you did with ``base_site.html`` -- "
"copy it from the default directory into your custom directory, and make "
"changes."
msgstr ""
"Tabhair faoi deara gur féidir aon cheann de na teimpléid admin "
"réamhshocraithe Django a shárú. Chun teimpléad a shárú, déan an rud céanna a "
"rinne tú le ``base_site.html`` -- cóipeáil é ón eolaire réamhshocraithe "
"isteach i do eolaire saincheaptha, agus déan athruithe."

msgid "Customizing your *application's* templates"
msgstr "Saincheapadh d'iarratais * teimpléid"

msgid ""
"Astute readers will ask: But if :setting:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` was empty "
"by default, how was Django finding the default admin templates? The answer "
"is that, since :setting:`APP_DIRS <TEMPLATES-APP_DIRS>` is set to ``True``, "
"Django automatically looks for a ``templates/`` subdirectory within each "
"application package, for use as a fallback (don't forget that "
"``django.contrib.admin`` is an application)."
msgstr ""
"Fiafróidh léitheoirí géara: Ach má bhí: socrú:`DIRS <TEMPLATES-DIRS>` folamh "
"de réir réamhshocraithe, conas a d'aimsigh Django na teimpléid "
"réamhshocraithe admin? Is é an freagra ná, ós rud é go bhfuil : "
"socrú:`APP_DIRS <TEMPLATES-APP_DIRS>` socraithe go ``True``, lorgaíonn "
"Django go huathoibríoch fochomhadlann ``templates/`` laistigh de gach "
"pacáiste feidhmchláir, lena úsáid mar chúltaca (don ' ná déan dearmad gur "
"feidhmchlár é ``django.contrib.admin``)."

msgid ""
"Our poll application is not very complex and doesn't need custom admin "
"templates. But if it grew more sophisticated and required modification of "
"Django's standard admin templates for some of its functionality, it would be "
"more sensible to modify the *application's* templates, rather than those in "
"the *project*. That way, you could include the polls application in any new "
"project and be assured that it would find the custom templates it needed."
msgstr ""
"Níl ár bhfeidhmchlár vótaíochta an-chasta agus ní bhíonn teimpléid "
"shaincheaptha riaracháin ag teastáil uaidh. Ach dá bhfásfadh sé níos "
"sofaisticiúla agus go raibh gá le mionathrú a dhéanamh ar theimpléid "
"chaighdeánacha riaracháin Django le haghaidh cuid dá fheidhmiúlacht, bheadh ​​"
"sé níos ciallmhaire teimpléid *an fheidhmchláir* a mhodhnú, seachas iad siúd "
"sa *tionscadal*. Ar an mbealach sin, d'fhéadfá an t-iarratas vótaíochta a "
"áireamh in aon tionscadal nua agus a bheith cinnte go bhfaighidh sé na "
"teimpléid saincheaptha a bhí de dhíth air."

msgid ""
"See the :ref:`template loading documentation <template-loading>` for more "
"information about how Django finds its templates."
msgstr ""
"Féach an :ref:`doiciméadú luchtaithe teimpléad <template-loading>` le "
"haghaidh tuilleadh eolais faoin gcaoi a n-aimsíonn Django a theimpléid."

msgid "Customize the admin index page"
msgstr "Saincheap an leathanach innéacs admin"

msgid ""
"On a similar note, you might want to customize the look and feel of the "
"Django admin index page."
msgstr ""
"Ar nóta comhchosúil, b'fhéidir gur mhaith leat cuma agus mothú an "
"leathanaigh innéacs riaracháin Django a shaincheapadh."

msgid ""
"By default, it displays all the apps in :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` that have "
"been registered with the admin application, in alphabetical order. You may "
"want to make significant changes to the layout. After all, the index is "
"probably the most important page of the admin, and it should be easy to use."
msgstr ""
"De réir réamhshocraithe, taispeánann sé na haipeanna go léir i: "
"socrú:`INSTALLED_APPS` atá cláraithe leis an bhfeidhmchlár riaracháin, in "
"ord aibítre. B'fhéidir gur mhaith leat athruithe suntasacha a dhéanamh ar an "
"leagan amach. Tar éis an tsaoil, is dócha gurb é an t-innéacs an leathanach "
"is tábhachtaí den riarthóir, agus ba cheart go mbeadh sé éasca le húsáid."

msgid ""
"The template to customize is ``admin/index.html``. (Do the same as with "
"``admin/base_site.html`` in the previous section -- copy it from the default "
"directory to your custom template directory). Edit the file, and you'll see "
"it uses a template variable called ``app_list``. That variable contains "
"every installed Django app. Instead of using that, you can hard-code links "
"to object-specific admin pages in whatever way you think is best."
msgstr ""
"Is é ``admin/index.html`` an teimpléad atá le oiriúnú. (Déan mar an gcéanna "
"le `` admin/base_site.html`` sa rannán roimhe seo -- cóipeáil é ón eolaire "
"réamhshocraithe chuig do eolaire teimpléid saincheaptha). Cuir an comhad in "
"eagar, agus feicfidh tú go n-úsáideann sé athróg teimpléid ar a dtugtar `` "
"app_list``. Tá gach aip Django suiteáilte san athróg sin. In ionad é sin a "
"úsáid, is féidir leat naisc a chódú go crua chuig leathanaigh riaracháin a "
"bhaineann go sonrach leis an oibiacht ar bith cibé bealach is fearr leat."

msgid ""
"When you're comfortable with the admin, read :doc:`part 8 of this tutorial </"
"intro/tutorial08>` to learn how to use third-party packages."
msgstr ""
"Nuair atá tú ar do chompord leis an riarthóir, léigh :doc:`cuid 8 den rang "
"teagaisc seo </intro/tutorial08>` chun foghlaim conas pacáistí tríú páirtí a "
"úsáid."

msgid "Writing your first Django app, part 8"
msgstr "Do chéad aip Django a scríobh, cuid 8"

msgid ""
"This tutorial begins where :doc:`Tutorial 7 </intro/tutorial07>` left off. "
"We've built our web-poll application and will now look at third-party "
"packages. One of Django's strengths is the rich ecosystem of third-party "
"packages. They're community developed packages that can be used to quickly "
"improve the feature set of an application."
msgstr ""
"Tosaíonn an cúrsa teagaisc seo nuair a d'fhág :doc:`Tutorial 7 </intro/"
"tutorial07>` as. Tá ár bhfeidhmchlár vótaíochta tógtha againn agus "
"féachfaimid anois ar phacáistí tríú páirtí. Ar cheann de láidreachtaí Django "
"tá an t-éiceachóras saibhir de phacáistí tríú páirtí. Is pacáistí forbartha "
"pobail iad is féidir a úsáid chun gné-thacar feidhmchláir a fheabhsú go tapa."

msgid ""
"This tutorial will show how to add :pypi:`Django Debug Toolbar <django-debug-"
"toolbar>`, a commonly used third-party package. The Django Debug Toolbar has "
"ranked in the top three most used third-party packages in the Django "
"Developers Survey in recent years."
msgstr ""
"Léireoidh an rang teagaisc seo conas :pypi:`Barra Uirlisí Dífhabhtaithe "
"Django <django-debug-toolbar>` a chur leis, pacáiste tríú páirtí a úsáidtear "
"go coitianta. Tá an Django Debug Toolbar rangaithe ar na trí phacáiste tríú "
"páirtí is mó a úsáidtear i Suirbhé Forbróirí Django le blianta beaga anuas."

msgid "Installing Django Debug Toolbar"
msgstr "Suiteáil Django Debug Toolbar"

msgid ""
"Django Debug Toolbar is a useful tool for debugging Django web applications. "
"It's a third-party package that is maintained by the community organization "
"`Django Commons <https://github.com/django-commons>`_. The toolbar helps you "
"understand how your application functions and to identify problems. It does "
"so by providing panels that provide debug information about the current "
"request and response."
msgstr ""
"Is uirlis úsáideach é Django Debug Toolbar chun feidhmchláir ghréasáin "
"Django a dhífhabhtú. Is pacáiste tríú páirtí é atá á chothabháil ag an "
"eagraíocht pobail `Django Commons <https://github.com/django-commons>`_. "
"Cuidíonn an barra uirlisí leat tuiscint a fháil ar an gcaoi a bhfeidhmíonn "
"d’fheidhmchlár agus chun fadhbanna a aithint. Déanann sé amhlaidh trí "
"phainéil a sholáthar a sholáthraíonn faisnéis dífhabhtaithe faoin iarratas "
"agus faoin bhfreagra reatha."

msgid ""
"To install a third-party application like the toolbar, you need to install "
"the package by running the below command within an activated virtual "
"environment. This is similar to our earlier step to :ref:`install Django "
"<installing-official-release>`."
msgstr ""
"Chun feidhmchlár tríú páirtí cosúil leis an mbarra uirlisí a shuiteáil, ní "
"mór duit an pacáiste a shuiteáil tríd an ordú thíos a rith laistigh de "
"thimpeallacht fhíorúil gníomhachtaithe. Tá sé seo cosúil lenár gcéim níos "
"luaithe chun :ref:` Django a shuiteáil <installing-official-release>`."

msgid ""
"Third-party packages that integrate with Django need some post-installation "
"setup to integrate them with your project. Often you will need to add the "
"package's Django app to your :setting:`INSTALLED_APPS` setting. Some "
"packages need other changes, like additions to your URLconf (``urls.py``)."
msgstr ""
"Tá roinnt socruithe iar-shuiteála ag teastáil ó phacáistí tríú páirtí a "
"chomhtháthaíonn le Django chun iad a chomhtháthú le do thionscadal. Go minic "
"beidh ort aip Django an phacáiste a chur le do shocrú:`INSTALLED_APPS`. "
"Teastaíonn athruithe eile ó roinnt pacáistí, amhail breisiúcháin le do "
"URLconf (``urls.py``)."

msgid ""
"Django Debug Toolbar requires several setup steps. Follow them in `its "
"installation guide <https://django-debug-toolbar.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"
"installation.html>`_. The steps are not duplicated in this tutorial, because "
"as a third-party package, it may change separately to Django's schedule."
msgstr ""
"Éilíonn Django Debug Toolbar roinnt céimeanna socraithe. Lean iad ina "
"threoir suiteála <https://django-debug-toolbar.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"
"installation.html>`_. Ní dhéantar na céimeanna a mhacasamhlú sa rang "
"teagaisc seo, mar mar phacáiste tríú páirtí, féadfaidh sé athrú ar leithligh "
"ar sceideal Django."

msgid ""
"Once installed, you should be able to see the DjDT \"handle\" on the right "
"side of the browser window when you browse to ``http://localhost:8000/admin/"
"``. Click it to open the debug toolbar and use the tools in each panel. See "
"the `panels documentation page`__ for more information on what the panels "
"show."
msgstr ""
"Nuair a bheidh tú suiteáilte, ba cheart go mbeifeá in ann an \"láimhseáil\" "
"DjDT a fheiceáil ar thaobh na láimhe deise den fhuinneog brabhsálaí nuair a "
"bhrabhsálann tú chuig `` http://localhost:8000/admin/``. Cliceáil é chun an "
"barra uirlisí dífhabhtaithe a oscailt agus úsáid na huirlisí i ngach "
"painéal. Féach ar an `leathanach doiciméadaithe painéil`__ le haghaidh "
"tuilleadh eolais ar cad a thaispeánann na painéil."

msgid "Getting help from others"
msgstr "Cabhair a fháil ó dhaoine eile"

msgid ""
"At some point you will run into a problem, for example the toolbar may not "
"render. When this happens and you're unable to resolve the issue yourself, "
"there are options available to you."
msgstr ""
"Ag am éigin beidh fadhb agat, mar shampla ní féidir an barra uirlisí a "
"sholáthar. Nuair a tharlaíonn sé seo agus nach bhfuil tú in ann an cheist a "
"réiteach tú féin, tá roghanna ar fáil duit."

msgid ""
"If the problem is with a specific package, check if there's a "
"troubleshooting guide or FAQ in the package's documentation. For example the "
"Django Debug Toolbar has a `Tips section <https://django-debug-"
"toolbar.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tips.html>`_ that outlines troubleshooting "
"options."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Search for similar issues on the package's issue tracker. Django Debug "
"Toolbar’s is `on GitHub <https://github.com/django-commons/django-debug-"
"toolbar/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+sort%3Aupdated-desc>`_."
msgstr ""
"Cuardaigh saincheisteanna comhchosúla ar rianaitheoir eisiúna an phacáiste. "
"Tá Barra Uirlisí Dífhabhtaithe Django `ar GitHub <https://github.com/django-"
"commons/django-debug-toolbar/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+sort%3Aupdated-"
"desc>`_."

msgid "Consult the `Django Forum <https://forum.djangoproject.com/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Téigh i gcomhairle leis an bhFóram Django <https://forum.djangoproject.com/"
">`_."

msgid "Join the `Django Discord server <https://chat.djangoproject.com>`_."
msgstr ""

msgid "Installing other third-party packages"
msgstr "Suiteáil pacáistí tríú páirtí eile"

msgid ""
"There are many more third-party packages, which you can find using the "
"fantastic Django resource, `Django Packages <https://djangopackages.org/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Tá i bhfad níos mó pacáistí tríú páirtí ann, ar féidir leat a fháil ag baint "
"úsáide as acmhainn iontach Django, `Pacáistí Django <https://"
"djangopackages.org/>`_."

msgid ""
"It can be difficult to know what third-party packages you should use. This "
"depends on your needs and goals. Sometimes it's fine to use a package that's "
"in its alpha state. Other times, you need to know it's production ready. "
"`Adam Johnson has a blog post <https://adamj.eu/tech/2021/11/04/the-well-"
"maintained-test/>`_ that outlines a set of characteristics that qualifies a "
"package as \"well maintained\". Django Packages shows data for some of these "
"characteristics, such as when the package was last updated."
msgstr ""
"Féadfaidh sé a bheith deacair fios a bheith agat cad iad na pacáistí tríú "
"páirtí ar cheart duit a úsáid. Braitheann sé seo ar do chuid riachtanas agus "
"spriocanna. Uaireanta tá sé ceart go leor pacáiste a úsáid atá ina staid "
"alfa. Amanna eile, ní mór duit fios a bheith agat go bhfuil sé réidh le "
"táirgeadh. `Tá blagphost ag Adam Johnson <https://adamj.eu/tech/2021/11/04/"
"the-well-maintained-test/>`_ a leagann amach sraith saintréithe a cháilíonn "
"pacáiste mar phacáiste \"cothabháilte go maith\" . Taispeánann Pacáistí "
"Django sonraí maidir le cuid de na tréithe seo, mar shampla nuair a "
"nuashonraíodh an pacáiste an uair dheireanach."

msgid ""
"As Adam points out in his post, when the answer to one of the questions is "
"\"no\", that's an opportunity to contribute."
msgstr ""
"Mar a luann Adam ina phost, nuair is é \"ní hea\" an freagra ar cheann de na "
"ceisteanna, sin deis cur leis."

msgid ""
"The beginner tutorial ends here. In the meantime, you might want to check "
"out some pointers on :doc:`where to go from here </intro/whatsnext>`."
msgstr ""
"Críochnaíonn an teagaisc do thosaitheoirí anseo. Idir an dá linn, b'fhéidir "
"gur mhaith leat roinnt leideanna a sheiceáil ar :doc:`cá le dul as seo </"
"intro/whatsnext>`."

msgid ""
"If you are familiar with Python packaging and interested in learning how to "
"turn polls into a \"reusable app\", check out :doc:`Advanced tutorial: How "
"to write reusable apps</intro/reusable-apps>`."
msgstr ""
"Má tá cur amach agat ar phacáistiú Python agus má tá suim agat a fhoghlaim "
"conas pobalbhreith a thiontú ina “aip ath-inúsáidte”, seiceáil "
"amach :doc:`Ceacht teagaisc: Conas aipeanna ath-inúsáidte a scríobh</intro/"
"reusable-apps>`."

msgid "What to read next"
msgstr "Cad atá le léamh ina dhiaidh sin"

msgid ""
"So you've read all the :doc:`introductory material </intro/index>` and have "
"decided you'd like to keep using Django. We've only just scratched the "
"surface with this intro (in fact, if you've read every single word, you've "
"read about 5% of the overall documentation)."
msgstr ""
"Mar sin tá an :doc:`ábhar tosaigh</intro/index>` léite agat agus tá cinneadh "
"déanta agat gur mhaith leat leanúint ar aghaidh ag úsáid Django. Níl ach an "
"dromchla díreach scríobtha againn leis an réamhrá seo (go deimhin, má tá "
"gach focal amháin léite agat, tá thart ar 5% den cháipéisíocht iomlán léite "
"agat)."

msgid "So what's next?"
msgstr "Mar sin, cad atá le teacht?"

msgid ""
"Well, we've always been big fans of learning by doing. At this point you "
"should know enough to start a project of your own and start fooling around. "
"As you need to learn new tricks, come back to the documentation. There's "
"also a bigger `Django ecosystem`_ out there for you to explore that the "
"community has created."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We've put a lot of effort into making Django's documentation useful, clear "
"and as complete as possible. The rest of this document explains more about "
"how the documentation works so that you can get the most out of it."
msgstr ""
"Tá an-iarracht déanta againn doiciméadú Django a dhéanamh úsáideach, soiléir "
"agus chomh iomlán agus is féidir. Míníonn an chuid eile den doiciméad seo "
"níos mó faoi conas a oibríonn an doiciméadú ionas gur féidir leat an leas is "
"mó a bhaint as."

msgid ""
"(Yes, this is documentation about documentation. Rest assured we have no "
"plans to write a document about how to read the document about "
"documentation.)"
msgstr ""
"(Is ea, is doiciméadú é seo faoi dhoiciméid. Bígí cinnte nach bhfuil aon "
"phlean againn doiciméad a scríobh faoi conas an doiciméad a léamh faoi "
"dhoiciméid.)"

msgid "Finding documentation"
msgstr "Doiciméadú a aimsiú"

msgid ""
"Django's got a *lot* of documentation -- almost 450,000 words and counting "
"-- so finding what you need can sometimes be tricky. A good place to start "
"is the :ref:`genindex`. We also recommend using the builtin search feature."
msgstr ""
"Tá *go leor* doiciméadaithe faighte ag Django -- beagnach 450,000 focal agus "
"comhaireamh -- mar sin is deacair uaireanta a bheith ag lorg cad atá uait. "
"Áit mhaith le tosú is ea an :tag:`genindex`. Molaimid freisin an ghné "
"cuardaigh insuite a úsáid."

msgid "Or you can just browse around!"
msgstr "Nó is féidir leat brabhsáil timpeall!"

msgid "How the documentation is organized"
msgstr "Conas a eagraítear na doiciméid"

msgid ""
"Django's main documentation is broken up into \"chunks\" designed to fill "
"different needs:"
msgstr ""
"Déantar príomhdhoiciméadú Django a bhriseadh suas ina \"sciopaí\" atá "
"deartha chun riachtanais éagsúla a líonadh:"

msgid ""
"The :doc:`introductory material </intro/index>` is designed for people new "
"to Django -- or to web development in general. It doesn't cover anything in "
"depth, but instead gives a high-level overview of how developing in Django "
"\"feels\"."
msgstr ""
"Tá an :doc:`ábhar tosaigh </intro/index>` deartha do dhaoine nach bhfuil nua "
"do Django -- nó d'fhorbairt gréasáin go ginearálta. Ní chlúdaíonn sé aon rud "
"domhain, ach ina ionad sin tugann sé forbhreathnú ardleibhéil ar conas a "
"mhothaíonn forbairt i Django."

msgid ""
"The :doc:`topic guides </topics/index>`, on the other hand, dive deep into "
"individual parts of Django. There are complete guides to "
"Django's :doc:`model system </topics/db/index>`, :doc:`template engine </"
"topics/templates>`, :doc:`forms framework </topics/forms/index>`, and much "
"more."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir freagraí ar cheisteanna fíor-choitianta a fháil freisin "
"sa :doc:`FAQ </faq/index>`."

msgid ""
"This is probably where you'll want to spend most of your time; if you work "
"your way through these guides you should come out knowing pretty much "
"everything there is to know about Django."
msgstr ""
"Is dócha gurb é seo an áit a mbeidh tú ag iarraidh an chuid is mó de do "
"chuid ama a chaitheamh; má oibríonn tú do bhealach a dhéanamh tríd na "
"treoracha seo ba chóir duit teacht amach agus fios agat beagnach gach rud "
"atá ar eolas faoi Django."

msgid ""
"Web development is often broad, not deep -- problems span many domains. "
"We've written a set of :doc:`how-to guides </howto/index>` that answer "
"common \"How do I ...?\" questions. Here you'll find information "
"about :doc:`generating PDFs with Django </howto/outputting-"
"pdf>`, :doc:`writing custom template tags </howto/custom-template-tags>`, "
"and more."
msgstr ""
"Is minic a bhíonn forbairt gréasáin leathan, ní domhain – baineann fadhbanna "
"le go leor réimsí. Táimid tar éis sraith de :doc:`treoraithe conas a "
"dhéanamh </howto/index>` a fhreagraíonn coitianta \"Conas a ...?\" "
"ceisteanna. Gheobhaidh tú faisnéis anseo faoi :doc: `PDF a ghiniúint le "
"Django </howto/outputting-pdf>`, :doc:` ag scríobh clibeanna saincheaptha "
"teimpléid </howto/custom-template-tags>`, agus tuilleadh."

msgid ""
"Answers to really common questions can also be found in the :doc:`FAQ </faq/"
"index>`."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir freagraí ar cheisteanna fíor-choitianta a fháil freisin "
"sa :doc:`FAQ </faq/index>`."

msgid ""
"The guides and how-to's don't cover every single class, function, and method "
"available in Django -- that would be overwhelming when you're trying to "
"learn. Instead, details about individual classes, functions, methods, and "
"modules are kept in the :doc:`reference </ref/index>`. This is where you'll "
"turn to find the details of a particular function or whatever you need."
msgstr ""
"Ní chlúdaíonn na treoracha agus na bealaí le gach rang, feidhm agus modh atá "
"ar fáil in Django -- a bheadh ​​thar a bheith tábhachtach agus tú ag iarraidh "
"foghlaim. Ina áit sin, coimeádtar sonraí faoi ranganna aonair, feidhmeanna, "
"modhanna agus modúil sa :doc:`reference </ref/index>`. Seo an áit a rachaidh "
"tú chun sonraí feidhm áirithe nó cibé rud a theastaíonn uait a fháil."

msgid ""
"If you are interested in deploying a project for public use, our docs "
"have :doc:`several guides</howto/deployment/index>` for various deployment "
"setups as well as a :doc:`deployment checklist</howto/deployment/checklist>` "
"for some things you'll need to think about."
msgstr ""
"Má tá suim agat tionscadal a imscaradh le haghaidh úsáid phoiblí, tá :doc: "
"`roinnt threoracha </howto/ imscaradh/index>` ag ár ndoiciméid le haghaidh "
"socruithe éagsúla imlonnaithe chomh maith le :doc:`seicliosta imlonnaithe</"
"howto/imscaradh/ seicliosta>` le haghaidh roinnt rudaí a chaithfidh tú "
"smaoineamh orthu."

msgid ""
"Finally, there's some \"specialized\" documentation not usually relevant to "
"most developers. This includes the :doc:`release notes </releases/index>` "
"and :doc:`internals documentation </internals/index>` for those who want to "
"add code to Django itself, and a :doc:`few other things that don't fit "
"elsewhere </misc/index>`."
msgstr ""
"Ar deireadh, tá roinnt doiciméad \"speisialaithe\" ann nach mbaineann le "
"formhór na bhforbróirí de ghnáth. Áiríonn sé seo na :doc:`nótaí scaoilte </"
"releases/index>` agus :doc: `doiciméadúchán inmheánach </ intéirnigh/"
"innéacs>` dóibh siúd ar mian leo cód a chur le Django féin, "
"agus :doc:`beagán rudaí eile nach n-oireann in aon áit eile </misc/index>`."

msgid "How documentation is updated"
msgstr "Conas a nuashonraítear doiciméadú"

msgid ""
"Just as the Django code base is developed and improved on a daily basis, our "
"documentation is consistently improving. We improve documentation for "
"several reasons:"
msgstr ""
"Díreach mar a fhorbraítear agus a fheabhsaítear bonn cód Django ar bhonn "
"laethúil, tá feabhas leanúnach ar ár ndoiciméadú. Cuirimid feabhas ar an "
"doiciméadú ar roinnt cúiseanna:"

msgid "To make content fixes, such as grammar/typo corrections."
msgstr ""
"Chun réitigh inneachair a dhéanamh, mar cheartúcháin ghramadaí/clóscríobh."

msgid ""
"To add information and/or examples to existing sections that need to be "
"expanded."
msgstr ""
"Eolas agus/nó samplaí a chur le rannáin atá ann cheana ar gá iad a leathnú."

msgid ""
"To document Django features that aren't yet documented. (The list of such "
"features is shrinking but exists nonetheless.)"
msgstr ""
"Chun gnéithe Django nach bhfuil doiciméadaithe fós a dhoiciméadú. (Tá liosta "
"na ngnéithe sin ag dul i laghad ach tá sé ann mar sin féin.)"

msgid ""
"To add documentation for new features as new features get added, or as "
"Django APIs or behaviors change."
msgstr ""
"Chun doiciméadú a chur leis le haghaidh gnéithe nua de réir mar a chuirtear "
"gnéithe nua leis, nó de réir mar a athraíonn APInna Django nó iompraíochtaí."

msgid ""
"Django's documentation is kept in the same source control system as its "
"code. It lives in the :source:`docs` directory of our Git repository. Each "
"document online is a separate text file in the repository."
msgstr ""
"Coimeádtar doiciméadú Django sa chóras rialaithe foinse céanna lena chód. Tá "
"sé ina chónaí san eolaire :foinse:`docs` dár stór Git. Is téacschomhad ar "
"leith é gach doiciméad ar líne sa stór."

msgid "Where to get it"
msgstr "Cá háit le fáil"

msgid ""
"You can read Django documentation in several ways. They are, in order of "
"preference:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat doiciméadú Django a léamh ar bhealaí éagsúla. Tá siad, in ord "
"tosaíochta:"

msgid "On the web"
msgstr "Ar an ngréasán"

msgid ""
"The most recent version of the Django documentation lives at https://"
"docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/. These HTML pages are generated automatically "
"from the text files in source control. That means they reflect the \"latest "
"and greatest\" in Django -- they include the very latest corrections and "
"additions, and they discuss the latest Django features, which may only be "
"available to users of the Django development version. (See :ref:`differences-"
"between-doc-versions` below.)"
msgstr ""
"Tá an leagan is déanaí den doiciméadú Django ina chónaí ag https://"
"docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/. Gintear na leathanaigh HTML seo go "
"huathoibríoch ó na comhaid téacs atá i gceannas foinse. Ciallaíonn sé sin go "
"léiríonn siad an \"is déanaí agus is mó\" i Django - áirítear iontu na "
"ceartúcháin agus na breisithe is déanaí, agus pléann siad na gnéithe Django "
"is déanaí, a d'fhéadfadh a bheith ar fáil d'úsáideoirí leagan forbartha "
"Django amháin. (Féach :tag:`differences-interween-doc-versions` thíos.)"

msgid ""
"We encourage you to help improve the docs by submitting changes, corrections "
"and suggestions in the `ticket system`_. The Django developers actively "
"monitor the ticket system and use your feedback to improve the documentation "
"for everybody."
msgstr ""
"Molaimid duit cabhrú leis na doiciméid a fheabhsú trí athruithe, ceartúcháin "
"agus moltaí a chur isteach sa `córas ticéid`_. Déanann forbróirí Django "
"monatóireacht ghníomhach ar chóras na dticéad agus úsáideann siad d'aiseolas "
"chun an doiciméadú a fheabhsú do gach duine."

msgid ""
"Note, however, that tickets should explicitly relate to the documentation, "
"rather than asking broad tech-support questions. If you need help with your "
"particular Django setup, try the `Django Forum`_ or the `Django Discord "
"server`_ instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "In plain text"
msgstr "I ngnáth-théacs"

msgid ""
"For offline reading, or just for convenience, you can read the Django "
"documentation in plain text."
msgstr ""
"Chun léamh as líne, nó ar mhaithe le caoithiúlacht amháin, is féidir leat "
"doiciméadú Django a léamh i ngnáth-théacs."

msgid ""
"If you're using an official release of Django, the zipped package (tarball) "
"of the code includes a ``docs/`` directory, which contains all the "
"documentation for that release."
msgstr ""
"Má tá scaoileadh oifigiúil de Django á úsáid agat, tá eolaire ``docs/`` i "
"bpacáiste zipped (tarball) an chóid, ina bhfuil na doiciméid go léir don "
"eisiúint sin."

msgid ""
"If you're using the development version of Django (aka the main branch), the "
"``docs/`` directory contains all of the documentation. You can update your "
"Git checkout to get the latest changes."
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ag baint úsáide as an leagan forbartha de Django (aka an príomh-"
"bhrainse), tá na doiciméid go léir san eolaire ``docs/``. Is féidir leat do "
"sheic amach Git a nuashonrú chun na hathruithe is déanaí a fháil."

msgid ""
"One low-tech way of taking advantage of the text documentation is by using "
"the Unix ``grep`` utility to search for a phrase in all of the "
"documentation. For example, this will show you each mention of the phrase "
"\"max_length\" in any Django document:"
msgstr ""
"Bealach amháin ísealteicneolaíochta chun leas a bhaint as doiciméadú an "
"téacs ná úsáid a bhaint as áis Unix ``grep`` chun frása a chuardach sa "
"doiciméadú go léir. Mar shampla, taispeánfaidh sé seo gach tagairt duit den "
"abairt \"max_length\" in aon doiciméad Django:"

msgid "As HTML, locally"
msgstr "Mar HTML, go háitiúil"

msgid ""
"You can get a local copy of the HTML documentation following a few steps:"
msgstr ""
"Is féidir leat cóip áitiúil den doiciméadú HTML a fháil tar éis roinnt "
"céimeanna:"

msgid ""
"Django's documentation uses a system called Sphinx__ to convert from plain "
"text to HTML. You'll need to install Sphinx by either downloading and "
"installing the package from the Sphinx website, or with ``pip``:"
msgstr ""
"Úsáideann doiciméadú Django córas ar a dtugtar Sphinx__ chun aistriú ó "
"ghnáth-théacs go HTML. Beidh ort Sphinx a shuiteáil tríd an bpacáiste a "
"íoslódáil agus a shuiteáil ó shuíomh Gréasáin Sphinx, nó le `` pip``:"

msgid ""
"Then, use the included ``Makefile`` to turn the documentation into HTML:"
msgstr ""
"Ansin, bain úsáid as an ``Makefile`` san áireamh chun an doiciméadú a "
"thiontú go HTML:"

msgid "You'll need `GNU Make`__ installed for this."
msgstr "Beidh `GNU Make`__ suiteáilte uait le haghaidh seo."

msgid "If you're on Windows you can alternatively use the included batch file:"
msgstr ""
"Má tá tú ar Windows is féidir leat an baiscchomhad a úsáid mar rogha eile:"

msgid "The HTML documentation will be placed in ``docs/_build/html``."
msgstr "Cuirfear na doiciméid HTML i ``docs/_build/html``."

msgid "Differences between versions"
msgstr "Difríochtaí idir leaganacha"

msgid ""
"The text documentation in the main branch of the Git repository contains the "
"\"latest and greatest\" changes and additions. These changes include "
"documentation of new features targeted for Django's next :term:`feature "
"release <Feature release>`. For that reason, it's worth pointing out our "
"policy to highlight recent changes and additions to Django."
msgstr ""
"Tá na hathruithe agus na breisithe “is déanaí agus is mó” sa doiciméadú "
"téacs i bpríomhbhrainse stór Git. Áirítear leis na hathruithe seo doiciméadú "
"ar ghnéithe nua atá dírithe ar an gcéad :téarma eile de chuid "
"Django:`eisiúint gné <Eisiúint Gné>`. Ar an ábhar sin, is fiú ár mbeartas a "
"chur in iúl chun aird a tharraingt ar athruithe agus ar bhreisithe le déanaí "
"ar Django."

msgid "We follow this policy:"
msgstr "Leanaimid an polasaí seo:"

msgid ""
"The development documentation at https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ is "
"from the main branch. These docs correspond to the latest feature release, "
"plus whatever features have been added/changed in the framework since then."
msgstr ""
"Tagann an doiciméadú forbartha ag https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ ón "
"bpríomhbhrainse. Freagraíonn na doiciméid seo don eisiúint gné is déanaí, "
"chomh maith le cibé gnéithe a cuireadh leis / a athraíodh sa chreat ó shin i "
"leith."

msgid ""
"As we add features to Django's development version, we update the "
"documentation in the same Git commit transaction."
msgstr ""
"De réir mar a chuirimid gnéithe le leagan forbartha Django, déanaimid na "
"doiciméid a nuashonrú san idirbheart gealltanas Git céanna."

msgid ""
"To distinguish feature changes/additions in the docs, we use the phrase: "
"\"New in Django Development version\" for the version of Django that hasn't "
"been released yet, or \"New in version X.Y\" for released versions."
msgstr ""
"Chun idirdhealú a dhéanamh idir athruithe/breisithe gné sna doiciméid, "
"úsáidimid an frása: \"Leagan Nua i bhForbairt Django\" don leagan de Django "
"nár eisíodh fós, nó \"Nua i leagan X.Y\" do leaganacha eisithe."

msgid ""
"Documentation fixes and improvements may be backported to the last release "
"branch, at the discretion of the merger, however, once a version of Django "
"is :ref:`no longer supported<supported-versions-policy>`, that version of "
"the docs won't get any further updates."
msgstr ""
"Is féidir socruithe agus feabhsúcháin doiciméad a aisiompú go dtí an brainse "
"eisithe is déanaí, de rogha an chumaisc, áfach, a luaithe is a bhíonn leagan "
"de Django :ref:`gan tacaíocht a thuilleadh <supported-versions-policy>`, "
"bhuaigh an leagan sin de na doiciméid Ní bhfaighidh tú aon nuashonruithe "
"breise."

msgid ""
"The `main documentation web page`_ includes links to documentation for "
"previous versions. Be sure you are using the version of the docs "
"corresponding to the version of Django you are using!"
msgstr ""
"Cuimsíonn an `príomhleathanach gréasáin doiciméadaithe`_ naisc chuig "
"doiciméadú le haghaidh leaganacha roimhe seo. Bí cinnte go bhfuil tú ag "
"baint úsáide as an leagan de na doiciméid a fhreagraíonn don leagan de "
"Django atá in úsáid agat!"
